     32       --------------------
     33       HISTORY of this file
     34       --------------------
     35       Jun 2017: Version 7.0 replaces GTAP.tab version 6.2
     36       Nov 2017: Added variables and equations representing tax-inclusive and
     37                 tax-exclusive real prices for mobile and sluggish endowments
     38                 - pefactreal(e,r)  --> tax-exclusive real factor prices
     39                 - pebfactreal(e,r) --> tax-inclusive real factor prices
     40       Apr 2018: Refined set definition in Section C-A1 (Allocative efficiency
     41                 effect: Activity, comodity and endowment Summary)
     42       Jul 2018: Defined a new set ENDT to distinguish endowment types (mobile,
     43                 sluggish and fixed) and added an endowment binary flag parameter
     44                 (ENDOWFLAG) to define endowment sets at run time.
     45       Dec 2019: Modified Section C-A21 and added Section CA25 in the Welfare
     46                 decomposition module to distinguish between output and income tax
     47                 effects. Also fixed a typo error by renaming Section A3 to A24
     48                 - Section 11.5  --> added element "inctax" in the Set CTAX
     49                 - Section C-A21 --> now only reports output tax effect
     50           [NEW] - Section C-A25 --> reports factor income tax effect
     51    
     52    
     53       ----------------------------------
     54       Overview of the GTAP.TAB Structure
     55       ----------------------------------
     56       Preliminaries:
     57           A-0. FILES
     58           A-1. SET definitions
     59           A-2. READ Base Data
     60           A-3. Key derivatives of Base Data
     61           A-4. Common COEFFICIENTS
     62           A-5. Common VARIABLES
     63    
     64       Equation Modules:
     65           1.  Firms
     66           2.  Commodity supply
     67           3.  Income distribution
     68           4.  Allocation of income across expenditure categories
     69           5.  Domestic final demand
     70           6.  Trade, goods market equilibrium and prices
     71           7.  Factor market equilibrium
     72           8.  Allocation of global saving
     73           9.  Tax revenue streams
     74          10.  Numeraire and Walras law
     75               ................................................
     76               Summary Indices (for use in welfare measurement)
     77               ................................................
     78               B-0. Variables and coefficients for summary indices
     79               B-1. Factor price indices
     80               B-2. Regional terms of trade (ToT)
     81               B-3. GDP indices (value, price and quantity)
     82               B-4. Aggregate trade indices (value, price and quantity)
     83               B-5. Trade balance indices
     84               B-6. Terms of trade (ToT) decomposition
     85          11.  Welfare measurement and decomposition
     86    
     87       Welfare summary and post-sim calculations:
     88          C. Welfare decomposition summary
     89          D. Volume changes (GTAPVol)
     90          E. Data balance checks
     91   >!
     92    
     93   !<
     94       ----------
     95       A-0. FILES
     96       ----------
     97   >!
     98    
     99   File
    100       GTAPSETS # file with set specification #;
    101   File
    102       GTAPDATA # file containing all Base Data #;
    103   File
    104       GTAPPARM # file containing behavioral parameters #;
    105   File (new)
    106       GTAPSUM # file containing data summary and accounting checks #;
    107    
    108   !<
    109       --------------------
    110       A-1. SET definitions
    111       --------------------
    112    
    113       Sets define relevant groupings of entities over which we will be performing
    114       operations in the model. SUBSETS are defined in order to facilitate
    115       summation over only a portion of a given group, e.g., margin commodities.
    116    
    117       The GTAP Model requires separate SET specification for activities and
    118       commodities because of multi-production possibilities--i.e., a single
    119       activity could produce multiple commodities (e.g., an agriculture activity
    120       producing multiple agricultural commodities), or for a commodity to be
    121       produced by multiple activities (e.g., electricity being produced by
    122       different generation activities).
    123    
    124       Although the standard GTAP Data Base has a diagonal 'make' matrix, it is
    125       possible to aggregate it such that the resulting aggregated
    126       database would have a non-diagonal 'make' matrix structure.
    127    
    128       Aide-Memoire for Sets and indices
    129       ---------------------------------
    130    
    131       Activities
    132       |-----------|
    133       |  ACTS(a)  |
    134       |-----------|
    135    
    136       Commodities
    137       |-----------------------|
    138       |        COMM(c)        |
    139       |-----------------------|
    140       |  MARG(m)  |  NMRG(n)  |
    141       |-----------------------|
    142    
    143       Endowments
    144       |---------------------------------------------------|
    145       |                      ENDW(e)                      |
    146       |---------------------------------------------------|
    147       |  ENDWF(e)  |  ENDWC(e)  |  ENDWM(e)  |  ENDWS(e)  |
    148       |---------------------------------------------------|
    149                    |              ENDWMS(e)               |
    150                    |--------------------------------------|
    151    
    152    
    153       Commodities and endowments
    154       |-----------------------|
    155       |        DEMD(d)        |
    156       |-----------------------|
    157       |  COMM(c)  |  ENDW(e)  |
    158       |-----------------------|
    159    
    160   >!
    161    
    162   Coefficient
    163       VERNUM # version of GTAP Data Base #;
    164   Read
    165       VERNUM from file GTAPDATA header "DVER";
    166   Update (change)
    167       VERNUM = 0.0; ! force it to be copied to update file !
    168    
    169   Set
    170       REG # regions #
    171       read elements from file GTAPSETS header "REG";
    172   Set
    173       COMM # commodities #
    174       read elements from file GTAPSETS header "COMM";
    175   Set
    176       MARG # margin commodities #
    177       read elements from file GTAPSETS header "MARG";
    178   Subset
    179       MARG is subset of COMM;
    180   Set
    181       NMRG # non-margin commodities # = COMM - MARG;
    182   Set
    183       ACTS # Activities #
    184       read elements from file GTAPSETS header "ACTS";
    185   Set
    186       ENDW # endowments #
    187       read elements from file GTAPSETS header "ENDW";
    188   Set !< The single element ENDWC set is defined for the sake of convenience >!
    189       ENDWC # capital endowment # (capital);
    190   Subset
    191       ENDWC is subset of ENDW;
    192   Set
    193       ENDWT # endowment types # (mobile, sluggish, fixed);
    194   Coefficient (parameter)(all,e,ENDW)(all,t,ENDWT)
    195       ENDOWFLAG(e,t) # binary (1,0) flag for endowment mobility #;
    196   Read
    197       ENDOWFLAG from file GTAPPARM header "EFLG";
    198   Assertion # checking just 1 non-zero in each factor row #
    199       (all,e,ENDW) sum{t,ENDWT: ENDOWFLAG(e,t) ne 0, 1} = 1;
    200   Set
    201       ENDWM # mobile endowments # = (all,e,ENDW:ENDOWFLAG(e,"mobile") ne 0);
    202   Subset
    203       ENDWM is subset of ENDW;
Declaration of 'ENDWM' as a SUBSET of 'ENDW'.
%% Information only.
    This subset relation is a consequence of earlier subset declarations.
    204   Set
    205       ENDWS # sluggish endowment # = (all,e,ENDW:ENDOWFLAG(e,"sluggish") ne 0);
    206   Subset
    207       ENDWS is subset of ENDW;
Declaration of 'ENDWS' as a SUBSET of 'ENDW'.
%% Information only.
    This subset relation is a consequence of earlier subset declarations.
    208   Set
    209       ENDWMS # mobile and sluggish endowments # = ENDWM + ENDWS;
    210   Subset
    211       ENDWMS is subset of ENDW;
    212   Subset
    213       ENDWC is subset of ENDWMS;
    214   Set
    215       ENDWF # Sector-specific endowment # = ENDW - ENDWMS;
    216   Set
    217       DEMD # demanded commodities and endowments # = ENDW + COMM;
    218    
    219   !<
    220       -------------------
    221       A-2. READ Base Data
    222       -------------------
    223       We read in here almost all the base data, and define variables and
    224       coefficients associated with them. A few data arrays, namely: VKB,
    225       VTMFSD and DPARSUM are read in their respective modules.
    226    
    227       Data flows and prices are valued at: supplier(S)
    228                                            basic(B)
    229                                            producer(P)
    230                                            FOB exports
    231                                            CIF imports
    232    
    233       The READ statements are divided into six sections:
    234       Firms
    235       Commodity Supply
    236       Government Consumption
    237       Private Consumption
    238       Investment Consumption
    239       Saving
    240       Global Bank
    241       International Trade and Transport
    242    
    243       Since these are invariant for each solution of the model, they are termed
    244       coefficients. Coefficients are assigned upper case to distinguish them
    245       from variables (this is purely cosmetic, as GEMPACK is not case-sensitive).
    246       Variables in GEMPACK are assigned lower case labels to denote the fact that
    247       they are percentage changes. In some cases, original levels values for
    248       selected variables are defined to permit the user to compare post-simulation
    249       levels values across several simulations.
    250    
    251       The updating command indicates how the new level of the coefficient will
    252       be computed based on the previous solution of the linearized equations.
    253       Note that the notation used in the update commands is a shorthand for
    254       total differentials of these coefficient values.  Thus, w * v indicates
    255       that we want to take the total differential of W * V, plug in the
    256       calculated values of w and v, and add this to the base level in order to
    257       obtain a revised value for this product.
    258   >!
    259    
    260   !<
    261       Firms
    262       -----
    263   >!
    264    
    265   !<  Domestic intermediate purchases by firms at basic prices >!
    266   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    267       pds(c,r) # price of domestically supplied commodity c in region r #;
    268   Variable (orig_level=VDFB)(all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    269       qfd(c,a,r) # demand for domestic commodity c by activity a in region r #;
    270   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    271       VDFB(c,a,r) # expenditure on domestic c by act. a in r at basic prices #;
    272   Read
    273       VDFB from file GTAPDATA header "VDFB";
    274   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    275       VDFB(c,a,r) = pds(c,r) * qfd(c,a,r);
    276    
    277   !<  Imported intermediate purchases by firms at basic prices >!
    278   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    279       pms(c,r) # price of aggregate commodity import bundle c in region r #;
    280   Variable (orig_level=VMFB)(all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    281       qfm(c,a,r) # imported commodity c for use by activity a in region r #;
    282   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    283       VMFB(c,a,r) # expenditure on imported c by act. a in r at basic prices #;
    284   Read
    285       VMFB from file GTAPDATA header "VMFB";
    286   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    287       VMFB(c,a,r) = pms(c,r) * qfm(c,a,r);
    288    
    289   !<  Domestic intermediate purchases by firms at producer prices >!
    290   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    291       pfd(c,a,r) # price of domestic com. c purchased by act. a in region r #;
    292   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    293       VDFP(c,a,r) # expenditure on dom. c by act. a in r at producer prices #;
    294   Read
    295       VDFP from file GTAPDATA header "VDFP";
    296   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    297       VDFP(c,a,r) = pfd(c,a,r) * qfd(c,a,r);
    298    
    299   !<  Imported intermediate purchases by firms at producer prices >!
    300   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    301       pfm(c,a,r) # price of imported com. c purchased by act. a in region r #;
    302   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    303       VMFP(c,a,r) # expenditure on imp. c by act. a in r at producer prices #;
    304   Read
    305       VMFP from file GTAPDATA header "VMFP";
    306   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    307       VMFP(c,a,r) = pfm(c,a,r) * qfm(c,a,r);
    308    
    309   !<  Endowment at supplier's (after income tax) prices >!
    310   Variable (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    311       pes(e,a,r) # supply (after income tax) price of e for use by a in r #;
    312   Variable (orig_level=EVOS)(all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    313       qes(e,a,r) # supply of endowment e for use by activity a in region r #;
    314   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    315       EVOS(e,a,r) # value of e for use by a in r at supplier (after tax) prices #;
    316   Read
    317       EVOS from file GTAPDATA header "EVOS";
    318   Update (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    319       EVOS(e,a,r) = pes(e,a,r) * qes(e,a,r);
    320    
    321   !<  Endowments at basic (income tax inclusive) prices >!
    322   Variable (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    323       peb(e,a,r) # basic price of endowment e in act. a in region r #;
    324   Variable (orig_level=EVFB)(all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    325       qfe(e,a,r) # demand for endowment e by act. a in region r #;
    326   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    327       EVFB(e,a,r) # expenditure on endowment e by act. a in r at basic prices #;
    328   Read
    329       EVFB from file GTAPDATA header "EVFB";
    330   Update (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    331       EVFB(e,a,r) = peb(e,a,r) * qfe(e,a,r);
    332    
    333   !<  Endowments at producer prices >!
    334   Variable (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    335       pfe(e,a,r) # price of endowment e purchased by activity a region r #;
    336   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    337       EVFP(e,a,r) # expenditure on endowment e by a in r at producer prices #;
    338   Read
    339       EVFP from file GTAPDATA header "EVFP";
    340   Update (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    341       EVFP(e,a,r) = pfe(e,a,r) * qfe(e,a,r);
    342    
    343   !<
    344       Commodity supply
    345       ----------------
    346   >!
    347    
    348   !<  'make' matrix at supplier's (i.e., output tax exclusive) prices >!
    349   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    350       ps(c,a,r) # supply price of commodity c produced by activity a in r #;
    351   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    352       qca(c,a,r) # supply of commodity c by activity a in r #;
    353   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    354       MAKES(c,a,r) # 'make' matrix valued at supplier's prices #;
    355   Read
    356       MAKES from file GTAPDATA header "MAKS";
    357   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    358       MAKES(c,a,r) = ps(c,a,r) * qca(c,a,r);
    359    
    360   !<  'make' matrix at basic (i.e., output tax inclusive) prices >!
    361   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    362       pca(c,a,r) # basic price of commodity c produced by activity a in r #;
    363   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    364       MAKEB(c,a,r) # 'make' matrix valued at basic prices #;
    365   Read
    366       MAKEB from file GTAPDATA header "MAKB";
    367   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    368       MAKEB(c,a,r) = pca(c,a,r)*qca(c,a,r);
    369    
    370   !<
    371       Government consumption
    372       ----------------------
    373   >!
    374    
    375   !<  Domestic commodity purchases by government at basic prices >!
    376   Variable (orig_level=VDGB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    377       qgd(c,r) # government demand for domestic commodity c in region r #;
    378   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    379       VDGB(c,r) # government expenditure on domestic c in r at basic prices #;
    380   Read
    381       VDGB from file GTAPDATA header "VDGB";
    382   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    383       VDGB(c,r) = pds(c,r) * qgd(c,r);
    384    
    385   !<  Imported commodity purchases by government at basic prices >!
    386   Variable (orig_level=VMGB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    387       qgm(c,r) # government demand for imported commodity c in region r #;
    388   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    389       VMGB(c,r) # government expenditure on imported c in r at basic prices #;
    390   Read
    391       VMGB from file GTAPDATA header "VMGB";
    392   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    393       VMGB(c,r) = pms(c,r) * qgm(c,r);
    394    
    395   !<  Domestic commodity purchases by government at producer prices >!
    396   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    397       pgd(c,r) # price of domestic com. c purchased by government in region r #;
    398   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    399       VDGP(c,r) # government expenditure on dom. c in r at producer prices #;
    400   Read
    401       VDGP from file GTAPDATA header "VDGP";
    402   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    403       VDGP(c,r) = pgd(c,r) * qgd(c,r);
    404    
    405   !<  Imported commodity purchases by government at producer prices >!
    406   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    407       pgm(c,r) # price of imported com. c purchased by government in region r #;
    408   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    409       VMGP(c,r) # government expenditure on imp. c in r at producer prices #;
    410   Read
    411       VMGP from file GTAPDATA header "VMGP";
    412   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    413       VMGP(c,r) = pgm(c,r) * qgm(c,r);
    414    
    415   !<
    416       Private consumption
    417       -------------------
    418   >!
    419    
    420   !<  Domestic commodity purchases by priv. household at basic prices >!
    421   Variable (orig_level=VDPB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    422       qpd(c,r) # private household demand for domestic commodity c in region r #;
    423   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    424       VDPB(c,r) # private household expenditure on dom. c in r at basic prices #;
    425   Read
    426       VDPB from file GTAPDATA header "VDPB";
    427   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    428       VDPB(c,r) = pds(c,r) * qpd(c,r);
    429    
    430   !<  Imported commodity purchases by priv. household at basic prices >!
    431   Variable (orig_level=VMPB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    432       qpm(c,r) # private household demand for imported commodity c in region r #;
    433   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    434       VMPB(c,r) # private household expenditure on imp. c in r at basic prices #;
    435   Read
    436       VMPB from file GTAPDATA header "VMPB";
    437   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    438       VMPB(c,r)= pms(c,r) * qpm(c,r);
    439    
    440   !<  Domesticcommodity purchases by priv. household at producer prices >!
    441   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    442       ppd(c,r) # price of domestic com. c purchased by private household in r #;
    443   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    444       VDPP(c,r) # private hhld expenditure on dom. c in r at producer prices #;
    445   Read
    446       VDPP from file GTAPDATA header "VDPP";
    447   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    448       VDPP(c,r) = ppd(c,r) * qpd(c,r);
    449    
    450   !<  Imported commodity purchases by priv. household at producer prices >!
    451   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    452       ppm(c,r) # price of imported com. c purchased by private household in r #;
    453   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    454       VMPP(c,r) # private hhld expenditure on imp. c in r at producer prices #;
    455   Read
    456       VMPP from file GTAPDATA header "VMPP";
    457   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    458       VMPP(c,r) = ppm(c,r) * qpm(c,r);
    459    
    460   !<
    461       Investment consumption
    462       ----------------------
    463   >!
    464    
    465   !<  Domestic commodity purchases by investment agent at basic prices >!
    466   Variable (orig_level=VDIB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    467       qid(c,r) # investment demand for domestic commodity c in region r #;
    468   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    469       VDIB(c,r) # investment expenditure on domestic c in r at basic prices #;
    470   Read
    471       VDIB from file GTAPDATA header "VDIB";
    472   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    473       VDIB(c,r) = pds(c,r) * qid(c,r);
    474    
    475   !<  Imported commodity purchases by investment agent at basic prices >!
    476   Variable (orig_level=VMIB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    477       qim(c,r) # investment demand for imported commodity c in region r #;
    478   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    479       VMIB(c,r) # investment expenditure on imported c in r at basic prices #;
    480   Read
    481       VMIB from file GTAPDATA header "VMIB";
    482   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    483       VMIB(c,r) = pms(c,r) * qim(c,r);
    484    
    485   !<  Domestic commodity purchases by investment agent at producer prices >!
    486   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    487       pid(c,r) # price of domestic com. c purchased by investment agent in r #;
    488   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    489       VDIP(c,r) # investment expenditure on dom. c in r at producer prices #;
    490   Read
    491       VDIP from file GTAPDATA header "VDIP";
    492   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    493       VDIP(c,r) = pid(c,r) * qid(c,r);
    494    
    495   !<  Imported commodity purchases by investment agent at producer prices >!
    496   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    497       pim(c,r) # price of imported com. c purchased by investment agent in r #;
    498   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    499       VMIP(c,r) # investment expenditure on imp. c in r at producer prices #;
    500   Read
    501       VMIP from file GTAPDATA header "VMIP";
    502   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    503       VMIP(c,r) = pim(c,r) * qim(c,r);
    504    
    505   !<
    506       Saving
    507       ------
    508   >!
    509    
    510   Variable (all,r,REG)
    511       psave(r) # price of saving in region r #;
    512   Variable (all,r,REG)
    513       qsave(r) # regional demand for NET saving #;
    514   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    515       SAVE(r) # NET saving in region r valued at producer prices #;
    516   Read
    517       SAVE from file GTAPDATA header "SAVE";
    518   Update (all,r,REG)
    519       SAVE(r) = psave(r) * qsave(r);
    520    
    521   !<
    522       Global bank
    523       -----------
    524   >!
    525    
    526   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
    527       pinv(r) # price index of investment goods #;
    528   Variable (all,r,REG)
    529       kb(r) # beginning-of-period capital stock in r #;
    530   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,r,REG)
    531       VDEP(r) # value of capital depeciation in r (exogenous) #;
    532   Read
    533       VDEP from file GTAPDATA header "VDEP";
    534   Update (all,r,REG)
    535       VDEP(r) = pinv(r) * kb(r);
    536   !<
    537       Value of capital depreciation is used to compute the (exogenous)
    538       depreciation rate and therefore does not appear in update.
    539   >!
    540    
    541   !<
    542       International trade
    543       -------------------
    544   >!
    545    
    546   !<  Exports at basic prices >!
    547   Variable (orig_level=VXSB)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    548       qxs(c,s,d) # export sales of commodity c from source s to destination d #;
    549   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    550       VXSB(c,s,d)
    551       # value of exports of  c from s to d at basic prices (tradeables only) #;
    552   Read
    553       VXSB from file GTAPDATA header "VXSB";
    554   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    555       VXSB(c,s,d) = pds(c,s) * qxs(c,s,d);
    556    
    557   !<  Exports at FOB (i.e., exports tax inclusive) prices >!
    558   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    559       pfob(c,s,d) # FOB world price of com. c from source s to destination d #;
    560   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    561       VFOB(c,s,d)
    562       # value of exports of c from s to d at FOB prices (tradeables only) #;
    563   Read
    564       VFOB from file GTAPDATA header "VFOB";
    565   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    566       VFOB(c,s,d) = pfob(c,s,d) * qxs(c,s,d);
    567    
    568   !<  Imports at CIF prices >!
    569   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    570       pcif(c,s,d) # CIF world price of imported com. c from source s to dest. d #;
    571   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    572       VCIF(c,s,d)
    573       # value of imports of c from s to d at CIF prices (tradeables only) #;
    574   Read
    575       VCIF from file GTAPDATA header "VCIF";
    576   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    577       VCIF(c,s,d) = pcif(c,s,d) * qxs(c,s,d);
    578    
    579   !<  Imports at basic (import tariff inclusive) prices >!
    580   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    581       pmds(c,s,d) # price of imported c supplied by source region s to dest. d #;
    582   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    583       VMSB(c,s,d)
    584       # value of imports of c from s to d at domestic (basic) prices #;
    585   Read
    586       VMSB from file GTAPDATA header "VMSB";
    587   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    588       VMSB(c,s,d) = pmds(c,s,d) * qxs(c,s,d);
    589    
    590   !<
    591       International transport margins
    592       -------------------------------
    593   >!
    594    
    595   Variable (orig_level=VST)(all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
    596       qst(m,r) # supply of margin m from region r for international transport #;
    597   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
    598       VST(m,r)
    599       # value of exports of margin m from r for int'l transport at basic prices #;
    600   Read
    601       VST from file GTAPDATA header "VST";
    602   Update (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
    603       VST(m,r) = pds(m,r) * qst(m,r);
    604    
    605   !<
    606       -------------------------------------
    607       A-3. Key derivatives of the Base Data
    608       -------------------------------------
    609    
    610       Key derivatives of the Base Data
    611       Regional expenditure and income
    612       Indirect tax receipts
    613       Miscellaneous coefficients and parameters
    614    
    615   >!
    616    
    617   !<  Intermediate and endowment expenditure by firms at producer prices >!
    618   Coefficient (all,d,DEMD)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    619       VFP(d,a,r) # expenditure on d by act. a in r valued at producer prices #;
    620   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    621       VFP(e,a,r) = EVFP(e,a,r);
    622   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    623       VFP(c,a,r) = VDFP(c,a,r) + VMFP(c,a,r);
    624    
    625   !<  Value of output at supplier's prices >!
    626   Coefficient (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    627       VOS(a,r) # output of act. a in r valued at supplier's prices #;
    628   Formula (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    629       VOS(a,r) = sum{d,DEMD, VFP(d,a,r)};
    630    
    631   !<  Endowments >!
    632   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
    633       VES(e,r) # endowment supply in region r, at supplier's (after tax) prices #;
    634   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
    635       VES(e,r) = sum{a,ACTS, EVOS(e,a,r)};
    636    
    637   !< Commodity supply >!
    638   Coefficient (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    639       MAKEBACT(a,r) # total output of activity a valued at basic prices #;
    640   Formula (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    641       MAKEBACT(a,r) = sum{c,COMM, MAKEB(c,a,r)};
    642    
    643   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    644       MAKEBCOM(c,r) # supply of commodity c valued at basic prices #;
    645   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    646       MAKEBCOM(c,r) = sum{a,ACTS, MAKEB(c,a,r)};
    647    
    648   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    649       VDB(c,r) # domestic sales of c in r at basic prices (tradeables only) #;
    650   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    651       VDB(c,r) = VDPB(c,r) + VDGB(c,r) + VDIB(c,r) + sum{a,ACTS, VDFB(c,a,r)};
    652    
    653   !<  Commodity supply = Commodity demand >!
    654   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    655       VCB(c,r) # supply of commodity c in region r valued at basic prices #;
    656   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    657       VCB(c,r) = VDB(c,r) + sum{d,REG, VXSB(c,r,d)} + IF[c in MARG, VST(c,r)];
    658    
    659   !<
    660       Regional expenditure and income
    661       -------------------------------
    662    
    663       Regional income is allocated between private consumption expenditure,
    664       government consumption expenditure, and saving.
    665    
    666       Expenditure of Regional household
    667       .................................
    668    
    669                      Regional household(h.h.)
    670                       Expenditure = Income
    671                                _/|\_
    672                              _/  |  \_
    673                            _/    |    \_
    674                          _/      |      \_
    675                        _/        |        \_
    676              Private h.h.        |        Government h.h.
    677              ( PRIVEXP )         |          ( GOVEXP )
    678                 _/\_             |              _/\_  <---(CES: ESUBG)
    679               _/    \_           |            _/    \_
    680              /        \          |           /        \
    681           Domestic  Imported   Saving    Domestic    Imported
    682            Goods     Goods     ( SAVE )    Goods       Goods
    683           ( VDPP )  ( VMPP )              ( VDGP )    ( VMGP )
    684    
    685       Note: The coefficients at the ends of branches are
    686             Base Data, e.g., VDPP, SAVE.
    687   >!
    688    
    689   !< Government consumption expenditure, GOVEXP >!
    690   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    691       VGP(c,r) # government cons. expenditure on c in r at producer prices #;
    692   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    693       VGP(c,r) = VDGP(c,r) + VMGP(c,r);
    694   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    695       GOVEXP(r) # aggregate government expenditure in region r #;
    696   Formula (all,r,REG)
    697       GOVEXP(r) = sum{c,COMM, VGP(c,r)};
    698    
    699   !< Private household consumption expenditure, PRIVEXP >!
    700   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    701       VPP(c,r) # private household expenditure on c in r at producer prices #;
    702   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    703       VPP(c,r) = VDPP(c,r) + VMPP(c,r);
    704   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    705       PRIVEXP(r) # aggregate private consumption expenditure in region r #;
    706   Formula (all,r,REG)
    707       PRIVEXP(r) = sum{c,COMM, VPP(c,r)};
    708    
    709   !< Investment consumption expenditure >!
    710   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    711       VIP(c,r) # expenditure on investment c valued at producer prices #;
    712   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    713       VIP(c,r) = VDIP(c,r) + VMIP(c,r);
    714    
    715   !< Aggregate income = aggregate expenditure + saving >!
    716   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    717       INCOME(r) # level of expenditure, which equals NET income in region r #;
    718   Formula (all,r,REG)
    719       INCOME(r) = PRIVEXP(r) + GOVEXP(r) + SAVE(r);
    720    
    721   !<
    722       Indirect tax receipts
    723       ---------------------
    724   >!
    725    
    726   !< Production tax revenue >!
    727   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    728       PTAX(c,a,r) # revenue from tax on commodity c produced by activity a in r #;
    729   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    730       PTAX(c,a,r) = MAKEB(c,a,r) - MAKES(c,a,r);
    731   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    732       TAXROUT(r) # total revenue from production tax payments in region r #;
    733   Formula (all,r,REG)
    734       TAXROUT(r) = sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS, PTAX(c,a,r)}};
    735    
    736   !< Government consumption tax revenue >!
    737   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    738       DGTAX(c,r) # tax revenue from gov't cons. of domestic c in region r #;
    739   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    740       DGTAX(c,r) = VDGP(c,r) - VDGB(c,r);
    741   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    742       MGTAX(c,r) # tax revenue from gov't consumption of imported c in region r #;
    743   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    744       MGTAX(c,r) = VMGP(c,r) - VMGB(c,r);
    745   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    746       TAXRGC(r) # total revenue from government consumption tax payments in r #;
    747   Formula (all,r,REG)
    748       TAXRGC(r) = sum{c,COMM, DGTAX(c,r) + MGTAX(c,r)};
    749    
    750   !< Private household consumption tax revenue >!
    751   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    752       DPTAX(c,r) # tax revenue from priv. hhld cons. of domestic c in region r #;
    753   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    754       DPTAX(c,r) = VDPP(c,r) - VDPB(c,r);
    755   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    756       MPTAX(c,r) # tax revenue from priv. hhld cons. of imported c in region r #;
    757   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    758       MPTAX(c,r) = VMPP(c,r) - VMPB(c,r);
    759   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    760       TAXRPC(r) # total revenue from priv. hhld consumption tax payments in r #;
    761   Formula (all,r,REG)
    762       TAXRPC(r) = sum{c,COMM, DPTAX(c,r) + MPTAX(c,r)};
    763    
    764   !< Investment consumption tax revenue >!
    765   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    766       DITAX(c,r) # tax revenue from investment cons. of domestic c in region r #;
    767   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    768       DITAX(c,r) = VDIP(c,r) - VDIB(c,r);
    769   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    770       MITAX(c,r) # tax revenue from investment cons. of imported c in region r #;
    771   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    772       MITAX(c,r) = VMIP(c,r) - VMIB(c,r);
    773   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    774       TAXRIC(r) # total revenue from investment consumption tax payments in r #;
    775   Formula (all,r,REG)
    776       TAXRIC(r) = sum{c,COMM, DITAX(c,r) + MITAX(c,r)};
    777    
    778   !< Intermediate consumption tax revenue >!
    779   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    780       DFTAX(c,a,r) # tax revenue from use of dom. intermediate c by act. a in r #;
    781   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    782       DFTAX(c,a,r) = VDFP(c,a,r) - VDFB(c,a,r);
    783   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    784       MFTAX(c,a,r) # tax revenue from use of imp. intermediate c by act. a in r #;
    785   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    786       MFTAX(c,a,r) = VMFP(C,a,r) - VMFB(c,a,r);
    787   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    788       TAXRIU(r) # total revenue from tax on intermediate goods usage in r #;
    789   Formula (all,r,REG)
    790       TAXRIU(r) = sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS, DFTAX(c,a,r) + MFTAX(c,a,r)}};
    791    
    792   !< Endowment tax revenue >!
    793   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    794       ETAX(e,a,r) # tax revenue from use of endowment e by act. a in region r #;
    795   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    796       ETAX(e,a,r) = EVFP(e,a,r) - EVFB(e,a,r);
    797   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    798       TAXRFU(r) # total revenue from use of factor/endowment e by act. a in r #;
    799   Formula (all,r,REG)
    800       TAXRFU(r) = sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, ETAX(e,a,r)}};
    801    
    802   !< Endowment income tax revenue <!
    803   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    804       INCTAX(e,a,r) # tax revenue from endowment income tax in region r #;
    805   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    806       INCTAX(e,a,r) = EVFB(e,a,r) - EVOS(e,a,r);
    807    
    808   !< Exports tax revenue <!
    809   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    810       XTAXD(c,s,d) # tax rev. from exports of c from source s to destination d #;
    811   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    812       XTAXD(c,s,d) = VFOB(c,s,d) - VXSB(c,s,d);
    813   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    814       TAXREXP(r) # total revenue from export tax payments in r #;
    815   Formula (all,s,REG)
    816       TAXREXP(s) = sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, XTAXD(c,s,d)}};
    817    
    818   !< Import tariff revenue >!
    819   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    820       MTAX(c,s,d) # tax rev from imports of c from source s to destination d #;
    821   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
    822       MTAX(c,s,d) = VMSB(c,s,d) - VCIF(c,s,d);
    823   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    824       TAXRIMP(r) # total revenue from import tax payments in r #;
    825   Formula (all,d,REG)
    826       TAXRIMP(d) = sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, MTAX(c,s,d)}};
    827    
    828   !<
    829       -----------------------------------
    830       A-4. Commom COEFFICIENTS/PARAMETERS
    831       -----------------------------------
    832       Common coefficients are defined as coefficients which are used in more
    833       than one module. For example, ESUBD(c,r) is used in the goverment household,
    834       private household, and firms modules.
    835   >!
    836    
    837   !< Regional investment expenditure >!
    838   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    839       REGINV(r) # regional GROSS investment in r #;
    840   Formula (all,r,REG)
    841       REGINV(r) = sum{c,COMM, VIP(c,r)};
    842   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    843       NETINV(r) # regional NET investment in region r #;
    844   Formula (all,r,REG)
    845       NETINV(r) = REGINV(r) - VDEP(r);
    846    
    847   !< Net global investment expenditure >!
    848   Coefficient
    849       GLOBINV # global expenditures on net investment #;
    850   Formula
    851       GLOBINV = sum{r,REG, NETINV(r)};
    852    
    853   !< Elasticity of cost with respect to utility from private consumption >!
    854   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    855       CONSHR(c,r) # share of private hhld consumption devoted to good c in r #;
    856   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    857       CONSHR(c,r) = VPP(c,r) / PRIVEXP(r);
    858    
    859   Coefficient (parameter)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    860       INCPAR(c,r) # expansion parameter in the CDE minimum expenditure function #;
    861   Read
    862       INCPAR from file GTAPPARM header "INCP";
    863   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
    864       UELASPRIV(r)
    865       # elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consumption #;
    866   Formula (all,r,REG)
    867       UELASPRIV(r) = sum{c,COMM, CONSHR(c,r) * INCPAR(c,r)};
    868    
    869   !<  Domestic/imported Armington elasticity >!
    870   Coefficient (parameter)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    871       ESUBD(c,r)
    872       # region-specific elast. of subst. for dom. and imp. goods for all agents #;
    873   Read
    874       ESUBD from file GTAPPARM header "ESBD";
    875   Assertion (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG) ESUBD(c,r) ge 0;
    876    
    877   !<
    878       ---------------------
    879       A-5. Common VARIABLES
    880       ---------------------
    881    
    882       Common variables are defined as variables which are used in more than one
    883       module. For example, the variable y(r) is used in the Goverment
    884       Consumption, Private Consumption, Firms, Regional Household and
    885       Investment, Global Bank and Saving modules.
    886       Appendices, e.g., Summary Indices, are not included in this definition.
    887   >!
    888    
    889   Variable (orig_level=INCOME)(all,r,REG)
    890       y(r) # regional household income in region r #;
    891   Variable (all,r,REG)
    892       pop(r) # regional population #;
    893    
    894   Variable (all,r,REG)
    895       pgov(r) # price index for gov't expenditure in region r #;
    896   Variable (all,r,REG)
    897       yg(r) # regional government consumption expenditure in region r #;
    898   Variable (all,r,REG)
    899       ug(r) # per capita utility from gov't expend. in region r #;
    900    
    901   Variable (all,r,REG)
    902       ppriv(r) # price index for priv. household cons. expenditure in region r #;
    903   Variable (all,r,REG)
    904       yp(r) # regional private consumption expenditure in region r #;
    905   Variable (all,r,REG)
    906       uepriv(r) # elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consumption #;
    907   Variable (all,r,REG)
    908       up(r) # per capita utility from private expend. in region r #;
    909    
    910   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    911       to(c,a,r) # power of tax on com. c supplied by act. a in region r #;
    912   Variable (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    913       tinc(e,a,r) # power of income tax on endowment e supplied to act. a in r #;
    914   Variable (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
    915       endwslack(e,r) # slack variable in endowment market clearing condition #;
    916   !<
    917       endwslack is exogenous, unless the user wishes to employ a partial
    918       equilibrium closure in which the price of one or more of the primary factors
    919       is fixed.
    920   >!
    921    
    922   Variable (orig_level=VMB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
    923       qms(c,r) # aggregate imports of c in region r, basic price weights #;
    924   Variable
    925       globalcgds # global supply of capital goods for NET investment #;
    926   Variable
    927       pcgdswld # world average price of capital goods (net investment weights) #;
    928    
    929   !<
    930       ================
    931       Equation modules
    932       ================
    933       1.  Firms
    934       2.  Commodity supply
    935       3.  Income distribution
    936       4.  Allocation of income across expenditure categories
    937       5.  Domestic final demand
    938       6.  Trade, goods market equilibrium and prices
    939       7.  Factor market equilibrium
    940       8.  Allocation of global saving
    941       9.  Tax revenue streams
    942       10. Numeraire and Walras law
    943       11. Welfare measurement and decomposition
    944   >!
    945    
    946   !<
    947       --------
    948       1. Firms
    949       --------
    950    
    951       We now turn to the behavioral equations for firms. The following picture
    952       describes the firms production structure.
    953    
    954                                    qo(a,r)  [ao(a,r)]
    955                                    /\
    956                                   /  \  <----- CES[ESUBT]
    957                                  /    \
    958                                 /      \
    959                                /        \
    960               [ava(a,r)]  qva(a,r)     qint(a,r)  [aint(a,r)]
    961                           /|\            |
    962       CES[ESUBVA]----->  / | \           |  <------ CES[ESUBC]
    963                         /  |  \          |
    964                        /   |   \         |
    965                       /    |    \        |
    966                   Land  Labor  Capital  qfa(c,a,r)  [afa(c,a,r)]
    967                      qfe(e,a,r)          /\
    968                     [afe(e,a,r)]        /  \  <----- CES[ESUBD]
    969                                        /    \
    970                                       /      \
    971                                      /        \
    972                                  Domestic    Foreign
    973                                  qfd(c,a,r)  qfm(c,a,r)
    974    
    975       1-1. Top production nest
    976       1-2. Second level nests
    977       1-3. Sourcing of commodities by firms
    978       1-4. Technical change equations
    979   >!
    980    
    981   !<
    982       1-1. Top production nest
    983       ------------------------
    984   >!
    985    
    986   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    987       po(a,r) # unit cost/revenue of activity a in region r #;
    988   Variable (orig_level=VOS)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    989       qo(a,r) # output of activity a in region r #;
    990   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    991       ao(a,r) # output augmenting technical change by activity a in region r #;
    992   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    993       pint(a,r) # Price of composite intermediate input c by activity a in r #;
    994   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    995       qint(a,r) # Composite intermediate input c by activity a in r #;
    996   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    997       aint(a,r) # Composite interm. input augmenting tech change by act. a in r #;
    998   Coefficient (parameter)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
    999       ESUBT(a,r)
   1000       # elast. of sub. bet. composite intermediate and factor inputs in prod'n #;
   1001   Read
   1002       ESUBT from file GTAPPARM header "ESBT";
   1003   Assertion (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG) ESUBT(a,r) ge 0;
   1004    
   1005   Equation E_qint
   1006   # sector demands for composite intermediate commodity inputs by act. a in r #
   1007   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1008       qint(a,r)
   1009           = - aint(a,r) + qo(a,r) - ao(a,r)
   1010           - ESUBT(a,r) * [pint(a,r) - aint(a,r) - po(a,r) - ao(a,r)];
   1011    
   1012   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1013       pva(a,r) # firms' price of value added in act. a of region r #;
   1014   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1015       qva(a,r) # value added in act. a of region r #;
   1016   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1017       ava(a,r) # value added augmenting tech change by act. a in region r #;
   1018    
   1019   Equation E_qva
   1020   # sector demands for primary factor composite #
   1021   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1022       qva(a,r)
   1023           = -ava(a,r) + qo(a,r) - ao(a,r)
   1024           - ESUBT(a,r) * [pva(a,r) - ava(a,r) - po(a,r) - ao(a,r)];
   1025    
   1026   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1027       pfa(c,a,r) # firms' price for commodity c for use by act. a in r #;
   1028   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1029       qfa(c,a,r) # demand for commodity c for use by act. a in region r #;
   1030   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1031       afa(c,a,r) # composite intermed. inpt c augmenting tech ch. by act. a in r #;
   1032   Variable (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1033       afe(e,a,r) # primary factor e augmenting tech change by act. a in r #;
   1034   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1035       profitslack(a,r) # slack variable in the zero profit equation #;
   1036   !<
   1037       profitslack is exogenous, unless the user wishes to specify output in a
   1038       given region exogenously.
   1039   >!
   1040    
   1041   Coefficient (all,d,DEMD)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1042       STC(d,a,r) # share of input d in total costs of act. a in r #;
   1043   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   1044   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   1045   Formula (all,d,DEMD)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1046       STC(d,a,r) = VFP(d,a,r) / VOS(a,r);
   1047   Zerodivide off;
   1048    
   1049   Equation E_qo
   1050   # industry zero pure profits condition #
   1051   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1052       po(a,r) + ao(a,r)
   1053           = sum{e,ENDW, STC(e,a,r) * [pfe(e,a,r) - afe(e,a,r) - ava(a,r)]}
   1054           + sum{c,COMM, STC(c,a,r) * [pfa(c,a,r) - afa(c,a,r) - aint(a,r)]}
   1055           + profitslack(a,r);
   1056   !<
   1057       E_qo defines industry zero pure profits condition. This condition
   1058       permits us to determine the endogenous output level for each sector,
   1059       except when profitslack is itself endogenous.
   1060   >!
   1061    
   1062   !<
   1063       1-2. Second level nest
   1064       ----------------------
   1065   >!
   1066    
   1067   Coefficient (parameter)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1068       ESUBC(a,r)
   1069       # elasticity of substitution among intermediate inputs in production #;
   1070   Read
   1071       ESUBC from file GTAPPARM header "ESBC";
   1072   Assertion (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG) ESUBC(a,r) ge 0;
   1073    
   1074   Equation E_qfa
   1075   # industry demands for intermediate inputs c by act. a in region r #
   1076   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1077       qfa(c,a,r)
   1078           = - afa(c,a,r) + qint(a,r)
   1079           - ESUBC(a,r) * [pfa(c,a,r) - afa(c,a,r) - pint(a,r)];
   1080    
   1081   Coefficient (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1082       TINTCOM(a,r) # total intermediate commodity inputs of act. a in r #;
   1083   Formula (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1084       TINTCOM(a,r) = sum{c,COMM,VFP(c,a,r)};
   1085   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1086       INTSHR(c,a,r) # share of intermed. c in total com. inputs of act. a in r #;
   1087   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   1088   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   1089   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1090       INTSHR(c,a,r) = VFP(c,a,r)/TINTCOM(a,r);
   1091   Zerodivide off;
   1092    
   1093   Equation E_pint
   1094   # price of composite intermediate commodity inputs by act. a in r #
   1095   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1096       pint(a,r) = sum{c,COMM, INTSHR(c,a,r) * [pfa(c,a,r) - afa(c,a,r)]};
   1097   !<
   1098       E_pint defines the average price of intermediate input composite.
   1099   >!
   1100    
   1101   Coefficient (parameter)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1102       ESUBVA(a,r)
   1103       # elast. of sub. among capital/labor/land in value added of activity a #;
   1104   Read
   1105       ESUBVA from file GTAPPARM header "ESBV";
   1106   Assertion (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG) ESUBVA(a,r) ge 0;
   1107    
   1108   Coefficient (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1109       VVA(a,r) # value added in act. a in region r #;
   1110   Formula (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1111       VVA(a,r) = sum{e,ENDW, VFP(e,a,r)};
   1112   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)
   1113       DEFAULTVASHR(e) # zerodivide default for VASHR # ;
   1114   Formula (all,e,ENDW)
   1115       DEFAULTVASHR(e)
   1116           = sum{a,ACTS, sum{r,REG, VFP(e,a,r)}}
   1117           / sum{a,ACTS, sum{r,REG, VVA(a,r)}};
   1118   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1119       VASHR(e,a,r) # share of e in total value added in act. a in r #;
   1120   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG: VVA(a,r) <> 0)
   1121       VASHR(e,a,r) = VFP(e,a,r) / VVA(a,r);
   1122   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG: VVA(a,r) = 0)
   1123       VASHR(e,a,r) = DEFAULTVASHR(e);
   1124    
   1125   Equation E_qfe
   1126   # demands for endowment commodities #
   1127   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1128       qfe(e,a,r)
   1129           = - afe(e,a,r) + qva(a,r)
   1130           - ESUBVA(a,r) * [pfe(e,a,r) - afe(e,a,r) - pva(a,r)];
   1131    
   1132   Equation E_pva
   1133   # effective price of primary factor composite in each sector/region #
   1134   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1135       pva(a,r) = sum{e,ENDW, VASHR(e,a,r) * [pfe(e,a,r) - afe(e,a,r)]};
   1136    
   1137   !<
   1138       1-3. Sourcing of commodities by firms
   1139       -------------------------------------
   1140   >!
   1141    
   1142   Equation E_qfd
   1143   # act. a demands for domestic good c #
   1144   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1145       qfd(c,a,r) = qfa(c,a,r) - ESUBD(c,r) * [pfd(c,a,r) - pfa(c,a,r)];
   1146    
   1147   Equation E_qfm
   1148   # act. a demands for composite import c #
   1149   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1150       qfm(c,a,r) = qfa(c,a,r) - ESUBD(c,r) * [pfm(c,a,r) - pfa(c,a,r)];
   1151    
   1152   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,s,REG)
   1153       FMSHR(c,a,s) # share of firms' imports in dom. composite, purch. prices #;
   1154   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   1155   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,s,REG)
   1156       FMSHR(c,a,s) = VMFP(c,a,s) / VFP(c,a,s);
   1157   Zerodivide off;
   1158    
   1159   Equation E_pfa
   1160   # industry price for composite commodities #
   1161   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1162       pfa(c,a,r) = [1 - FMSHR(c,a,r)] * pfd(c,a,r) + FMSHR(c,a,r) * pfm(c,a,r);
   1163    
   1164   !<
   1165       1-4. Technical change equations
   1166       -------------------------------
   1167   >!
   1168    
   1169   !< Hicks-neutral technical change shifters >!
   1170   Variable (all,a,ACTS)
   1171       aosec(a) # output tech change for act. a, worldwide #;
   1172   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1173       aoreg(r) # specific output tech change in region r #;
   1174   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1175       aoall(a,r) # output augmenting technical change in act. a of r #;
   1176   Equation E_ao
   1177   # sector/region specific average rate of output augmenting tech change #
   1178   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1179       ao(a,r) = aosec(a) + aoreg(r) + aoall(a,r);
   1180    
   1181   !< Intermediate input technical change and shifters >!
   1182   Variable (all,c,COMM)
   1183       afcom(c) # intermediate tech change of input c, worldwide #;
   1184   Variable (all,a,ACTS)
   1185       afsec(a) # intermediate tech change of act. a, worldwide #;
   1186   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1187       afreg(r) # intermediate tech change in region r #;
   1188   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1189       afall(c,a,r) # intermediate input c augmenting tech change by act. a in r #;
   1190   Equation E_afa
   1191   # sector/region specific average rate of intermediates augmenting tech change #
   1192   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1193       afa(c,a,r) = afcom(c) + afsec(a) + afreg(r) + afall(c,a,r);
   1194    
   1195   !< Composite value-added technical change and shifters >!
   1196   Variable (all,a,ACTS)
   1197       avasec(a) # value added tech change for act. a, worldwide #;
   1198   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1199       avareg(r) # value added tech change in region r #;
   1200   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1201       avaall(a,r) # value added augmenting technical change in act. a of r #;
   1202   Equation E_ava
   1203   # sector/region specific average rate of value added augmenting tech change #
   1204   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1205       ava(a,r) = avasec(a) + avareg(r) + avaall(a,r);
   1206    
   1207   !< Factor input technical change and shifters  >!
   1208   Variable (all,e,ENDW)
   1209       afecom(e) # factor input tech change of endowwment e, worldwide #;
   1210   Variable (all,a,ACTS)
   1211       afesec(a) # factor input tech change of act. a, worldwide #;
   1212   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1213       afereg(r) # factor input tech change in region r #;
   1214   Variable (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1215       afeall(e,a,r) # primary factor e augmenting tech change for act. a in r #;
   1216   Equation E_afe
   1217   # sector/region specific average rate of prim. factor e augmenting tech change #
   1218   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1219       afe(e,a,r) = afecom(e) + afesec(a) + afereg(r) + afeall(e,a,r);
   1220    
   1221   !< Composite intermediate input technical change and shifters >!
   1222   Variable (all,a,ACTS)
   1223       aintsec(a) # composite interm. input augmenting tech change, worldwide #;
   1224   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1225       aintreg(r) # composite interm. input augmenting tech change in region r #;
   1226   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1227       aintall(a,r) # comp. interm. input augmenting tech change of act. a in r #;
   1228   Equation E_aint
   1229   # sector/region specific Composite intermediate input augmenting tech change #
   1230   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1231       aint(a,r) = aintsec(a) + aintreg(r) + aintall(a,r);
   1232    
   1233   !<
   1234       ---------------------
   1235       2-0. Commodity supply
   1236       ---------------------
   1237    
   1238       The following picture describes commodity supply and sourcing. On the supply
   1239       side, activities with multiple outputs are given a CET specification wherein
   1240       they maximize their total revenue stream subject to being on the constant
   1241       elasticity of transformation frontier. On the demand side, buyers of a
   1242       commodity produced by multiple activities wish to minimize the total cost
   1243       of supply subject to a CES preference function.
   1244    
   1245                                    qo(a,r)  [ao(a,r)]
   1246                                     |
   1247                  CET[ETRAQ] ----->  | 'make'
   1248                                     |
   1249                                  qca(c,a,r)
   1250                                     |
   1251                  CES[ESUBQ] ----->  |  'sourcing'
   1252                                     |
   1253                                   qc(c,r)
   1254   >!
   1255    
   1256   Coefficient (parameter)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1257       ETRAQ(a,r)
   1258       # elasticity of transformation among commodities produced by act. a #;
   1259   Read
   1260       ETRAQ from file GTAPPARM header "ETRQ";
   1261   Assertion (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG) ETRAQ(a,r) lt 0;
   1262    
   1263   Coefficient (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1264       MAKESCOM(a,r) # pre-tax output of activity a in r #;
   1265   Formula (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1266       MAKESCOM(a,r) = sum{c,COMM, MAKES(c,a,r)};
   1267   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1268       MAKESACTSHR(c,a,r) # share of c and a in output of a at supplier prices #;
   1269   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   1270   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   1271   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1272       MAKESACTSHR(c,a,r) = MAKES(c,a,r) / MAKESCOM(a,r);
   1273   Zerodivide off;
   1274    
   1275   Equation E_qca
   1276   # supply of commodities by act. a #
   1277   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1278       qca(c,a,r) = IF[MAKES(c,a,r) gt 0,
   1279                       qo(a,r) - ETRAQ(a,r) * [ps(c,a,r) - po(a,r)]];
   1280    
   1281   Equation E_po
   1282   # average unit (tax-exclusive) cost of output of act. a #
   1283   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1284        po(a,r) = sum{c,COMM, MAKESACTSHR(c,a,r) * ps(c,a,r)};
   1285    
   1286   Equation E_ps
   1287   # links basic and supply price of commodity c produced by activity a in r #
   1288   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1289       pca(c,a,r) = ps(c,a,r) + to(c,a,r);
   1290   !<
   1291       E_ps links supplier/producer (pre-) and basic (post-tax) prices for firms.
   1292       This captures the effect of output taxes or subsidies.
   1293       Note: The power of activity tax, to, is commodity- and activity-specific.
   1294             to(c,a,r) > 1 in the case of a tax
   1295             to(c,a,r) < 1 in the case of a subsidy.
   1296   >!
   1297    
   1298   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1299       pb(a,r) # price index: basic (tax-inclusive) price of output of act. a #;
   1300   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1301       MAKEBACTSHR(c,a,r) # share of c and a in output of act. a at basic prices #;
   1302   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   1303   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   1304   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1305       MAKEBACTSHR(c,a,r) = MAKEB(c,a,r) / MAKEBACT(a,r);
   1306   Zerodivide off;
   1307    
   1308   Equation E_pb
   1309   # price index: basic (tax-inclusive) price of output of act. a #
   1310   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1311        pb(a,r) = sum{c,COMM, MAKEBACTSHR(c,a,r) * pca(c,a,r)};
   1312    
   1313   Coefficient (parameter)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1314       ESUBQ(c,r)
   1315       # 1/CES elast. for sourcing of commodity c produced by various activities #;
   1316   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1317       ESUBQ(c,r) = 0.0; ! ie, Default 0.0 means perfect substitutes !
   1318   Read (ifheaderexists) ESUBQ from file GTAPPARM header "ESBQ";
   1319   Assertion (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG) ESUBQ(c,r) ge 0;
   1320   !<
   1321       ESUBQ is 1/CES elasticity. ESUBQ=0.0 means that commodity c produced by 2
   1322       or more activities are perfect substitutes--i.e., each activity receives the
   1323       same price (i.e., the law of one price holds) for a given commodity.
   1324       In the equation E_pca below,  pca(c,a,r) = pds(c,r) if ESUBQ = 0.0
   1325       But this will not work well if two or more activities each only produce the
   1326       same good (e.g., CoalElec and NuclearElec each only produce electricity),
   1327       resulting in structurally singular matrix problems, especially under the
   1328       standard GTAP closure, where most factors used by these activitiesare
   1329       perfectly mobile. In such cases, capital could be set as a sluggish
   1330       factor (note: if ETRAE=-0.000001, capital becomes a sector-specific factor);
   1331       or alternatively, capital could be perfectfly mobile across sectors but with
   1332       ESUBQ set to allow for a degree of commodity sourcing differentiation
   1333       (i.e., commodity c produced by diff activities are imperfect substitutes).
   1334       For example, ESUBQ could be set to 0.5 giving an elasticity of substitution
   1335       of 2.0 = 1/ESUBQ = 1/0.5. Alternative values for ESUBQ could be defined by
   1336       the user in the parameter input file.
   1337   >!
   1338    
   1339   Variable (orig_level=VCB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1340       qc(c,r) # total commodity supply in region r #;
   1341   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1342       MAKEBCOMSHR(c,a,r) # share of c by a in commodity supply at basic prices #;
   1343   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   1344   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   1345   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1346       MAKEBCOMSHR(c,a,r) = MAKEB(c,a,r) / MAKEBCOM(c,r);
   1347   Zerodivide off;
   1348    
   1349   Equation E_pca
   1350   # CES allocation of commodity output by activity (ESUBQ(c,r) is 1/CES elast.) #
   1351   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1352       pca(c,a,r) = IF[MAKEB(c,a,r) gt 0,
   1353                       pds(c,r) - ESUBQ(c,r) * [qca(c,a,r) - qc(c,r)]];
   1354    
   1355   Equation E_qc
   1356   # market clearing condition for total commodity supply #
   1357   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1358        qc(c,r) = sum{a,ACTS, MAKEBCOMSHR(c,a,r) * qca(c,a,r)};
   1359    
   1360   !<
   1361       ------------------------
   1362       3-0. Income distribution
   1363       ------------------------
   1364   >!
   1365    
   1366   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1367       fincome(r) # factor income at basic prices net of depreciation #;
   1368   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1369       FY(r) # primary factor income in r net of depreciation #;
   1370   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1371       FY(r) = sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, EVFB(e,a,r)}} - VDEP(r);
   1372    
   1373   Equation E_fincome
   1374   # factor income at basic prices net of depreciation #
   1375   (all,r,REG)
   1376       FY(r) * fincome(r)
   1377           = sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, EVFB(e,a,r)*[peb(e,a,r) + qes(e,a,r)]}}
   1378           - VDEP(r)  * [pinv(r) + kb(r)];
   1379    
   1380   !< Computation of Regional Income >!
   1381   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1382       incomeslack(r) # slack variable in the expression for regional income #;
   1383       !< This is exogenous, unless the user wishes to fix regional income. >!
   1384   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   1385       del_indtaxr(r) # change in ratio of indirect taxes to INCOME in r #;
   1386   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1387       INDTAX(r) # indirect tax receipts in r #;
   1388   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1389       INDTAX(r) = TAXRPC(r) + TAXRGC(r) + TAXRIC(r) + TAXRIU(r) + TAXRFU(r)
   1390                 + TAXROUT(r) + TAXREXP(r) + TAXRIMP(r);
   1391    
   1392   Equation E_y
   1393   # regional income = sum of primary factor income and indirect tax receipts #
   1394   (all,r,REG)
   1395       INCOME(r) * y(r)
   1396           = FY(r) * fincome(r)
   1397           + 100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_indtaxr(r)
   1398           + INDTAX(r) * y(r)
   1399           + INCOME(r) * incomeslack(r);
   1400    
   1401   !<
   1402       -------------------------------------------------------
   1403       4-0. Allocation of income across expenditure categories
   1404       -------------------------------------------------------
   1405   >!
   1406    
   1407   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1408       uelas(r) # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility #;
   1409   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1410       dpsave(r) # saving distribution parameter #;
   1411   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1412       dpgov(r) # government consumption distribution parameter #;
   1413   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1414       dppriv(r) # private consumption distribution parameter #;
   1415    
   1416   Equation E_qsave
   1417   # saving #
   1418   (all,r,REG)
   1419       psave(r) + qsave(r) - y(r) = uelas(r) + dpsave(r);
   1420    
   1421   Equation E_yg
   1422   # government consumption expenditure #
   1423   (all,r,REG)
   1424       yg(r) - y(r) = uelas(r) + dpgov(r);
   1425    
   1426   Equation E_yp
   1427   # private consumption expenditure #
   1428   (all,r,REG)
   1429       yp(r) - y(r) = -[uepriv(r) - uelas(r)] + dppriv(r);
   1430    
   1431   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1432       dpav(r) # average distribution parameter shift, for EV calc. #;
   1433   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1434       XSHRPRIV(r) # private expenditure share in regional income #;
   1435   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1436       XSHRPRIV(r) = PRIVEXP(r) / INCOME(r);
   1437   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1438       XSHRGOV(r) # government expenditure share in regional income #;
   1439   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1440       XSHRGOV(r) = GOVEXP(r) / INCOME(r);
   1441   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1442       XSHRSAVE(r) # saving share in regional income #;
   1443   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1444       XSHRSAVE(r) = SAVE(r) / INCOME(r);
   1445    
   1446   Equation E_uelas
   1447   # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility #
   1448   (all,r,REG)
   1449       uelas(r) = XSHRPRIV(r) * uepriv(r) - dpav(r);
   1450    
   1451   Equation E_dpav
   1452   # average distribution parameter shift #
   1453   (all,r,REG)
   1454       dpav(r)
   1455           = XSHRPRIV(r) * dppriv(r)
   1456           + XSHRGOV(r)  * dpgov(r)
   1457           + XSHRSAVE(r) * dpsave(r);
   1458    
   1459   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1460       p(r) # price index for disposition of income by regional household #;
   1461    
   1462   Equation E_p
   1463   # price index for disposition of income by regional household #
   1464   (all,r,REG)
   1465       p(r) = XSHRPRIV(r) * ppriv(r) + XSHRGOV(r) * pgov(r)
   1466            + XSHRSAVE(r) * psave(r);
   1467    
   1468   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1469       au(r) # input-neutral shift in utility function #;
   1470   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1471       dpsum(r) # sum of the distribution parameters #;
   1472   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1473       u(r) # per capita utility from aggregate hhld expend. in region r #;
   1474   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1475       DPARSUM(r) # sum of distribution parameters #;
   1476   Read
   1477       DPARSUM from file GTAPDATA header "DPSM";
   1478   Update (all,r,REG)
   1479       DPARSUM(r) = dpsum(r);
   1480    
   1481   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1482       UTILELAS(r) # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility #;
   1483   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1484       UTILELAS(r)
   1485           = [UELASPRIV(r) * XSHRPRIV(r) + XSHRGOV(r) + XSHRSAVE(r)] / DPARSUM(r);
   1486   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1487       DPARPRIV(r) # private consumption distribution parameter #;
   1488   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1489       DPARPRIV(r) = UELASPRIV(r) * XSHRPRIV(r) / UTILELAS(r);
   1490   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1491       DPARGOV(r) # government consumption distribution parameter #;
   1492   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1493       DPARGOV(r) = XSHRGOV(r) / UTILELAS(r);
   1494    
   1495   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1496       DPARSAVE(r) # saving distribution parameter #;
   1497   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1498       DPARSAVE(r) = XSHRSAVE(r) / UTILELAS(r);
   1499    
   1500   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1501       UTILPRIV(r) # utility from private consumption #;
   1502   Formula (initial)(all,r,REG)
   1503       UTILPRIV(r) = 1.0;
   1504   Update (all,r,REG)
   1505       UTILPRIV(r) = up(r);
   1506    
   1507   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1508       UTILGOV(r) # utility from government consumption #;
   1509   Formula (initial)(all,r,REG)
   1510       UTILGOV(r) = 1.0;
   1511   Update (all,r,REG)
   1512       UTILGOV(r) = ug(r);
   1513    
   1514   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1515       UTILSAVE(r) # utility from saving #;
   1516   Formula (initial)(all,r,REG)
   1517       UTILSAVE(r) = 1.0;
   1518   Update (change) (all,r,REG)
   1519       UTILSAVE(r) = [[qsave(r) - pop(r)] / 100] * UTILSAVE(r);
   1520    
   1521   Equation E_u
   1522   # regional household utility #
   1523   (all,r,REG)
   1524       u(r) = au(r) + DPARPRIV(r) * loge(UTILPRIV(r)) * dppriv(r)
   1525            + DPARGOV(r) * loge(UTILGOV(r)) * dpgov(r)
   1526            + DPARSAVE(r) * loge(UTILSAVE(r)) * dpsave(r)
   1527            + [1.0 / UTILELAS(r)] * [y(r) - pop(r) - p(r)];
   1528    
   1529   Equation E_dpsum
   1530   # sum of the distribution parameters #
   1531   (all,r,REG)
   1532       DPARSUM(r) * dpsum(r)
   1533           = DPARPRIV(r) * dppriv(r)
   1534           + DPARGOV(r) * dpgov(r)
   1535           + DPARSAVE(r) * dpsave(r);
   1536    
   1537   !<
   1538       --------------------------
   1539       5-0. Domestic final demand
   1540       --------------------------
   1541   >!
   1542    
   1543   !<
   1544       5-1. Private expenditures
   1545       -------------------------
   1546   >!
   1547    
   1548   !<  We first compute for the Allen Partials, Price and Income Elasticities
   1549       then derive Private household's Composite Demand >!
   1550   Coefficient (parameter)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1551       SUBPAR(c,r)
   1552       # substitution parameter in CDE minimum expenditure function #;
   1553   Read
   1554       SUBPAR from file GTAPPARM header "SUBP";
   1555   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1556       ALPHA(c,r) # 1 - sub. parameter in the CDE minimum expenditure function #;
   1557   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1558       ALPHA(c,r) = 1 - SUBPAR(c,r);
   1559   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,k,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1560       APE(c,k,r) # Allen partial elast. of sub. between composite c and k in r #;
   1561   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,k,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1562       APE(c,k,r)
   1563           = ALPHA(c,r) + ALPHA(k,r) - sum{n,COMM, CONSHR(n,r) * ALPHA(n,r)};
   1564   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1565       APE(c,c,r)
   1566           = 2.0 * ALPHA(c,r)
   1567           - sum{n,COMM, CONSHR(n,r) * ALPHA(n,r)}
   1568           - ALPHA(c,r) / CONSHR(c,r);
   1569    
   1570   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1571       EY(c,r) # income elast. of private hhld demand for c in r #;
   1572   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1573       EY(c,r)
   1574           =   [1.0 / sum{n,COMM, CONSHR(n,r) * INCPAR(n,r)}]
   1575               * [INCPAR(c,r) * [1.0 - ALPHA(c,r)]
   1576                   + sum{n,COMM, CONSHR(n,r) * INCPAR(n,r) * ALPHA(n,r)}]
   1577           + [ALPHA(c,r) - sum{n,COMM, CONSHR(n,r) * ALPHA(n,r)}];
   1578    
   1579   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,k,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1580       EP(c,k,r)
   1581       # uncomp. elast. of private hhld demand for c wrt price of k in r #;
   1582   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,k,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1583       EP(c,k,r) = 0;
   1584   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,k,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1585       EP(c,k,r) = [APE(c,k,r) - EY(c,r)] * CONSHR(k,r);
   1586    
   1587   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1588       ppa(c,r) # private consumption price for commodity c in region r #;
   1589   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1590       qpa(c,r) # private hhld demand for commodity c in region r #;
   1591    
   1592   Equation E_qpa
   1593   # private consumption demands for composite commodities #
   1594   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1595       qpa(c,r) - pop(r)
   1596           = sum{k,COMM, EP(c,k,r) * ppa(k,r)} + EY(c,r) * [yp(r) - pop(r)];
   1597   !<
   1598       E_qpa defines private consumption demands for composite commodities.
   1599       Demand system is on a per capita basis. Here, yp(r) - pop(r) is % change in
   1600       per capita income.
   1601   >!
   1602    
   1603   !< Utility from Private Consumption >!
   1604   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1605       XWCONSHR(c,r) # expansion-parameter-weighted consumption share #;
   1606   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1607       XWCONSHR(c,r) = CONSHR(c,r) * INCPAR(c,r) / UELASPRIV(r);
   1608    
   1609   Equation E_uepriv
   1610   # elasticity of expenditure wrt utility from private consumption #
   1611   (all,r,REG)
   1612       uepriv(r) = sum{c,COMM, XWCONSHR(c,r) * [ppa(c,r) + qpa(c,r) - yp(r)]};
   1613    
   1614   Equation E_ppriv
   1615   # price index for private consumption expenditure #
   1616   (all,r,REG)
   1617       ppriv(r) = sum{c,COMM, CONSHR(c,r) * ppa(c,r)};
   1618    
   1619   Equation E_up
   1620   # computation of utility from private consumption in r #
   1621   (all,r,REG)
   1622       UELASPRIV(r) * up(r) = yp(r) - ppriv(r) - pop(r) ;
   1623   !<
   1624       E_up determines private consumption utility for a representative
   1625       household in region r, based on the per capita private expenditure
   1626       function.
   1627   >!
   1628    
   1629   Equation E_qpd
   1630   # private consumption demand for domestic goods #
   1631   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1632       qpd(c,r) = qpa(c,r) - ESUBD(c,r) * [ppd(c,r) - ppa(c,r)];
   1633    
   1634   !<  Composite Tradeables >!
   1635   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1636       PMSHR(c,r) # share of imports in private hhld cons. at producer prices #;
   1637   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1638       PMSHR(c,r) = VMPP(c,r) / VPP(c,r);
   1639    
   1640   Equation E_qpm
   1641   # private consumption demand for aggregate imports #
   1642   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1643       qpm(c,r) = qpa(c,r) - ESUBD(c,r) * [ppm(c,r) - ppa(c,r)];
   1644    
   1645   Equation E_ppa
   1646   # private consumption price for composite commodities #
   1647   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1648       ppa(c,r) = [1 - PMSHR(c,r)] * ppd(c,r) + PMSHR(c,r) * ppm(c,r);
   1649    
   1650   !<
   1651       5-2. Public expenditures
   1652       -------------------------
   1653   >!
   1654    
   1655   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1656       pga(c,r) # government consumption price for commodity c in region r #;
   1657   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1658       qga(c,r) # government hhld demand for commodity c in region r #;
   1659   Coefficient (parameter)(all,r,REG)
   1660       ESUBG(r)
   1661       # region-specific elast. of subst. for composite government consumption #;
   1662   Read
   1663       ESUBG from file GTAPPARM header "ESBG";
   1664   Assertion (all,r,REG) ESUBG(r) ge 0;
   1665    
   1666   Equation E_qga
   1667   # government consumption demands for composite commodities #
   1668   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1669       qga(c,r) = yg(r) - pgov(r) - ESUBG(r) * [pga(c,r) - pgov(r)];
   1670    
   1671   Equation E_pgov
   1672   # price index for aggregate gov't purchases #
   1673   (all,r,REG)
   1674       pgov(r) = sum{c,COMM, [VGP(c,r) / GOVEXP(r)] * pga(c,r)};
   1675    
   1676   Equation E_ug
   1677   # utility from government consumption in r #
   1678   (all,r,REG)
   1679       ug(r) = yg(r) - pgov(r) - pop(r);
   1680    
   1681   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   1682   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   1683   !<  Composite tradeables >!
   1684   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1685       GMSHR(c,r) # share of imports for gov't hhld at producer prices #;
   1686   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1687       GMSHR(c,r) = VMGP(c,r) / VGP(c,r);
   1688   Zerodivide off;
   1689    
   1690   Equation E_qgd
   1691   # government consumption demand for domestic goods #
   1692   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1693       qgd(c,r) = qga(c,r) - ESUBD(c,r) * [pgd(c,r) - pga(c,r)];
   1694    
   1695   Equation E_qgm
   1696   # government consumption demand for aggregate imports #
   1697   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1698       qgm(c,r) = qga(c,r) - ESUBD(c,r) * [pgm(c,r) - pga(c,r)];
   1699    
   1700   Equation E_pga
   1701   # government consumption price for composite commodities #
   1702   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1703       pga(c,r) = [1 - GMSHR(c,r)] * pgd(c,r) + GMSHR(c,r) * pgm(c,r);
   1704    
   1705   !<
   1706       5-3. Investment expenditures
   1707       ----------------------------
   1708   >!
   1709    
   1710   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1711       pia(c,r) # price of investment commodity in region r #;
   1712   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1713       qia(c,r) # demand for investment commodity c in region r #;
   1714   Variable (orig_level=REGINV)(all,r,REG)
   1715       qinv(r) # demand for investment/capital goods in region r #;
   1716    
   1717   Equation E_qia
   1718   # Top level (Leontief) demand for investment goods #
   1719   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1720       qia(c,r) = qinv(r);
   1721    
   1722   Equation E_pinv
   1723   # defines the price of investment #
   1724   (all,r,REG)
   1725       pinv(r) = sum{c,COMM, [VIP(c,r) / REGINV(r)] * pia(c,r)};
   1726    
   1727   Equation E_qid
   1728   # demand for domestic investment commodity c #
   1729   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1730       qid(c,r) = qia(c,r) - ESUBD(c,r) * [pid(c,r) - pia(c,r)];
   1731    
   1732   Equation E_qim
   1733   # demand for imported investment commodity c #
   1734   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1735       qim(c,r) = qia(c,r) - ESUBD(c,r) * [pim(c,r) - pia(c,r)];
   1736    
   1737   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   1738   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   1739   !<  Composite tradeables >!
   1740   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1741       IMSHR(c,r) # share of imports for investment at producer prices #;
   1742   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1743       IMSHR(c,r) = VMIP(c,r) / VIP(c,r);
   1744   Zerodivide off;
   1745    
   1746   Equation E_pia
   1747   # invesment price for composite commodities #
   1748   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1749       pia(c,r) = [1 - IMSHR(c,r)] * pid(c,r) + IMSHR(c,r) * pim(c,r);
   1750    
   1751   !<
   1752       -----------------------------------------------
   1753       6-0. Trade, goods market equilibrium and prices
   1754       -----------------------------------------------
   1755   >!
   1756    
   1757   !<
   1758       6-1. Sourcing of imports
   1759       ------------------------
   1760   >!
   1761    
   1762   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1763       VMB(c,r) # value of aggregate imports of commodity c in r #;
   1764   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1765       VMB(c,r) = sum{a,ACTS, VMFB(c,a,r)} + VMIB(c,r)
   1766                + VMPB(c,r) + VMGB(c,r);
   1767    
   1768   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1769       FMCSHR(c,a,r) # share of import c used by act. a in r #;
   1770   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   1771       FMCSHR(c,a,r) = VMFB(c,a,r) / VMB(c,r);
   1772    
   1773   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1774       PMCSHR(c,r) # share of import c used by priv. hhlds in total imports in r #;
   1775   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1776       PMCSHR(c,r) = VMPB(c,r) / VMB(c,r);
   1777    
   1778   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1779       GMCSHR(c,r) # the share of import c by gov't hhlds in total imports in r #;
   1780   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1781       GMCSHR(c,r) = VMGB(c,r) / VMB(c,r);
   1782    
   1783   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1784       IMCSHR(c,r) # share of import c by investment agent in total imports in r #;
   1785   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1786       IMCSHR(c,r) = VMIB(c,r) / VMB(c,r);
   1787    
   1788   Equation E_qms
   1789   # assures mkt clearing for imported goods entering each region #
   1790   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1791       qms(c,r)
   1792           = sum{a,ACTS, FMCSHR(c,a,r) * qfm(c,a,r)}
   1793           + PMCSHR(c,r) * qpm(c,r)
   1794           + GMCSHR(c,r) * qgm(c,r)
   1795           + IMCSHR(c,r) * qim(c,r);
   1796    
   1797   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1798       ams(c,s,d) # commodity c augmenting tech change from s to d #;
   1799   Coefficient (parameter)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1800       ESUBM(c,r)
   1801       # region-specific elast. of sub. among imports c in Armington structure #;
   1802   Read
   1803       ESUBM from file GTAPPARM header "ESBM";
   1804   Assertion (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG) ESUBM(c,r) ge 0;
   1805    
   1806   Equation E_qxs
   1807   # regional demand for disaggregated imported commodities by source #
   1808   (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1809       qxs(c,s,d)
   1810           = -ams(c,s,d) + qms(c,d)
   1811           - ESUBM(c,d) * [pmds(c,s,d) - ams(c,s,d) - pms(c,d)];
   1812    
   1813   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   1814       IMPBASIC(c,d) # total imports of good c by DEST region d, at basic prices #;
   1815   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   1816       IMPBASIC(c,d) = sum{s,REG, VMSB(c,s,d)};
   1817   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1818       MSHRS(c,s,d) # share of imports from s in imp. bill of r at basic prices #;
   1819   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1820       MSHRS(c,s,d) = VMSB(c,s,d) / IMPBASIC(c,d);
   1821    
   1822   Equation E_pms
   1823   # price for aggregate imports #
   1824   (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   1825       pms(c,d) = sum{s,REG, MSHRS(c,s,d) * [pmds(c,s,d) - ams(c,s,d)]};
   1826    
   1827   !<
   1828       6-2. International trade and transport margins
   1829       ----------------------------------------------
   1830   >!
   1831    
   1832   !<
   1833       6-2-1. Demand for Global Transport Services
   1834       -------------------------------------------
   1835   >!
   1836    
   1837   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1838       ptrans(c,s,d) # cost index for international transport of c from s to d #;
   1839   Variable (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1840       qtmfsd(m,c,s,d) # international usage margin m on c from s to d #;
   1841   !<
   1842       International margin usage, by Margin, Freight, Source, and Destination,
   1843       i.e., the percent change in usage of m in transport of c from s to d.
   1844   >!
   1845    
   1846   Variable (all,m,MARG)
   1847       pt(m) # price index of composite margins services, by margin mode m #;
   1848   Variable (all,m,MARG)
   1849       qtm(m) # global margin usage #;
   1850   Variable (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1851       atmfsd(m,c,s,d) # tech change in m's shipping of c from region s to d #;
   1852   !<
   1853       Technical progress in shipping by Margin, Freight, Source, and
   1854       Destination.  This is endogenous and driven by the following mode-,
   1855       commodity-, source-, and destination-specific determinants.
   1856   >!
   1857    
   1858   Equation E_qtmfsd
   1859   # bilateral demand for transport services #
   1860   (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1861       qtmfsd(m,c,s,d) = qxs(c,s,d) - atmfsd(m,c,s,d);
   1862   !<
   1863       E_qtmfsd equation computes the bilateral demand for international
   1864       transportation services.  It reflects the fact that the demand for
   1865       services along any particular route is proportional to the quantity of
   1866       merchandise shipped [i.e., QXS(c,s,d)].  It is here that we introduce the
   1867       potential for input-augmenting tech change, atmfsd(m,c,s,d), which is
   1868       commodity- and route-specific.  Thus, in the levels:
   1869               ATMFSD(m,c,s,d) * QTMFSD(m,c,s,d) = QXS(c,s,d)
   1870       where QTMFSD is the amount of composite margins services m used along this
   1871       route.  Technological improvements are reflected by atmfsd(c,s,d) > 0, and
   1872       these reduce the margins services required for this c,s,d triplet.  Tech.
   1873       change also dampens the cost of shipping, thereby lowering the CIF price
   1874       implied by a given FOB value (see 6-2-2).
   1875   >!
   1876    
   1877   Coefficient (ge 0) (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1878       VTMFSD(m,c,s,d)
   1879       # int'l margin usage, by margin, freight, source, and destination #;
   1880   Read
   1881       VTMFSD from file GTAPDATA header "VTWR";
   1882   Update (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1883       VTMFSD(m,c,s,d) = pt(m) * qtmfsd(m,c,s,d);
   1884    
   1885   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1886       VTFSD(c,s,d) # aggregate value of svces in the shipment of c from s to d #;
   1887   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1888       VTFSD(c,s,d) = sum{m,MARG, VTMFSD(m,c,s,d)};
   1889   !<
   1890       In a balanced data base, (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG),
   1891       VCIF(c,s,d) = VFOB(c,s,d) + VTFSD(c,s,d).
   1892   >!
   1893    
   1894   Coefficient
   1895       VTUSE # international margin services usage #;
   1896   Formula
   1897       VTUSE = sum{m,MARG, sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, sum{d,REG, VTMFSD(m,c,s,d)}}}};
   1898   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)
   1899       VTMUSE(m) # international margin services usage, by type #;
   1900   Formula (all,m,MARG)
   1901       VTMUSE(m) = sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, sum{d,REG, VTMFSD(m,c,s,d)}}};
   1902    
   1903   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1904       VTFSD_MSH(m,c,s,d) # share of margin m in cost of getting c from s to d #;
   1905   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   1906           (all,d,REG: VTFSD(c,r,d) > 0.0)
   1907       VTFSD_MSH(m,c,r,d) = VTMFSD(m,c,r,d) / VTFSD(c,r,d);
   1908   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)
   1909           (all,d,REG: VTFSD(c,s,d) = 0.0)
   1910       VTFSD_MSH(m,c,s,d) = VTMUSE(m) / VTUSE;
   1911    
   1912   Equation E_ptrans
   1913   #  generates flow-specific modal average cost of transport index (cf. HT7) #
   1914   (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1915       ptrans(c,s,d)
   1916           = sum{m,MARG, VTFSD_MSH(m,c,s,d) * [pt(m) - atmfsd(m,c,s,d)]};
   1917   !<
   1918       average cost index for margin services used in getting c from s to d
   1919   >!
   1920    
   1921   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)
   1922       VTMPROV(m) # international margin services provision #;
   1923   Formula (all,m,MARG)
   1924       VTMPROV(m) = sum{r,REG, VST(m,r)};
   1925   !<
   1926       In a balanced data base, VTMPROV = VTMUSE.
   1927   >!
   1928   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   1929       VTRPROV(r) # international margin supply, by region #;
   1930   Formula (all,r,REG)
   1931       VTRPROV(r) = sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r)};
   1932   Coefficient
   1933       VT # international margin supply #;
   1934   Formula
   1935       VT = sum{m,MARG, sum{r,REG, VST(m,r)}};
   1936    
   1937   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1938       VTMUSESHR(m,c,s,d) # share of c,s,d usage in global demand for m #;
   1939   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1940       VTMUSESHR(m,c,s,d) = VTFSD(c,s,d) / VT;
   1941   Formula
   1942       (all,m,MARG: VTMUSE(m) <> 0.0)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1943       VTMUSESHR(m,c,s,d) = VTMFSD(m,c,s,d) / VTMUSE(m);
   1944    
   1945   Equation E_qtm
   1946   # global demand for margin m #
   1947   (all,m,MARG)
   1948       qtm(m)
   1949           = sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, sum{d,REG,
   1950             VTMUSESHR(m,c,s,d) * qtmfsd(m,c,s,d)}}};
   1951    
   1952   Coefficient (parameter)(all,m,MARG)
   1953       ESUBS(m)
   1954       # elasticity of sub. among transportation service inputs #;
   1955   Read
   1956       ESUBS from file GTAPPARM header "ESBS";
   1957   Assertion (all,m,MARG) ESUBS(m) ge 0;
   1958    
   1959   Equation E_qst
   1960   # generate demand for regional supply of global transportation service #
   1961   (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   1962       qst(m,r) = qtm(m) - ESUBS(m)*[pds(m,r) - pt(m)];
   1963    
   1964   !<
   1965       6-2-2. Supply of Transport Services
   1966       -----------------------------------
   1967   >!
   1968    
   1969   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   1970       VTSUPPSHR(m,r) # share of region r in global supply of margin m #;
   1971   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   1972       VTSUPPSHR(m,r) = VTRPROV(r) / VT;
   1973   Formula (all,m,MARG: VTMPROV(m) <> 0.0)(all,r,REG)
   1974       VTSUPPSHR(m,r) = VST(m,r) / VTMPROV(m);
   1975    
   1976   Equation E_pt
   1977   # generate price index for composite transportation services #
   1978   (all,m,MARG)
   1979       pt(m) = sum{r,REG, VTSUPPSHR(m,r) * pds(m,r)};
   1980   !<
   1981       E_pt equation generates a price index for transportation services based on
   1982       zero profits.  NOTE:
   1983       (1) Sales to international transportation are not subject to export tax.
   1984           This is why we base the costs to the transport sector at basic prices
   1985           of the goods sold to international transportation.
   1986       (2) We assume that the supply shares for margin services are uniform
   1987           across freight, source of freight, and destination.
   1988   >!
   1989    
   1990   Variable (all,m,COMM)
   1991       atm(m) # tech change in mode m, worldwide #;
   1992   Variable (all,c,COMM)
   1993       atf(c) # tech change shipping of c, worldwide #;
   1994   Variable (all,r,REG)
   1995       ats(r) # tech change shipping from region r #;
   1996   Variable (all,d,REG)
   1997       atd(d) # tech change shipping to d #;
   1998   Variable (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   1999       atall(m,c,s,d) # tech change in m's shipping of c from region s to d #;
   2000    
   2001   Equation E_atmfsd
   2002   #  generates flow-specific average rate of technical change #
   2003   (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2004       atmfsd(m,c,s,d) = atm(m) + atf(c) + ats(s) + atd(d) + atall(m,c,s,d);
   2005    
   2006   !<
   2007       6-3. Trade prices
   2008       -----------------
   2009   >!
   2010    
   2011   !<
   2012       6-3-1. Export Prices
   2013       --------------------
   2014   >!
   2015    
   2016   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2017       tx(c,r) # dest.-gen. change in subsidy on exports of c from r #;
   2018   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2019       txs(c,s,d) # dest.-spec. change in subsidy on exports of c from s to d #;
   2020   !<
   2021       The variable txs captures changes in the power of bilateral export taxes.
   2022       However, the presence of a destination-generic export subsidy shift (tx)
   2023       also permits the user to swap a single export tax shock with another
   2024       target variable.  It is most naturally swapped with the variable qo to
   2025       insulate domestic producers from the world market.
   2026    
   2027       The sign of tx(c,r) and txs(c,s,d) has been CHANGED in GTAP model version 7
   2028       tx(c,r)  > 1 in the case of a tax
   2029       txs(c,r) > 1 in the case of a tax
   2030       tx(c,r)  < 1 in the case of a subsidy.
   2031       txs(c,r) < 1 in the case of a subsidy.
   2032   >!
   2033    
   2034   Equation E_pfob
   2035   # links basic and FOB exports prices #
   2036   (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2037       pfob(c,s,d) = pds(c,s) + tx(c,s) + txs(c,s,d);
   2038    
   2039   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2040       VCIFCOST(c,s,d) # value of imports calculated as total cost of imports #;
   2041   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2042       VCIFCOST(c,s,d) = VFOB(c,s,d) + VTFSD(c,s,d);
   2043    
   2044   Zerodivide (zero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   2045   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2046       FOBSHR(c,s,d) # FOB share in (com. and margin) imports at CIF prices #;
   2047   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2048       FOBSHR(c,s,d) = VFOB(c,s,d) / VCIFCOST(c,s,d);
   2049   Zerodivide (zero_by_zero) off;
   2050    
   2051   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2052       TRNSHR(c,s,d) # Intl. transp. share in (com. and marg) imp. at CIF prices #;
   2053   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2054       TRNSHR(c,s,d) = 1 - FOBSHR(c,s,d);
   2055    
   2056   Equation E_pcif
   2057   # links FOB and CIF prices for good c shipped from region s to d #
   2058   (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2059       pcif(c,s,d) = FOBSHR(c,s,d) * pfob(c,s,d) + TRNSHR(c,s,d) * ptrans(c,s,d);
   2060   !<
   2061       This equation links export and import prices for each commodity/route
   2062       triplet.  Note that technical change is embodied in ptrans(c,s,d) which is
   2063       a cost index.
   2064   >!
   2065    
   2066   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2067       tm(c,r) # source-gen. change in tax on imports of c into r #;
   2068   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2069       tms(c,s,d) # source-spec. change in tax on imports of c from s to d #;
   2070   !<
   2071       The variable tms captures changes in the power of bilateral import taxes.
   2072       However, the presence of a source-generic import tariff shift (tm) also
   2073       permits the user to swap a single import tariff shock with another target
   2074       variable.  In particular, to insulate domestic producers from import price
   2075       changes, it may be swapped with the relative price variable pr -- see
   2076       below.
   2077   >!
   2078    
   2079   Equation E_pmds
   2080   # links basic domestic import prices and CIF import prices #
   2081   (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2082       pmds(c,s,d) = pcif(c,s,d) + tm(c,d) + tms(c,s,d);
   2083    
   2084   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2085       pr(c,r) # ratio of domestic to imported prices in r #;
   2086   Equation E_pr
   2087   # defines target price ratio to be attained via the variable levy #
   2088   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2089       pr(c,r) = pds(c,r) - pms(c,r);
   2090   !<
   2091       E_pr equation defines the target price ratio to be attained VIP the
   2092       variable levy.  This price ratio is the ratio of domestic to average
   2093       imported goods' price.  Note that the way this price ratio is defined, it
   2094       includes intraregional imports as well.  In most applications, regions
   2095       will represent groups of individual countries.  However, in the case of
   2096       the EU, this is problematic, since recent versions of the database have
   2097       incorporated intra-EU trade flows.  Therefore, when aggregated to the EU
   2098       level, the composite import price includes both intra-EU and outside
   2099       imports.  So some modification is needed to handle the EU case.
   2100   >!
   2101    
   2102   !<
   2103       6-4. Goods market equilibrium
   2104       -----------------------------
   2105   >!
   2106   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2107       FDCSHR(c,a,r) # share of dom. prod. c used by act. a in r #;
   2108   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2109       FDCSHR(c,a,r) = VDFB(c,a,r) / VDB(c,r);
   2110   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2111       PDCSHR(c,r) # share of domestic prod. of c used by private hhlds in r #;
   2112   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2113       PDCSHR(c,r) = VDPB(c,r) / VDB(c,r);
   2114   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2115       GDCSHR(c,r) # share of imports of c used by gov't hhlds in r #;
   2116   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2117       GDCSHR(c,r) = VDGB(c,r) / VDB(c,r);
   2118   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2119       IDCSHR(c,r) # share of domestic prod. of c used by investment in r #;
   2120   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2121       IDCSHR(c,r) = VDIB(c,r) / VDB(c,r);
   2122    
   2123   Variable (orig_level=VDB)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2124       qds(c,r) # domestic sales of commodity c in r #;
   2125   Equation E_qds
   2126   # assures market clearing for domestic sales #
   2127   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2128       qds(c,r) = sum{a,ACTS, FDCSHR(c,a,r) * qfd(c,a,r)}
   2129                + PDCSHR(c,r) * qpd(c,r)
   2130                + GDCSHR(c,r) * qgd(c,r)
   2131                + IDCSHR(c,r) * qid(c,r);
   2132    
   2133   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2134       tradslack(c,r) # slack variable in tradeables market clearing condition #;
   2135   !<
   2136       tradslack is exogenous unless the user wishes to specify the price of
   2137       tradeables exogenously, in which case the analysis becomes partial
   2138       equilibrium and walraslack must be exogenized.
   2139   >!
   2140   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2141       DSSHR(c,r) # share of domestic sales of c in r #;
   2142   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2143       DSSHR(c,r) = VDB(c,r) / VCB(c,r);
   2144   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   2145       STSHR(m,r) # share of sales of m to global transport services in r #;
   2146   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   2147       STSHR(m,r) = VST(m,r) / VCB(m,r);
   2148   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2149       XSSHR(c,s,d) # share of export sales of c to s in r #;
   2150   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   2151       XSSHR(c,s,d) = VXSB(c,s,d) / VCB(c,s);
   2152    
   2153   Equation E_pds
   2154   # assures market clearing for commodities #
   2155   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2156       qc(c,r) = DSSHR(c,r) * qds(c,r) + sum(d,REG, XSSHR(c,r,d) * qxs(c,r,d))
   2157               + IF[c in MARG, STSHR(c,r) * qst(c,r)]
   2158               + tradslack(c,r);
   2159    
   2160   !<
   2161       6-5. Agents' prices for goods
   2162       -----------------------------
   2163   >!
   2164    
   2165   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2166       tfd(c,a,r) # tax on domestic c purchased by act. a in r #;
   2167   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2168       tfm(c,a,r) # tax on imported c purchased by act. a in r #;
   2169    
   2170   Equation E_pfd
   2171   # links domestic basic and firm prices #
   2172   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2173       pfd(c,a,r) = pds(c,r) + tfd(c,a,r);
   2174   !<
   2175       E_pfd  links domestic basic and firm prices. It holds only for domestic
   2176       goods and it captures the effect of commodity taxation of firms.
   2177   >!
   2178    
   2179   Equation E_pfm
   2180   # links domestic basic and firm prices #
   2181   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2182       pfm(c,a,r) = pms(c,r) + tfm(c,a,r);
   2183   !<
   2184       E_pfm links domestic basic and firm prices.  It holds only for imported
   2185       goods and it captures the effect of commodity taxation of firms.
   2186   >!
   2187    
   2188   Variable (orig_level=LevTPD)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2189       tpd(c,r) # power of tax on domestic c purchased by private hhld in r #;
   2190   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2191       tpm(c,r) # power of tax on imported c purchased by private hhld in r #;
   2192   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2193       LevTPD(c,r) # levels TPD #;
   2194   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   2195   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG) LevTPD(c,r)  =  VDPP(c,r) / VDPB(c,r);
   2196   Zerodivide off;
   2197    
   2198   Equation E_ppd
   2199   # links basic and private household consumption prices for domestic com. c #
   2200   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2201       ppd(c,r) = pds(c,r) + tpd(c,r);
   2202    
   2203   Equation E_ppm
   2204   # links basic and private household consumption prices for imported com. c #
   2205   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2206       ppm(c,r) = pms(c,r) + tpm(c,r);
   2207    
   2208   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2209       tgd(c,r) # power of tax on domestic c purchased by government hhld in r #;
   2210   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2211       tgm(c,r) # power of tax on imported c purchased by gov't hhld in r #;
   2212    
   2213   Equation E_pgd
   2214   # links basic and government consumption prices for domestic com. c #
   2215   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2216       pgd(c,r) = pds(c,r) + tgd(c,r);
   2217    
   2218   Equation E_pgm
   2219   # links basic and government consumption prices for imported com. c #
   2220   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2221       pgm(c,r) = pms(c,r) + tgm(c,r);
   2222    
   2223   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2224       tid(c,r) # power of tax on domestic invesment commodity c in region r #;
   2225   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2226       tim(c,r) # power of tax on imported invesment commodity c in region r #;
   2227    
   2228   Equation E_pid
   2229   # links basic and investment consumption prices for domestic com. c #
   2230   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2231       pid(c,r) = pds(c,r) + tid(c,r);
   2232    
   2233   Equation E_pim
   2234   # links basic and investment consumption prices for imported com. c #
   2235   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2236       pim(c,r) = pms(c,r) + tim(c,r);
   2237    
   2238    
   2239   !<
   2240       6-6. Private hhld tax shifter
   2241       -----------------------------
   2242   >!
   2243   Variable  (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2244       tpdall(c,r) # comm.-, source-spec. shifter in private cons. tax of dom. c #;
   2245   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2246       tpmall(c,r) # comm.-, source-spec. shifter in private cons. tax of imp. c #;
   2247   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2248       tpreg(r) # source-generic tax shifter on private cons. #;
   2249   !<
   2250       The variable tpreg(r) can be swapped with del_ttaxr(r) in order to generate
   2251       a tax replacement scenario, whereby taxes remain a constant share of
   2252       national income.
   2253   >!
   2254    
   2255   Equation E_tpd
   2256   # permits uniform consumption tax change #
   2257   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2258       tpd(c,r) = tpdall(c,r) + tpreg(r);
   2259    
   2260   Equation E_tpm
   2261   # permits uniform consumption tax change #
   2262   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2263       tpm(c,r) = tpmall(c,r) + tpreg(r);
   2264    
   2265   !<
   2266       ----------------------------
   2267       7. Factor market equilibrium
   2268       ----------------------------
   2269   >!
   2270    
   2271   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,e,ENDWMS)(all,r,REG)
   2272       pe(e,r) # price of mobile and sluggish endowment e in region r #;
   2273   Variable (all,e,ENDWMS)(all,r,REG)
   2274       qe(e,r) # supply of mobile and sluggish endowment e in region r #;
   2275    
   2276   !<
   2277       7-1. Mobile endowments
   2278       ----------------------
   2279   >!
   2280    
   2281   Coefficient (all,e,ENDWM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2282       ENDWMSHR(e,a,r) # share of mobile endow. e used by act. a at supply prices #;
   2283   Formula (all,e,ENDWM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2284       ENDWMSHR(e,a,r) = EVOS(e,a,r) / VES(e,r);
   2285    
   2286   Equation E_pe1
   2287   # mkt clearing for perfectly mobile endowments in each r #
   2288   (all,e,ENDWM)(all,r,REG)
   2289       qe(e,r) = sum{a,ACTS, ENDWMSHR(e,a,r) * qfe(e,a,r)} + endwslack(e,r);
   2290    
   2291   Equation E_qes1
   2292   # basic price of mobile endowments in a in r #
   2293   (all,e,ENDWM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2294       pes(e,a,r) = pe(e,r);
   2295    
   2296   !<
   2297       7-2. Sluggish endowments
   2298       ------------------------
   2299   >!
   2300    
   2301   Coefficient (parameter)(all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   2302       ETRAE(e,r)
   2303       # region-specific elast. of transformation for sluggish factor endowments #;
   2304   Read
   2305       ETRAE from file GTAPPARM header "ETRE";
   2306   Assertion (all,e,ENDWS)(all,r,REG) ETRAE(e,r) lt 0;
   2307    
   2308   Equation E_qes2
   2309   # allocation of sluggish endowments across sectors #
   2310   (all,e,ENDWS)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2311       qes(e,a,r) = qe(e,r) - ETRAE(e,r) * [pes(e,a,r) - pe(e,r)]
   2312                  - endwslack(e,r);
   2313    
   2314   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2315       REVSHR(e,a,r) # Share of endowment e in total endowment revenue/supply #;
   2316   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2317       REVSHR(e,a,r) = EVOS(e,a,r) / VES(e,r);
   2318    
   2319   Equation E_pe2
   2320   # composite price for sluggish endowments #
   2321   (all,e,ENDWS)(all,r,REG)
   2322       pe(e,r) = sum{a,ACTS, REVSHR(e,a,r) * pes(e,a,r)};
   2323    
   2324   !<
   2325       7-3. Sector-specific endowments
   2326       -------------------------------
   2327   >!
   2328    
   2329   Variable (all,e,ENDWF)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2330       qesf(e,a,r) # fixed endowment e in act. a in region r #;
   2331    
   2332   Equation E_qes3
   2333   # equation to assist use of TABmate's automatic closure tool #
   2334   (all,e,ENDWF)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2335       qes(e,a,r) = qesf(e,a,r);
   2336   !<
   2337       For convenience, variable qesf and equation E_qesf are added to assist use
   2338      of TABmate's automatic closure tool
   2339   >!
   2340    
   2341   !<
   2342       7-4. Price of endowments
   2343       ------------------------
   2344   >!
   2345   Variable (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2346       tfe(e,a,r) # tax on primary factor e used by act. a in region r #;
   2347    
   2348   Equation E_pfe
   2349   # links basic and firm demand prices for mobile endowments #
   2350   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2351       pfe(e,a,r) = peb(e,a,r) + tfe(e,a,r);
   2352    
   2353   Equation E_pes
   2354   # links supply (pre-) and basic (post-tax) endowment prices #
   2355   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2356       peb(e,a,r) = pes(e,a,r) + tinc(e,a,r);
   2357    
   2358   Equation E_peb !< This equation assures market clearing for all endowments >!
   2359   # market clearing for endowments in each r #
   2360   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2361       qfe(e,a,r) = qes(e,a,r);
   2362    
   2363   !<
   2364       8. Allocation of global saving
   2365       -------------------------------
   2366   >!
   2367    
   2368   !<
   2369       8-1. Investment preliminaries
   2370       -----------------------------
   2371   >!
   2372   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2373       ke(r) # end-of-period capital stock in r #;
   2374   Coefficient (ge 0)(all,r,REG)
   2375       VKB(r) # value of beginning-of-period capital stock in region r #;
   2376   Update (all,r,REG)
   2377       VKB(r) = pinv(r) * kb(r);
   2378   Read
   2379       VKB from file GTAPDATA header "VKB";
   2380   !<
   2381       VKB(r) is used only in this sub-module, so its data are read here.  The
   2382       associated variables, pinv(r) and kb(r), are used across modules, so they
   2383       have been defined as common variables.
   2384   >!
   2385    
   2386   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2387       INVKERATIO(r)
   2388       # ratio of gross investment to end-of-period capital stock in r #;
   2389   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2390       INVKERATIO(r) = REGINV(r) / [VKB(r) + NETINV(r)];
   2391    
   2392   Equation E_ke
   2393   # ending capital stock equals beginning stock plus net investment.  #
   2394   (all,r,REG)
   2395       ke(r) = INVKERATIO(r) * qinv(r) + [1.0 - INVKERATIO(r)] * kb(r);
   2396    
   2397   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2398       GROSSCAP(r) # gross return to capital #;
   2399   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2400       GROSSCAP(r) = sum{e,ENDWC, VES(e,r)};
   2401    
   2402   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2403       GRNETRATIO(r) # ratio of GROSS/NET rates of return on capital in r #;
   2404   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2405       GRNETRATIO(r) = GROSSCAP(r) / [GROSSCAP(r) - VDEP(r)];
   2406   !<
   2407       NOTE: [GROSSCAP(r) - VDEP(r)] is net returns to capital.
   2408   >!
   2409    
   2410   Variable (orig_level=RORELEV)(all,r,REG)
   2411       rore(r) # expected net rate of return on capital stock in r #;
   2412   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2413       rorc(r) # current net rate of return on capital stock in r #;
   2414   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2415       rental(r) # rental rate on capital = ps("capital",r) #;
   2416    
   2417   Equation E_rental
   2418   # defines a variable for capital rental rate #
   2419   (all,r,REG)
   2420       rental(r) = sum{e,ENDWC, [VES(e,r) / GROSSCAP(r)] * pe(e,r)};
   2421    
   2422   Equation E_rorc
   2423   # current rate of return on capital in region r #
   2424   (all,r,REG)
   2425       rorc(r) = GRNETRATIO(r) * [rental(r) - pinv(r)];
   2426    
   2427   Equation E_kb
   2428   # associates change in cap. services w/ change in cap. stock #
   2429   (all,r,REG)
   2430       kb(r) = sum{e,ENDWC, [VES(e,r) / GROSSCAP(r)] * qe(e,r)};
   2431   !<
   2432       E_kb equation associates any change in capital services during the period
   2433       with a change in capital stock.  Full capacity utilization is assumed.
   2434   >!
   2435    
   2436   !<
   2437       8-2. Rate-of-return sensitive investment allocation
   2438       ---------------------------------------------------
   2439   >!
   2440    
   2441   Coefficient (parameter)(all,r,REG)
   2442       RORFLEX(r)
   2443       # flexibility of expected net ROR on capital stock in r wrt investment #;
   2444   Read
   2445       RORFLEX from file GTAPPARM header "RFLX";
   2446   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2447       RORELEV(r) # level of rore, for orig_level (equilibria make_levels_tab) #;
   2448   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2449       RORELEV(r) = {[GROSSCAP(r) - VDEP(r)] / VKB(r)}
   2450           * [VKB(r) / {VKB(r) - VDEP(r) + REGINV(r)}]^RORFLEX(r);
   2451   !<
   2452       RORFLEX is the flexibility of the expected net rate of return on the
   2453       capital stock, in region r, with respect to investment.  If a region's
   2454       capital stock increases by 1%, then it is expected that the net rate of
   2455       return on capital will decline by RORFLEX %.  A larger absolute value for
   2456       this parameter will reduce the tendency of international investment flows
   2457       to respond to changes in expected rates of return.
   2458   >!
   2459    
   2460   Equation E_rore
   2461   # expected rate of return depends on the current return and investment #
   2462   (all,r,REG)
   2463       rore(r) = rorc(r) - RORFLEX(r) * [ke(r) - kb(r)];
   2464    
   2465   Coefficient (integer,parameter)
   2466       RORDELTA
   2467       # binary coefficient to switch mechanism of allocating investment funds #;
   2468   Read
   2469       RORDELTA from file GTAPPARM header "RDLT";
   2470   !<
   2471       RORDELTA is a binary coefficient which determines the mechanism of
   2472       allocating investment funds across regions.  When RORDELTA = 1, investment
   2473       funds are allocated across regions to equate the change in the expected
   2474       rates of return (i.e., rore(r)).  When RORDELTA = 0, investment funds are
   2475       allocated across regions to maintain the existing composition of capital
   2476       stocks.
   2477   >!
   2478    
   2479   Variable
   2480       rorg # global net rate of return on capital stock #;
   2481   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2482       cgdslack(r) # slack variable for qinv(r) #;
   2483   !<
   2484       cgdslack is exogenous, unless the user wishes to exogenously fix the level
   2485       of gross investment in a region, in which case it can be swapped with
   2486       cgdslack.
   2487   >!
   2488    
   2489   Equation E_qinv
   2490   # either gross investment or expected rate of return in region r #
   2491   (all,r,REG)
   2492       RORDELTA * rore(r)
   2493       + [1 - RORDELTA]
   2494       * [[REGINV(r) / NETINV(r)] * qinv(r) - [VDEP(r) / NETINV(r)] * kb(r)]
   2495           = RORDELTA * rorg + [1 - RORDELTA] * globalcgds + cgdslack(r);
   2496   !<
   2497       This equation determines either gross investment or the expected rate of
   2498       return in each region, depending on the setting for the binary RORDELTA
   2499       parameter.
   2500   >!
   2501    
   2502   Variable (all,e,ENDWC)(all,r,REG)
   2503       expand(e,r) # change in investment relative to endowment stock #;
   2504   Equation E_expand
   2505   # change in investment relative to endowment stock #
   2506   (all,e,ENDWC)(all,r,REG)
   2507       expand(e,r) = qinv(r) - qe(e,r);
   2508   !<
   2509       Capital Accumulation
   2510       (based on the theory laid out in GTAP Technical Paper #7)
   2511   >!
   2512    
   2513   !<
   2514       8-3. Investment allocation based on initial capital shares
   2515       ----------------------------------------------------------
   2516   >!
   2517    
   2518   Equation E_globalcgds
   2519   # either expected global rate of return or global net investment #
   2520       RORDELTA * globalcgds + [1 - RORDELTA] * rorg
   2521           = RORDELTA
   2522           * sum{r,REG,
   2523               [REGINV(r) / GLOBINV] * qinv(r) - [VDEP(r) / GLOBINV] * kb(r)}
   2524           + [1 - RORDELTA] * sum{r,REG, [NETINV(r) / GLOBINV] * rore(r)};
   2525   !<
   2526       E_globalcgds equation computes either the change in global net investment
   2527       (when RORDELTA = 1), or the change in the expected global rate of return on
   2528       capital (when RORDELTA = 0).
   2529   >!
   2530    
   2531   !<
   2532       8-4. Price of saving
   2533       ---------------------
   2534   >!
   2535    
   2536   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2537       psaveslack(r) # slack variable for the saving price equation #;
   2538   !<
   2539       psaveslack is exogenous under the normal closure.  However, in order to
   2540       replicate simulations from the GTAP book, where there was a single saving
   2541       price, psaveslack may be swapped with psave in order to fix the latter.
   2542       In this case, pcgdswld must be the numeraire so that each region faces the
   2543       same price of saving.
   2544   >!
   2545    
   2546   Equation E_psave
   2547   # price of saving #
   2548   (all,r,REG)
   2549       psave(r)
   2550           = pinv(r)
   2551           + sum{s,REG, [[NETINV(s) - SAVE(s)] / GLOBINV] * pinv(s)}
   2552           + psaveslack(r);
   2553   !<
   2554       In contrast to the GTAP book, the price of saving is now region-specific
   2555       and it changes at the same rate as the price of regional investment, plus
   2556       an adjustment factor which accounts for the fact that saving and
   2557       investment are not equal at the regional level.
   2558   >!
   2559    
   2560   Equation E_pcgdswld
   2561   # price index for the aggregate global cgds composite #
   2562       pcgdswld = sum{r,REG, [NETINV(r) / GLOBINV] * pinv(r)};
   2563    
   2564   !<
   2565       9. Tax revenue streams
   2566       ----------------------
   2567   >!
   2568    
   2569   !<
   2570       9-1. Tax revenues generated in production
   2571       -----------------------------------------
   2572   >!
   2573    
   2574   !<
   2575       The following variables could be dropped when converting to levels
   2576       equation for income.  They are only needed for the linearized equation.
   2577       The idea here is to look at the ratio of taxes to income in order to
   2578       preserve homogeneity in prices.  (We could also look at changes in tax
   2579       revenue, but then a uniform price increase would change this variable.)
   2580       Obviously a simple percentage change variable doesn't work, since many
   2581       taxes are initially zero.  The basic logic of this approach is as follows:
   2582    
   2583       Let R be the ratio of taxes to income: R = T/Y, then:
   2584           dR = d(T/Y) = R(t - y)/100
   2585       multiply through by Y to get:
   2586           YdR = dT - Ty/100
   2587       This ratio change is computed for each tax type and for total taxes.  Then
   2588       the change in tax revenue itself may be computed as:
   2589           dT = YdR + Ty/100
   2590       in order to determine regional income.
   2591   >!
   2592    
   2593   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2594       del_taxrout(r) # change in ratio of output tax to INCOME #;
   2595   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2596       del_taxrfu(r) # change in ratio of tax on primary factor usage to INCOME #;
   2597   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2598       del_taxriu(r) # change in ratio of tax on intermediate usage to INCOME #;
   2599   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2600       del_taxrpc(r) # change in ratio of private consumption tax to INCOME #;
   2601   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2602       del_taxrgc(r) # change in ratio of government consumption tax to INCOME #;
   2603   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2604       del_taxric(r) # change in ratio of investment consumption tax to INCOME #;
   2605   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2606       del_taxrexp(r) # change in ratio of export tax to INCOME #;
   2607   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2608       del_taxrimp(r) # change in ratio of import tax to INCOME #;
   2609   Variable (change) (all,r,REG)
   2610       del_taxrinc(r) # change in ratio of income tax to INCOME #;
   2611    
   2612   Equation E_del_taxrout
   2613   # change in ratio of output tax payments to regional income #
   2614   (all,r,REG)
   2615       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrout(r) + TAXROUT(r) * y(r)
   2616           = sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   2617              MAKEB(c,a,r) * to(c,a,r) + PTAX(c,a,r) * [ps(c,a,r) + qca(c,a,r)]}};
   2618    
   2619   Equation E_del_taxrfu
   2620   # change in ratio of tax payments on factor usage to regional income #
   2621   (all,r,REG)
   2622       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrfu(r) + TAXRFU(r) * y(r)
   2623           = sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS,
   2624              VFP(e,a,r) * tfe(e,a,r) + ETAX(e,a,r) * [peb(e,a,r) + qfe(e,a,r)]}};
   2625    
   2626   Equation E_del_taxriu
   2627   # change in ratio of tax payments on intermediate goods to regional income #
   2628   (all,r,REG)
   2629       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxriu(r) + TAXRIU(r) * y(r)
   2630           = sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   2631               VDFP(c,a,r) * tfd(c,a,r) + DFTAX(c,a,r) * [pds(c,r) + qfd(c,a,r)]}}
   2632           + sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   2633               VMFP(c,a,r) * tfm(c,a,r) + MFTAX(c,a,r) * [pms(c,r) + qfm(c,a,r)]}};
   2634    
   2635   !<
   2636       9-2. Tax revenues generated in domestic final demand
   2637       ----------------------------------------------------
   2638   >!
   2639    
   2640   Equation E_del_taxrpc
   2641   # change in ratio of private consumption tax payments to regional income #
   2642   (all,r,REG)
   2643       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrpc(r) + TAXRPC(r) * y(r)
   2644           = sum{c,COMM,
   2645               VDPP(c,r) * tpd(c,r) + DPTAX(c,r) * [pds(c,r) + qpd(c,r)]}
   2646           + sum{c,COMM,
   2647               VMPP(c,r) * tpm(c,r) + MPTAX(c,r) * [pms(c,r) + qpm(c,r)]};
   2648    
   2649   Equation E_del_taxrgc
   2650   # change in ratio of government consumption tax payments to regional income #
   2651   (all,r,REG)
   2652       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrgc(r) + TAXRGC(r) * y(r)
   2653           = sum{c,COMM,
   2654               VDGP(c,r) * tgd(c,r) + DGTAX(c,r) * [pds(c,r) + qgd(c,r)]}
   2655           + sum{c,COMM,
   2656               VMGP(c,r) * tgm(c,r) + MGTAX(c,r) * [pms(c,r) + qgm(c,r)]};
   2657    
   2658   Equation E_del_taxric
   2659   # change in ratio of investment tax payments to regional income #
   2660   (all,r,REG)
   2661       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxric(r) + TAXRIC(r) * y(r)
   2662           = sum{c,COMM,
   2663               VDIP(c,r) * tid(c,r) + DITAX(c,r) * [pds(c,r) + qid(c,r)]}
   2664           + sum{c,COMM,
   2665               VMIP(c,r) * tim(c,r) + MITAX(c,r) * [pms(c,r) + qim(c,r)]};
   2666    
   2667   !<
   2668       9-3. Tax revenues generated in international trade
   2669       --------------------------------------------------
   2670   >!
   2671    
   2672   Equation E_del_taxrexp
   2673   # change in ratio of export tax payments to regional income #
   2674   (all,s,REG)
   2675       100.0 * INCOME(s) * del_taxrexp(s) + TAXREXP(s) * y(s)
   2676           = sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,s,d) * [tx(c,s) + txs(c,s,d)]
   2677           + XTAXD(c,s,d) * [pds(c,s) + qxs(c,s,d)]}};
   2678    
   2679   Equation E_del_taxrimp
   2680   # change in ratio of import tax payments to regional income #
   2681   (all,d,REG)
   2682       100.0 * INCOME(d) * del_taxrimp(d) + TAXRIMP(d) * y(d)
   2683           = sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG,
   2684               VMSB(c,s,d) * [tm(c,d) + tms(c,s,d)]
   2685               + MTAX(c,s,d) * [pcif(c,s,d) + qxs(c,s,d)]}};
   2686    
   2687   !<
   2688       9-4. Income taxes and other tax identities
   2689       ------------------------------------------
   2690   >!
   2691    
   2692   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2693       TAXRINC(r) # income tax payments in r #;
   2694   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2695       TAXRINC(r) = sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, INCTAX(e,a,r)}};
   2696    
   2697   Equation E_del_taxrinc
   2698   # change in ratio of income tax payments to regional income #
   2699   (all,r,REG)
   2700       100.0 * INCOME(r) * del_taxrinc(r) + TAXRINC(r) * y(r)
   2701           = sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, EVFB(e,a,r) * [tinc(e,a,r)]
   2702           + INCTAX(e,a,r) * [pes(e,a,r) + qfe(e,a,r)]}};
   2703    
   2704   Equation E_del_indtaxr
   2705   # change in ratio of indirect taxes to INCOME in r #
   2706   (all,r,REG)
   2707       del_indtaxr(r)
   2708           = del_taxrout(r) + del_taxrfu(r)
   2709           + del_taxriu(r) + del_taxrpc(r) + del_taxrgc(r) + del_taxric(r)
   2710           + del_taxrimp(r)+ del_taxrexp(r);
   2711    
   2712   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   2713       del_ttaxr(r) # change in ratio of taxes to INCOME in r #;
   2714   Equation E_del_ttaxr
   2715   # change in ratio of taxes to INCOME in r #
   2716   (all,r,REG)
   2717       del_ttaxr(r)
   2718           = del_indtaxr(r) + del_taxrinc(r);
   2719   !<
   2720      The del_ttaxr variable can be swapped with the commodity- and source-generic
   2721      consumption tax shift, tp(r), in order to generate a tax replacement
   2722      scenario, whereby taxes remain a constant share of national income.
   2723   >!
   2724    
   2725   !<
   2726       10. Numeraire and closure
   2727       -------------------------
   2728   >!
   2729    
   2730   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   2731       pfactor(r) # price index (at basic prices) of primary factors, by region #;
   2732   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2733       VENDWREG(r) # value of primary factors, at basic prices, by region #;
   2734   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2735       VENDWREG(r) = sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, EVFB(e,a,r)}};
   2736    
   2737   Equation E_pfactor
   2738   # computes % change in price index of primary factors, by region #
   2739   (all,r,REG)
   2740       VENDWREG(r) * pfactor(r)
   2741           = sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, EVFB(e,a,r) * peb(e,a,r)}};
   2742    
   2743   Variable (orig_level=1.0)
   2744       pfactwld # world price index of primary factors #;
   2745   Coefficient
   2746       VENDWWLD # value of primary factors, at basic prices, worldwide #;
   2747   Formula
   2748       VENDWWLD = sum{r,REG, VENDWREG(r)};
   2749    
   2750   Equation E_rorg
   2751   # computes % change in global price index of primary factors #
   2752       VENDWWLD * pfactwld = sum{r,REG, VENDWREG(r) * pfactor(r)};
   2753   !<  This equation derives the price index of primary factors. Note that this is
   2754       the only instance where an equation name breaks the GTAP model's naming
   2755       convention (i.e., equation name does directly not relate to variable being
   2756       derived). This is because PFACTWLD is exogenous as the model.s price
   2757       anchor (numeraire) and thus this equation .explains., RORG which has no
   2758       separate equation (which has been dropped due to Walras' law). Note as well
   2759       that the equation is separated into two. The first E_pfactor defines a
   2760       regional index for factor prices, and the second defines the global index.
   2761       By naming this equation E_rorg and because pfactwld is exogenous, we can
   2762       for convenience, use TABmate's automatic closure tool to list down all
   2763       exogenous and endogenous variable split (i.e., closure) that is consistent
   2764       with the standard GTAP closure. Using TABmate's automatic closure tool is
   2765       beneficial especially during model development or extension.
   2766   >!
   2767    
   2768   Variable
   2769       walras_sup # supply in omitted market--global supply of cgds composite #;
   2770   Variable
   2771       walras_dem # demand in the omitted market--global demand for saving #;
   2772   Variable
   2773       walraslack # slack variable in the omitted market #;
   2774    
   2775   Equation E_walras_sup
   2776   # extra equation: computes change in supply in the omitted market #
   2777       walras_sup = pcgdswld + globalcgds;
   2778   !<
   2779       This is an extra equation which simply computes change in supply in the
   2780       omitted market.  (modified from HT 12 to reflect the value as opposed to
   2781       quantity change, in light of the new treatment of psave(r))
   2782   >!
   2783    
   2784   Equation E_walras_dem
   2785   # extra equation: computes change in demand in the omitted market #
   2786       GLOBINV * walras_dem = sum{r,REG, SAVE(r) * [psave(r) + qsave(r)]};
   2787   !<
   2788       E_walras_dem is an extra equation which simply computes change in demand in
   2789       the omitted market.  (modified from HT 13 to reflect the value as opposed to
   2790       quantity change)
   2791   >!
   2792    
   2793   Equation E_walraslack
   2794   # Check Walras' Law.  Value of "walraslack" should be zero #
   2795       walras_sup = walras_dem + walraslack;
   2796   !<
   2797       E_walraslack allows us to verify that Walras' Law holds. The value of
   2798       walraslack should be zero in any GE simulation. The variable walraslack is
   2799       endogenous under normal, GE closure.  If the GE links are broken, then
   2800       walraslack must be swapped with the numeraire, thereby forcing global
   2801       saving to explicitly equal global investment.
   2802   >!
   2803    
   2804   !<
   2805       ---------------
   2806       Summary Indices
   2807       ---------------
   2808    
   2809       We first calculate a number of useful summary statistics, including
   2810       terms of trade variables/coefficients which are used in the
   2811       Welfare Measurement and Decomposition section (Section 11)
   2812    
   2813       The following equations do not generally affect the equilibrium structure
   2814       of the model, although they do include the equation for the usual numeraire
   2815       variable, "pfactwld".
   2816    
   2817       B-0. Variables and coefficients for summary indices
   2818       B-1. Factor price indices
   2819       B-2. Regional terms of trade (ToT)
   2820       B-3. GDP indices (value, price and quantity)
   2821       B-4. Aggregate trade indices (value, price and quantity)
   2822       B-5. Trade balance indices
   2823       B-6. Terms of trade (ToT) decomposition
   2824   >!
   2825    
   2826   !<
   2827       B-0. Appendix-specific variables and coefficients
   2828       -------------------------------------------------
   2829       only used in this summary indices appendix
   2830   >!
   2831    
   2832   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)
   2833       vxwfob(c,s) # value of merchandise regional exports, by commodity, FOB #;
   2834   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)
   2835       vmwcif(c,s) # value of merchandise regional imports, by commodity, CIF #;
   2836   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2837       vxwreg(r) # value of merchandise exports, by region #;
   2838   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2839       vmwreg(r) # value of merchandise imports, by region, at world prices #;
   2840    
   2841   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2842       VXDFOB(c,r) # FOB value of com. c exports to all dest. (tradeables only) #;
   2843   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2844       VXDFOB(c,r) = sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d)};
   2845    
   2846   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2847       VXW(c,r) # value of exports by commodity c and region r at FOB prices #;
   2848   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   2849       VXW(c,r) = VXDFOB(c,r) + IF[c in MARG, VST(c,r)];
   2850    
   2851   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2852       VXWREGION(r) # value of exports by region r at FOB prices #;
   2853   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2854       VXWREGION(r) = sum{c,COMM, VXW(c,r)};
   2855    
   2856   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   2857       VMCIF(c,d) # value of commodity imports c by DEST. d at CIF prices #;
   2858   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   2859       VMCIF(c,d) = sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,d)};
   2860    
   2861   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2862       VMWREGION(r) # value of commodity imports by region r at CIF prices #;
   2863   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2864       VMWREGION(r) = sum{c,COMM, VMCIF(c,r)};
   2865    
   2866   !<
   2867       B-1. Factor price indices
   2868       -------------------------
   2869   >!
   2870    
   2871   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2872       pfactreal(e,a,r) # ratio of return to primary factor e to CPI in r #;
   2873   Equation E_pfactreal
   2874   # defines the real rate of return to primary factor e in region r #
   2875   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2876       pfactreal(e,a,r) = pes(e,a,r) - ppriv(r);
   2877   !<
   2878       This equation defines the real rate of return to primary factor e in
   2879       region r (new).
   2880   >!
   2881    
   2882   !<  GTAPv7 changes
   2883       November 2017
   2884       Modified equation E_pfactreal above
   2885       from:   pfactreal(e,a,r) = peb(e,a,r) - ppriv(r);
   2886       to:     pfactreal(e,a,r) = pes(e,a,r) - ppriv(r);
   2887    
   2888       Added variables and equations representing tax-inclusive and tax-exclusive
   2889       real prices for mobile and sluggish endowments
   2890       - pefactreal(e,r)  --> tax-exclusive real factor prices
   2891       - pebfactreal(e,r) --> tax-inclusive real factor prices
   2892   >!
   2893   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,e,ENDWMS)(all,r,REG)
   2894       pebfactreal(e,r)
   2895       # ratio of (tax-inclusive) return to mobile and sluggish factor e in r #;
   2896   Coefficient (all,e,ENDWMS)(all,r,REG)
   2897       VENDWMS(e,r) # value of mobile and sluggish e in r at basic prices #;
   2898   Coefficient (all,e,ENDWMS)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2899       ENDWMSSHR(e,a,r) # share of mobile and sluggish e usage by act a in reg r #;
   2900   Zerodivide default 0.5;
   2901   Formula (all,e,ENDWMS)(all,r,REG)
   2902       VENDWMS(e,r) = sum{a,ACTS, EVFB(e,a,r)};
   2903   Formula (all,e,ENDWMS)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   2904       ENDWMSSHR(e,a,r) = EVFB(e,a,r) / VENDWMS(e,r);
   2905   Zerodivide off;
   2906   Equation E_pebfactreal
   2907   # defines the real (tax-inclusive) return to mobile and sluggish factor e in r #
   2908   (all,e,ENDWMS)(all,r,REG)
   2909       pebfactreal(e,r) = sum{a, ACTS, ENDWMSSHR(e,a,r) *  peb(e,a,r)} - ppriv(r);
   2910    
   2911   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,e,ENDWMS)(all,r,REG)
   2912       pefactreal(e,r)
   2913       # ratio of (tax-exclusive) return to mobile and sluggish factor e in r #;
   2914   Equation E_pefactreal
   2915   # defines the real (tax-exclusive) return to mobile and sluggish factor e in r #
   2916   (all,e,ENDWMS)(all,r,REG)
   2917       pefactreal(e,r) = pe(e,r) - ppriv(r);
   2918   !< End of GTAPv7 changes >!
   2919    
   2920   !<
   2921       B-2. Regional terms of trade (ToT)
   2922       ----------------------------------
   2923    
   2924       The next three equations correspond to Table 10 of Hertel and Tsigas on
   2925       Regional Terms of Trade.
   2926   >!
   2927    
   2928   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   2929       psw(r) # index of prices received for tradeables produced in region r #;
   2930   Equation E_psw
   2931   # estimate change in index of prices received for tradeables c produced in r #
   2932   (all,r,REG)
   2933       VXWREGION(r) * psw(r)
   2934           = sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d) * pfob(c,r,d)}}
   2935           + sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r) * pds(m,r)};
   2936   !<
   2937       This equation estimates the change in the index of prices received for
   2938       tradeable products produced in r.  (modified from HT 64 to eliminate the
   2939       investment component)
   2940   >!
   2941    
   2942   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   2943       pdw(r) # index of prices paid for tradeables used in importing region r #;
   2944   Equation E_pdw
   2945   # estimate change in index of prices paid for tradeable products used in r #
   2946   (all,r,REG)
   2947       VMWREGION(r) * pdw(r)
   2948           = sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,r) * pcif(c,s,r)}};
   2949   !<
   2950       This equation estimates the change in the index of prices paid for
   2951       tradeable products used in r.  (modified from HT 65 to eliminate saving)
   2952   >!
   2953    
   2954   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   2955       tot(r) # terms of trade for region r: tot(r) = psw(r) - pdw(r) #;
   2956   Equation E_tot
   2957   # terms of trade equation computed as difference in psw and pdw #
   2958   (all,r,REG)
   2959       tot(r) = psw(r) - pdw(r);
   2960    
   2961   !<
   2962       B-3. GDP indices (value, price and quantity)
   2963       --------------------------------------------
   2964   >!
   2965    
   2966   ! GDP expenditure side summary !
   2967   Set
   2968       GDPEX (Household,Investment,Government,Exports,IntnlMargins,Imports);
   2969   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,g,GDPEX)
   2970       GDPEXP(r,g) # GDP expenditure side summary #;
   2971   Formula
   2972   (all,r,REG) GDPEXP(r,"Household")    = sum{c,COMM, VPP(c,r)};
   2973   (all,r,REG) GDPEXP(r,"Investment")   = sum{c,COMM, VIP(c,r)};
   2974   (all,r,REG) GDPEXP(r,"Government")   = sum{c,COMM, VGP(c,r)};
   2975   (all,s,REG) GDPEXP(s,"Exports")      = sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,s,d)}};
   2976   (all,r,REG) GDPEXP(r,"IntnlMargins") = sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r)};
   2977   (all,d,REG) GDPEXP(d,"Imports")      = - sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,d)}};
   2978   Write
   2979       GDPEXP to file GTAPSUM header "GDPE";
   2980    
   2981   Variable (all,r,REG)
   2982       vgdp(r) # change in value of GDP #;
   2983   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   2984       GDP(r) # gross domestic product in region r #;
   2985   Formula (all,r,REG)
   2986       GDP(r) = sum{g,GDPEX, GDPEXP(r,g)};
   2987   !<
   2988       Gross Domestic Product in region r. Trade is valued at FOB and CIF prices.
   2989   >!
   2990    
   2991   Equation E_vgdp
   2992   # change in value of GDP #
   2993   (all,r,REG)
   2994       GDP(r) * vgdp(r)
   2995           = sum{c,COMM, VGP(c,r) * [qga(c,r) + pga(c,r)]}
   2996           + sum{c,COMM, VPP(c,r) * [qpa(c,r) + ppa(c,r)]}
   2997           + sum{c,COMM, VIP(c,r) * [qinv(r) + pinv(r)]}
   2998           + sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d) * [qxs(c,r,d) + pfob(c,r,d)]}}
   2999           + sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r) * [qst(m,r) + pds(m,r)]}
   3000           - sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,r) * [qxs(c,s,r) + pcif(c,s,r)]}};
   3001    
   3002   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3003       pgdp(r) # GDP price index #;
   3004   Variable (orig_level=GDP)(all,r,REG)
   3005       qgdp(r) # GDP quantity index #;
   3006    
   3007   Equation E_pgdp
   3008   # GDP price index #
   3009   (all,r,REG)
   3010       GDP(r) * pgdp(r)
   3011           = sum{c,COMM, VGP(c,r) * pga(c,r)}
   3012           + sum{c,COMM, VPP(c,r) * ppa(c,r)}
   3013           + sum{c,COMM, VIP(c,r) * pia(c,r)}
   3014           + sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d) * pfob(c,r,d)}}
   3015           + sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r) * pds(m,r)}
   3016           - sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,r) * pcif(c,s,r)}};
   3017    
   3018   Equation E_qgdp
   3019   # GDP quantity index #
   3020   (all,r,REG)
   3021       GDP(r) * qgdp(r)
   3022           = sum{c,COMM, VGP(c,r) * qga(c,r)}
   3023           + sum{c,COMM, VPP(c,r) * qpa(c,r)}
   3024           + sum{c,COMM, VIP(c,r) * qia(c,r)}
   3025           + sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d) * qxs(c,r,d)}}
   3026           + sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r) * qst(m,r)}
   3027           - sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,r) * qxs(c,s,r)}};
   3028    
   3029   !<
   3030       modified from HT 72 for use with AnalyseGE
   3031   >!
   3032   Variable (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3033       compvalad(a,r) # composition of value added for good c and region r #;
   3034    
   3035   Equation E_compvalad
   3036   # track change in composition of value added #
   3037   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3038       compvalad(a,r) = qo(a,r) - qgdp(r);
   3039    
   3040   !<
   3041       B-4. Aggregate trade indices (value, price and quantity)
   3042       --------------------------------------------------------
   3043   >!
   3044    
   3045   !<
   3046       Common variables and coefficients
   3047       Value indices for aggregate trade
   3048       Price indices for aggregate trade
   3049       Quantity indices for aggregate trade
   3050   >!
   3051    
   3052   !<
   3053       Common variables and coefficients
   3054       .................................
   3055    
   3056       only used in this aggregate trade indices section
   3057   >!
   3058    
   3059   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3060       pxw(c,r) # aggregate exports price index of c from region r #;
   3061   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)
   3062       VXWCOMMOD(c) # value of world exports by commodity c at FOB prices #;
   3063   Formula (all,c,COMM)
   3064       VXWCOMMOD(c) = sum{r,REG, VXW(c,r)};
   3065   Coefficient
   3066       VXWLD # value of commodity exports, FOB, globally #;
   3067   Formula
   3068       VXWLD = sum{r,REG, VXWREGION(r)};
   3069    
   3070   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)
   3071       VMWCOMMOD(c) # global value of commodity imports, CIF, by commodity #;
   3072   Formula (all,c,COMM)
   3073       VMWCOMMOD(c) = sum{r,REG, VMCIF(c,r)};
   3074    
   3075   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3076       VXDXSB(c,r) # basic value of com. c exports to all dest. (tradeables only) #;
   3077   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3078       VXDXSB(c,r) = sum{d,REG, VXSB(c,r,d)};
   3079    
   3080   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3081       PW_PM(c,r) # ratio of world to domestic prices #;
   3082   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3083       PW_PM(c,r) = VXDFOB(c,r) / VXDXSB(c,r);
   3084    
   3085   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3086       VOW(c,r) # value of commodity output in r at FOB incl transp. services #;
   3087   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3088       VOW(c,r) = VDB(c,r) * PW_PM(c,r) + VXDFOB(c,r) + IF[c in MARG, + VST(c,r)];
   3089    
   3090   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)
   3091       VWOW(c) # value of world supply at world prices for c #;
   3092   Formula (all,c,COMM)
   3093       VWOW(c) = sum{r,REG, VOW(c,r)};
   3094    
   3095   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)
   3096       VWOU(c) # value of world output of c at user prices #;
   3097   Formula (all,c,COMM)
   3098       VWOU(c) = sum{r,REG, [VPP(c,r) + VGP(c,r)] + sum{a,ACTS, VFP(c,a,r)}};
   3099    
   3100   !<
   3101       Value indices for aggregate trade
   3102       .................................
   3103   >!
   3104    
   3105   Equation E_vxwfob
   3106   # the change in FOB value of exports of m from r #
   3107   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3108       VXW(c,r) * vxwfob(c,r)
   3109           = sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d) * [qxs(c,r,d) + pfob(c,r,d)]}
   3110           + IF[c in MARG, VST(c,r) * [qst(c,r) + pds(c,r)]];
   3111    
   3112   Equation E_vxwreg
   3113   # computes % change in value of merchandise exports, by region #
   3114   (all,r,REG)
   3115       VXWREGION(r) * vxwreg(r) = sum{c,COMM, VXW(c,r) * vxwfob(c,r)};
   3116    
   3117   Variable (all,c,COMM)
   3118       vxwcom(c) # value of global merchandise exports by commodity #;
   3119   Equation E_vxwcom
   3120   # computes % change in FOB value of global exports, by commodity #
   3121   (all,c,COMM)
   3122       VXWCOMMOD(c) * vxwcom(c) = sum{r,REG, VXW(c,r) * vxwfob(c,r)};
   3123    
   3124   Variable
   3125       vxwwld # value of world trade #;
   3126   Equation E_vxwwld
   3127   # computes % change in value of global exports #
   3128       VXWLD * vxwwld = sum{r,REG, VXWREGION(r) * vxwreg(r)};
   3129    
   3130   Equation E_vmwcif
   3131   # the change in CIF value of imports of commodity c into r #
   3132   (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   3133       VMCIF(c,d) * vmwcif(c,d)
   3134           = sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,d) * [pcif(c,s,d) + qxs(c,s,d)]};
   3135    
   3136   Equation E_vmwreg
   3137   # computes % change in value of imports, CIF basis, by region #
   3138   (all,r,REG)
   3139       VMWREGION(r) * vmwreg(r) = sum{c,COMM, VMCIF(c,r) * vmwcif(c,r)};
   3140    
   3141   Variable (all,c,COMM)
   3142       vmwcom(c) # value of global merchandise imports c, at world prices #;
   3143   Equation E_vmwcom
   3144   # computes % change in value of global imports, by commodity #
   3145   (all,c,COMM)
   3146       VMWCOMMOD(c) * vmwcom(c) = sum{s,REG, VMCIF(c,s) * vmwcif(c,s)};
   3147    
   3148   Variable (all,c,COMM)
   3149       valuew(c) # value of world supply of good c #;
   3150   Equation E_valuew
   3151   # change in value of world output of comm. c at FOB prices #
   3152   (all,c,COMM)
   3153       VWOW(c) * valuew(c) = sum{r,REG, VOW(c,r) * [pxw(c,r) + qc(c,r)]};
   3154    
   3155   Variable (all,c,COMM)
   3156       valuewu(c) # value of world supply of good c at user prices #;
   3157   Equation E_valuewu
   3158   # change in value of world output of commodity c at user prices #
   3159   (all,c,COMM)
   3160       VWOU(c) * valuewu(c)
   3161           = sum{s,REG, VPP(c,s) * [ppa(c,s) + qpa(c,s)]
   3162           + VGP(c,s) * [pga(c,s) + qga(c,s)]
   3163           + sum{a,ACTS, VFP(c,a,s) * [pfa(c,a,s) + qfa(c,a,s)]}};
   3164    
   3165   !<
   3166       Price indices for aggregate trade
   3167       .................................
   3168   >!
   3169    
   3170   Equation E_pxw
   3171   # change in FOB price index of exports of m from r #
   3172   (all,C,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3173       VXW(c,r) * pxw(c,r)
   3174           = sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d) * pfob(c,r,d)}
   3175           + IF[c in MARG, VST(c,r) * pds(c,r)];
   3176    
   3177   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3178       pxwreg(r) # price index of merchandise exports, by region #;
   3179   Equation E_pxwreg
   3180   # computes % change in price index of exports, by region #
   3181   (all,r,REG)
   3182       VXWREGION(r) * pxwreg(r) = sum{c,COMM, VXW(c,r) * pxw(c,r)};
   3183    
   3184   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,c,COMM)
   3185       pxwcom(c) # price index of global merchandise exports by commodity #;
   3186   Equation E_pxwcom
   3187   # computes % change in price index of exports, by commodity #
   3188   (all,c,COMM)
   3189       VXWCOMMOD(c) * pxwcom(c) = sum{r,REG, VXW(c,r) * pxw(c,r)};
   3190    
   3191   Variable (orig_level=1.0)
   3192       pxwwld # price index of world trade #;
   3193   Equation E_pxwwld
   3194   # computes % change in price index of global exports #
   3195       VXWLD * pxwwld = sum{r,REG, VXWREGION(r) * pxwreg(r)};
   3196    
   3197   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3198       pmw(c,r) # world price of composite import c in region r #;
   3199   Equation E_pmw
   3200   # computes % change in CIF price index of imports of c into d #
   3201   (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   3202       VMCIF(c,d) * pmw(c,d) = sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,d) * pcif(c,s,d)};
   3203    
   3204   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,r,REG)
   3205       pmwreg(r) # price index of merchandise imports, by region #;
   3206   Equation E_pmwreg
   3207   # computes % change in price index of imports, by region #
   3208   (all,r,REG)
   3209       VMWREGION(r) * pmwreg(r) = sum{c,COMM, VMCIF(c,r) * pmw(c,r)};
   3210    
   3211   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,c,COMM)
   3212       pmwcom(c) # price index of global merchandise imports by commodity #;
   3213   Equation E_pmwcom
   3214   # computes % change in price index of imports, by commodity #
   3215   (all,c,COMM)
   3216       VMWCOMMOD(c) * pmwcom(c) = sum{r,REG, VMCIF(c,r) * pmw(c,r)};
   3217    
   3218   Variable (all,c,COMM)
   3219       pw(c) # world price index for total good c supplies #;
   3220   Equation E_pw
   3221   # change in index of world prices, FOB, for total production of c #
   3222   (all,c,COMM)
   3223       VWOW(c) * pw(c) = sum{r,REG, VOW(c,r) * pxw(c,r)};
   3224    
   3225   Variable (orig_level=1.0)(all,c,COMM)
   3226       pwu(c) # world price index for total good c supplies at user prices #;
   3227   Equation E_pwu
   3228   # change in index of user prices for deflating world production of c #
   3229   (all,c,COMM)
   3230       VWOU(c) * pwu(c)
   3231           = sum{s,REG, VPP(c,s) * ppa(c,s)
   3232           + VGP(c,s) * pga(c,s)
   3233           + VIP(c,s) * pinv(s)
   3234           + sum{a,ACTS, VFP(c,a,s) * pfa(c,a,s)}};
   3235    
   3236   !<
   3237       Quantity indices for aggregate trade
   3238       ....................................
   3239   >!
   3240    
   3241   Variable (orig_level=VXW)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3242       qxw(c,r) # aggregate exports of c from region r, FOB weights #;
   3243   Equation E_qxw
   3244   # change in volume of exports of (margin and non-margin) commodity c from r #
   3245   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3246       VXW(c,r) * qxw(c,r)
   3247           = sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d) * qxs(c,r,d)}
   3248           + IF[c in MARG, VST(c,r) * qst(c,r)];
   3249   !<
   3250       modified from HT 89 for use with AnalyseGE
   3251   >!
   3252    
   3253   Variable (orig_level=VXWREGION)(all,r,REG)
   3254       qxwreg(r) # volume of merchandise exports, by region #;
   3255   Equation E_qxwreg
   3256   # computes % change in quantity index of exports, by region #
   3257   (all,r,REG)
   3258       VXWREGION(r) * qxwreg(r) = sum{c,COMM, VXW(c,r) * qxw(c,r)};
   3259   !<
   3260       modified from HT 91 for use with AnalyseGE
   3261   >!
   3262    
   3263   Variable (orig_level=VXWCOMMOD)(all,c,COMM)
   3264       qxwcom(c) # volume of global merchandise exports by commodity #;
   3265   Equation E_qxwcom
   3266   # computes % change in quantity index of exports, by commodity #
   3267   (all,c,COMM)
   3268       VXWCOMMOD(c) * qxwcom(c) = sum{r,REG, VXW(c,r) * qxw(c,r)};
   3269   !<
   3270       modified from HT 93 for use with AnalyseGE
   3271   >!
   3272    
   3273   Variable (orig_level=VXWLD)
   3274       qxwwld # volume of world trade #;
   3275   Equation E_qxwwld
   3276   # computes % change in quantity index of global exports #
   3277       VXWLD * qxwwld = sum{r,REG, VXWREGION(r) * qxwreg(r)};
   3278   !<
   3279       modified from HT 95 for use with AnalyseGE
   3280   >!
   3281    
   3282   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   3283       qmw(c,d) # aggregate imports of c into region s, CIF weights #;
   3284   Equation E_qmw
   3285   # change in volume of imports of commodity c into d #
   3286   (all,c,COMM)(all,d,REG)
   3287       VMCIF(c,d) * qmw(c,d) = sum{s,REG, VCIF(c,s,d) * qxs(c,s,d)};
   3288   !<
   3289       modified from HT 90 for use with AnalyseGE
   3290   >!
   3291    
   3292   Variable (orig_level=VMWREGION)(all,r,REG)
   3293       qmwreg(r) # volume of merchandise imports, by region #;
   3294   Equation E_qmwreg
   3295   # computes % change in quantity index of imports, by region #
   3296   (all,s,REG)
   3297       VMWREGION(s) * qmwreg(s) = sum{c,COMM, VMCIF(c,s) * qmw(c,s)};
   3298   !<
   3299       modified from HT 92 for use with AnalyseGE
   3300   >!
   3301    
   3302   Variable (orig_level=VMWCOMMOD)(all,c,COMM)
   3303       qmwcom(c) # volume of global merchandise imports by commodity #;
   3304   Equation E_qmwcom
   3305   # computes % change in quantity index of imports, by commodity #
   3306   (all,c,COMM)
   3307       VMWCOMMOD(c) * qmwcom(c) = sum{s,REG, VMCIF(c,s) * qmw(c,s)};
   3308   !<
   3309       modified from HT 94 for use with AnalyseGE
   3310   >!
   3311    
   3312   Variable (all,c,COMM)
   3313       qow(c) # quantity index for world supply of good c #;
   3314   Equation E_qow
   3315   # change in index of world production of c #
   3316   (all,c,COMM)
   3317       VWOW(c) * qow(c) = sum{r,REG, VOW(c,r) * qc(c,r)};
   3318   !<
   3319       modified from HT 96 for use with AnalyseGE
   3320   >!
   3321    
   3322   Variable (orig_level=VWOU)(all,c,COMM)
   3323       qowu(c) # quantity index for world supply of good c at user prices #;
   3324   Equation E_qowu
   3325   # change in index of world production of c evaluated at user prices #
   3326   (all,c,COMM)
   3327       VWOU(c) * qowu(c)
   3328           = sum{s,REG, VPP(c,s) * qpa(c,s)
   3329           + VGP(c,s) * qga(c,s)
   3330           + VIP(c,s) * qia(c,s)
   3331           + sum{a,ACTS, VFP(c,a,s) * qfa(c,a,s)}};
   3332    
   3333   !<
   3334       B-5. Trade balance indices
   3335       --------------------------
   3336   >!
   3337    
   3338   Variable (change)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3339       del_tbalc(c,r) # change in trade balance by c and by r, $ US million #;
   3340   !<
   3341       A positive value indicates that the change in exports exceeds the change
   3342       in imports.
   3343   >!
   3344   Equation E_del_tbalc
   3345   # computes change in trade balance by commodity and by region #
   3346   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3347       del_tbalc(c,r)
   3348           = [VXW(c,r) / 100] * vxwfob(c,r) - [VMCIF(c,r) / 100] * vmwcif(c,r);
   3349    
   3350   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   3351       del_tbal(r) # change in trade balance X - M, $ US million #;
   3352   Equation E_del_tbal
   3353   # computes change in trade balance (X - M), by region #
   3354   (all,r,REG)
   3355       del_tbal(r)
   3356           = [VXWREGION(r) / 100] * vxwreg(r) - [VMWREGION(r) / 100] * vmwreg(r);
   3357    
   3358   !<
   3359       In order to maintain homogeneity in the presence of a fixed trade balance,
   3360       it is useful to have a nominal variable which this is measured against.
   3361       The next equation provides this, and we recommend users fix del_tbalry
   3362       instead of fixing del_tbal in future simulations.  The strategy is the same
   3363       one used above for taxes.
   3364   >!
   3365    
   3366   Variable
   3367       ywld # world income #;
   3368   Coefficient
   3369       INCOMEWLD # World income #;
   3370   Formula
   3371       INCOMEWLD = sum{r,REG, INCOME(r)};
   3372    
   3373   Equation E_ywld
   3374   # world income #
   3375       INCOMEWLD * ywld = sum{r,REG, INCOME(r) * y(r)};
   3376    
   3377   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   3378       del_tbalry(r) # change in trade bal. of r as a percentage of world income #;
   3379   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3380       TBAL(r) # trade balance for region r #;
   3381   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3382       TBAL(r) = VXWREGION(r) - VMWREGION(r);
   3383    
   3384   Equation E_del_tbalry
   3385   # change in trade balance of region r as a percentage of world income #
   3386   (all,r,REG)
   3387       INCOMEWLD * del_tbalry(r)
   3388           = VXWREGION(r) * vxwreg(r) - VMWREGION(r) * vmwreg(r)
   3389           - TBAL(r) * ywld;
   3390    
   3391   !<
   3392       B-6. Terms of trade (ToT) decomposition
   3393       ---------------------------------------
   3394       Computations for decomposition the terms-of-trade effect
   3395       Reference: Robert McDougall, SALTER No. 12 Working Paper
   3396   >!
   3397    
   3398   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3399       SX_CR(c,r) # share of good c in total exports from r #;
   3400   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   3401       SX_CR(m,r)
   3402           = [sum{d,REG, VFOB(m,r,d)} + VST(m,r)]
   3403           / [sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d)}}
   3404               + sum{k,MARG, VST(k,r)}];
   3405   Formula (all,n,NMRG)(all,r,REG)
   3406       SX_CR(n,r)
   3407           = sum{d,REG, VFOB(n,r,d)}
   3408           / [sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, VFOB(c,r,d)}}
   3409               + sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r)}];
   3410    
   3411   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)(all,s,REG)
   3412       VTMCOMM(m,s) # margin usage of m in getting imports to region s #;
   3413   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,s,REG)
   3414       VTMCOMM(m,s) = sum{c,COMM, sum{r,REG, VTMFSD(m,c,r,s)}};
   3415    
   3416   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3417       VMWDCRALL(c,s) # imports of c into s, with direct allocation of margins #;
   3418   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3419       VMWDCRALL(c,s) = sum{r,REG, VFOB(c,r,s)} + IF[c in MARG, VTMCOMM(c,s)];
   3420    
   3421   Coefficient (all,s,REG)
   3422       VMWDATOT(s) # total imports into s, calculated on direct allocation basis #;
   3423   Formula (all,s,REG)
   3424       VMWDATOT(s) = sum{c,COMM, VMWDCRALL(c,s)};
   3425    
   3426   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3427       SM_CR(c,r)  # share of good c in total imports into r #;
   3428   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3429       SM_CR(c,s) = VMWDCRALL(c,s) / VMWDATOT(s);
   3430    
   3431   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   3432       SM_CRS(c,r,s) # share of imports of good c into s from r at FOB prices #;
   3433   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   3434       SM_CRS(c,r,s) = VFOB(c,r,s) / VMWDCRALL(c,s);
   3435    
   3436   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   3437       SMT_CR(m,r) # share of transport cost in imports of margin commodity #;
   3438   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,s,REG)
   3439       SMT_CR(m,s) = VTMCOMM(m,s) / VMWDCRALL(m,s);
   3440    
   3441   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3442       pm_cr(c,r) # imports price index for good c and region r #;
   3443   Equation E_pm_cr
   3444   # price index for total imports of m in s -- margins commodities #
   3445   (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)
   3446       pm_cr(c,s)
   3447           = sum{r,REG, SM_CRS(c,r,s) * pfob(c,r,s)}
   3448           + IF[c in MARG, SMT_CR(c,s) * pt(c)];
   3449    
   3450   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3451       c1_cr(c,r) # contribution of world price, px_c, to ToT #;
   3452   Equation E_c1_cr
   3453   # contribution of world export price index of good c to ToT for region r #
   3454   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3455       c1_cr(c,r) = [SX_CR(c,r) - SM_CR(c,r)] * [pxwcom(c) - pxwwld];
   3456    
   3457   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3458       c2_cr(c,r) # contribution of regional export price, px_cr, to ToT #;
   3459   Equation E_c2_cr
   3460   # contribution of regional export price of good c for region r #
   3461   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3462       c2_cr(c,r) = SX_CR(c,r) * [pxw(c,r) - pxwcom(c)];
   3463    
   3464   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3465       c3_cr(c,r) # contribution of regional import price, pm_cr, to ToT #;
   3466   Equation E_c3_cr
   3467   # contribution of imports price index of good c for region r #
   3468   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3469       c3_cr(c,r) = SM_CR(c,r) * [pm_cr(c,r) - pxwcom(c)];
   3470    
   3471   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3472       c1_r(r) # contribution of world prices for all goods to ToT #;
   3473   Equation E_c1_r
   3474   # contribution of world price indexes of all goods to ToT for r #
   3475   (all,r,REG)
   3476       c1_r(r) = sum{c,COMM, c1_cr(c,r)};
   3477    
   3478   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3479       c2_r(r) # contribution of regional export prices to ToT #;
   3480   Equation E_c2_r
   3481   # contribution of regional exports prices to ToT for r #
   3482   (all,r,REG)
   3483       c2_r(r) = sum{c,COMM, c2_cr(c,r)};
   3484    
   3485   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3486       c3_r(r) # contribution of regional import prices to ToT #;
   3487   Equation E_c3_r
   3488   # contribution of regional import prices to ToT for r #
   3489   (all,r,REG)
   3490       c3_r(r) = sum{c,COMM, c3_cr(c,r)};
   3491    
   3492   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3493       tot2(r) # trade terms for region r, computed from components #;
   3494   Equation E_tot2
   3495   # trade terms for region r, computed from components #
   3496   (all,r,REG)
   3497       tot2(r) = c1_r(r) + c2_r(r) - c3_r(r);
   3498    
   3499   !<
   3500       --------------------------------------------
   3501       11. Measurement and decomposition of welfare
   3502       --------------------------------------------
   3503    
   3504       11-0. Variables and coefficients
   3505       11-1. Government consumption shadow demand system
   3506       11-2. Private consumption shadow demand dystem
   3507       11-3. Regional Household shadow demand system
   3508       11-4. Equivalent Variation
   3509       11-5. Decomposition of welfare [Section 3.11 in JGEA paper]
   3510    
   3511       This section calculates equivalent variation "EV" and world equivalent
   3512       variation, "WEV", by determining the income "yev" that would be required
   3513       to achieve the current actual utility level "u" in a shadow demand system
   3514       in which prices are fixed.
   3515    
   3516       Section 11-2 calculates the utility elasticity of private consumption
   3517       expenditure, "ueprivev", within a shadow demand system for private
   3518       consumption, for use in section 11-3. Section 11-3 calculates private
   3519       consumption expenditure "ypev" for use in 11-2, and regional income "yev"
   3520       for use in 11-4, within a shadow demand system for the regional household.
   3521       Section 11-4 calculates "EV" and "WEV".
   3522    
   3523       Section 11-5 provides a decomposition welfare in the model as explained
   3524       in the GTAP model paper.
   3525   >!
   3526    
   3527   !<
   3528       11-0. Variables and coefficients
   3529       --------------------------------
   3530       only used in this Equivalent Variation section of the summary indices
   3531       appendix
   3532   >!
   3533    
   3534   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3535       uelasev(r) # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility, for EV calc. #;
   3536   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3537       ueprivev(r) # utility elast. of private consn expenditure, for EV calc. #;
   3538   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3539       ugev(r) # per capita utility from gov't expend., for EV calc. #;
   3540   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3541       upev(r) # per capita utility from private expend., for EV calc. #;
   3542   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3543       qsaveev(r) # total quantity of saving demanded, for EV calc. #;
   3544   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3545       yev(r) # regional household income in region r, for EV calc. #;
   3546   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3547       ypev(r) # private consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   3548   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3549       ygev(r) # government consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   3550    
   3551   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3552       INCOMEEV(r) # regional income, for EV calc. #;
   3553   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   3554       INCOMEEV(r) = INCOME(r);
   3555   Update (all,r,REG)
   3556       INCOMEEV(r) = yev(r);
   3557    
   3558   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3559       UTILPRIVEV(r) # utility from private consumption, for EV calcs #;
   3560   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   3561       UTILPRIVEV(r) = UTILPRIV(r);
   3562   Update (all,r,REG)
   3563       UTILPRIVEV(r) = upev(r);
   3564    
   3565   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3566       UTILGOVEV(r) # utility from private consumption, for EV calcs #;
   3567   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   3568       UTILGOVEV(r) = UTILGOV(r);
   3569   Update (all,r,REG)
   3570       UTILGOVEV(r) = ugev(r);
   3571    
   3572   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3573       UTILSAVEEV(r) # utility from private consumption, for EV calcs #;
   3574   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   3575       UTILSAVEEV(r) = UTILSAVE(r);
   3576   Update (change) (all,r,REG)
   3577       UTILSAVEEV(r) = [[qsaveev(r) - pop(r)] / 100] * UTILSAVEEV(r);
   3578    
   3579   !<
   3580       11-1. Government consumption shadow demand system
   3581       -------------------------------------------------
   3582   >!
   3583    
   3584   Equation E_ugev
   3585   # utility from government consumption in r #
   3586   (all,r,REG)
   3587       ygev(r) - pop(r) = ugev(r);
   3588    
   3589   !<
   3590       11-2. Private consumption shadow demand system
   3591       ----------------------------------------------
   3592   >!
   3593    
   3594   Variable (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3595       qpev(c,r)
   3596       # private hhld demand for commodity c in region r, for EV calc. #;
   3597    
   3598   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3599       VPPEV(c,r)
   3600       # private hhld expend. on c in r valued at purch. prices, for EV calc. #;
   3601   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3602       VPPEV(c,r) = VPP(c,r);
   3603   Update (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3604       VPPEV(c,r) = qpev(c,r);
   3605    
   3606   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3607       VPPREGEV(r) # private consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   3608   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3609       VPPREGEV(r) = sum{c,COMM, VPPEV(c,r)};
   3610   !<
   3611       VPPREGEV should agree with PRIVEXPEV.
   3612   >!
   3613    
   3614   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3615       CONSHREV(c,r)
   3616       # share of private hhld consn devoted to good c in r, for EV calc. #;
   3617   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3618       CONSHREV(c,r) = VPPEV(c,r) / VPPREGEV(r);
   3619   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3620       EYEV(c,r)
   3621       # expend. elast. of private hhld demand for c in r, for EV calc. #;
   3622   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3623       EYEV(c,r)
   3624           = [1.0 / sum{n,COMM, CONSHREV(n,r) * INCPAR(n,r)}]
   3625           * [INCPAR(c,r) * [1.0 - ALPHA(c,r)]
   3626               + sum{n,COMM, CONSHREV(n,r) * INCPAR(n,r) * ALPHA(n,r)}]
   3627           + ALPHA(c,r)
   3628           - sum{n,COMM, CONSHREV(n,r) * ALPHA(n,r)};
   3629    
   3630   Equation E_qpev
   3631       # private hhld demands for composite commodities, for EV calc. #
   3632       (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3633       qpev(c,r) - pop(r) = EYEV(c,r) * [ypev(r) - pop(r)];
   3634   !<
   3635       Prices are held constant for the EV calculation and so do not appear here.
   3636   >!
   3637    
   3638   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3639       UELASPRIVEV(r)
   3640       # elast. of cost wrt utility from private consn, for EV calc. #;
   3641   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3642       UELASPRIVEV(r) = sum{c,COMM, CONSHREV(c,r) * INCPAR(c,r)};
   3643    
   3644   Equation E_upev
   3645   # computation of utility from private consumption in r #
   3646   (all,r,REG)
   3647       ypev(r) - pop(r) = UELASPRIVEV(r) * upev(r);
   3648    
   3649   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3650       XWCONSHREV(c,r)
   3651       # expansion-parameter-weighted consumption share, for EV calc. #;
   3652   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   3653       XWCONSHREV(c,r) = CONSHREV(c,r) * INCPAR(c,r) / UELASPRIVEV(r);
   3654    
   3655   Equation E_ueprivev
   3656       # elasticity of cost wrt utility from private consn, for EV calc. #
   3657       (all,r,REG)
   3658       ueprivev(r)
   3659           = sum{c,COMM, XWCONSHREV(c,r) * [qpev(c,r) - ypev(r)]};
   3660   !<
   3661       Prices are held constant for the EV calculation and so do not appear here.
   3662   >!
   3663    
   3664   !<
   3665    
   3666       11-3. Regional Household shadow demand system
   3667       ---------------------------------------------
   3668   >!
   3669    
   3670   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3671       ysaveev(r) # NET saving expenditure, for EV calc. #;
   3672    
   3673   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3674       PRIVEXPEV(r)
   3675       # private consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   3676   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   3677       PRIVEXPEV(r) = PRIVEXP(r);
   3678   Update (all,r,REG)
   3679       PRIVEXPEV(r) = ypev(r);
   3680   !<
   3681       PRIVEXPEV should agree with VPPREGEV.
   3682   >!
   3683    
   3684   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3685       GOVEXPEV(r)
   3686       # government consumption expenditure in region r, for EV calc. #;
   3687   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   3688       GOVEXPEV(r) = GOVEXP(r);
   3689   Update (all,r,REG)
   3690       GOVEXPEV(r) = ygev(r);
   3691    
   3692   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3693       SAVEEV(r)
   3694       # saving in region r, for EV calc. #;
   3695   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   3696       SAVEEV(r) = SAVE(r);
   3697   Update (all,r,REG)
   3698       SAVEEV(r) = ysaveev(r);
   3699    
   3700   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3701       XSHRPRIVEV(r)
   3702       # private expenditure share in regional income, for EV calc. #;
   3703   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3704       XSHRPRIVEV(r) = PRIVEXPEV(r) / INCOMEEV(r);
   3705    
   3706   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3707       XSHRGOVEV(r)
   3708       # government expenditure share in regional income, for EV calc. #;
   3709   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3710       XSHRGOVEV(r) = GOVEXPEV(r) / INCOMEEV(r);
   3711    
   3712   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3713       XSHRSAVEEV(r) # saving share in regional income, for EV calc. #;
   3714   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3715       XSHRSAVEEV(r) = SAVEEV(r) / INCOMEEV(r);
   3716    
   3717   Variable (all,r,REG)
   3718       dpavev(r) # average distribution parameter shift, for EV calc. #;
   3719   Equation E_dpavev
   3720   # average distribution parameter shift, for EV calc. #
   3721       (all,r,REG)
   3722       dpavev(r)
   3723           = XSHRPRIVEV(r) * dppriv(r)
   3724           + XSHRGOVEV(r) * dpgov(r)
   3725           + XSHRSAVEEV(r) * dpsave(r);
   3726    
   3727   Equation E_uelasev
   3728       # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility, for EV calc. #
   3729       (all,r,REG)
   3730       uelasev(r) = XSHRPRIV(r) * ueprivev(r) - dpavev(r);
   3731    
   3732   Equation E_ypev
   3733   # private consumption expenditure, for EV calc. #
   3734       (all,r,REG)
   3735       ypev(r) - yev(r) = -[ueprivev(r) - uelasev(r)] + dppriv(r);
   3736    
   3737   Equation E_ygev
   3738   # government consumption expenditure #
   3739   (all,r,REG)
   3740       ygev(r) - yev(r) = uelasev(r) + dpgov(r);
   3741    
   3742   Equation E_ysaveev
   3743   # saving #
   3744   (all,r,REG)
   3745       ysaveev(r) - yev(r) = uelasev(r) + dpsave(r);
   3746    
   3747   Equation E_qsaveev
   3748   # saving #
   3749   (all,r,REG)
   3750       qsaveev(r) = ysaveev(r);
   3751   !<
   3752       Note that because psave doesn't change, qsaveev moves with ysaveev.
   3753   >!
   3754    
   3755   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3756       UTILELASEV(r)
   3757       # elasticity of cost of utility wrt utility, for EV calc. #;
   3758   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   3759       UTILELASEV(r) = UTILELAS(r);
   3760   Update (all,r,REG)
   3761       UTILELASEV(r) = uelasev(r);
   3762    
   3763   Equation E_yev
   3764   # equivalent income #
   3765   (all,r,REG)
   3766       u(r)
   3767           = au(r)
   3768           + DPARPRIV(r) * loge(UTILPRIVEV(r)) * dppriv(r)
   3769           + DPARGOV(r) * loge(UTILGOVEV(r)) * dpgov(r)
   3770           + DPARSAVE(r) * loge(UTILSAVEEV(r)) * dpsave(r)
   3771           + [1.0 / UTILELASEV(r)] * [yev(r) - pop(r)];
   3772    
   3773   !<
   3774       11-4. Equivalent Variation
   3775       --------------------------
   3776   >!
   3777    
   3778   Variable (change)(all,r,REG)
   3779       EV(r) # equivalent variation, $ US million #;
   3780   Equation E_EV
   3781   # regional EV #
   3782   (all,r,REG)
   3783       EV(r) = [INCOMEEV(r) / 100] * yev(r);
   3784    
   3785   Variable (change)
   3786       WEV # equivalent variation for the world #;
   3787   Equation E_WEV
   3788   # EV for the world #
   3789       WEV = sum{r,REG, EV(r)};
   3790    
   3791   !<
   3792       11-5. Welfare decomposition
   3793       ---------------------------
   3794       See GTAP Technical Paper No. 5 for derivation and interpretation.
   3795       See also "The Standard GTAP Model (Version 7)" paper.
   3796   >!
   3797    
   3798   !<
   3799       Declare new sets for Welfare decomposition and for use in DECOMP.TAB.
   3800       Supplementary sets for "toggles" in VIEWHAR.
   3801   >!
   3802   Set
   3803       DIR(domestic,imported);
   3804   Set
   3805       CTAX(prodtax,pfacttax,inctax,inputtax,contax,invtax,govtax,xtax,mtax);
   3806   Set
   3807       TECHTYPE(output,primfac,v_added,ininput,invest,transp,import);
   3808   Set
   3809       COLUMN(alloc_A1,ENDWB1,tech_C1,pop_D1,tot_E1,IS_F1,pref_G1);
   3810    
   3811   Coefficient (all,r,REG)
   3812       EVSCALFACT(r) # equivalent variation scaling factor #;
   3813   Formula (all,r,REG)
   3814       EVSCALFACT(r) = [UTILELASEV(r) / UTILELAS(r)] * [INCOMEEV(r) / INCOME(r)];
   3815    
   3816   Coefficient (all,m,MARG)(all,s,REG)
   3817       VTMD(m,s) # aggregate value of svce m in shipments to s #;
   3818   Formula (all,m,MARG)(all,s,REG)
   3819       VTMD(m,s) = sum{c,COMM, sum{r,REG, VTMFSD(m,c,r,s)}};
   3820    
   3821   Variable (linear,change)(all,r,REG)
   3822       EV_ALT(r) # regional EV computed in alternative way #;
   3823   Equation E_EV_ALT
   3824   # decomposition of Equivalent Variation #
   3825   (all,r,REG)
   3826       EV_ALT(r)
   3827           !< Preference shifts >!
   3828           = -[0.01 * UTILELASEV(r) * INCOMEEV(r)]
   3829           * [DPARPRIV(r) * loge(UTILPRIVEV(r) / UTILPRIV(r)) * dppriv(r)
   3830               + DPARGOV(r) * loge(UTILGOVEV(r) / UTILGOV(r)) * dpgov(r)
   3831               + DPARSAVE(r) * loge(UTILSAVEEV(r) / UTILSAVE(r)) * dpsave(r)]
   3832           !< Scaling factor >!
   3833           + [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3834           !< Changes in allocative efficiency >!
   3835           * [sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS, PTAX(c,a,r) * [qca(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}}
   3836               + sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS,
   3837                   INCTAX(e,a,r) * [qes(e,a,r) - pop(r)]}}
   3838               + sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS,
   3839                   ETAX(e,a,r) * [qfe(e,a,r) - pop(r)]}}
   3840               + sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   3841                   MFTAX(c,a,r) * [qfm(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}}
   3842               + sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   3843                   DFTAX(c,a,r) * [qfd(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}}
   3844               + sum{c,COMM, MPTAX(c,r) * [qpm(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   3845               + sum{c,COMM, DPTAX(c,r) * [qpd(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   3846               + sum{c,COMM, MGTAX(c,r) * [qgm(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   3847               + sum{c,COMM, DGTAX(c,r) * [qgd(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   3848               + sum{c,COMM, MITAX(c,r) * [qim(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   3849               + sum{c,COMM, DITAX(c,r) * [qid(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   3850               + sum{c,COMM, sum{d,REG, XTAXD(c,r,d) * [qxs(c,r,d) - pop(r)]}}
   3851               + sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, MTAX(c,s,r) * [qxs(c,s,r) - pop(r)]}}
   3852           !< Changes in endowments >!
   3853           + sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, EVOS(e,a,r) * [qes(e,a,r) - pop(r)]}}
   3854               !< Depreciation >!
   3855           - VDEP(r) * [kb(r) - pop(r)]
   3856           !< Changes in technology >!
   3857           + sum{a,ACTS, VOS(a,r) * ao(a,r)}
   3858               + sum{a,ACTS, VVA(a,r) * ava(a,r)}
   3859               + sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS, VFP(c,a,r) * aint(a,r)}}
   3860               + sum{a,ACTS, sum{e,ENDW, VFP(e,a,r) * afe(e,a,r)}}
   3861               + sum{a,ACTS, sum{c,COMM, VFP(c,a,r) * afa(c,a,r)}}
   3862               + sum{m,MARG, sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG,
   3863                   VTMFSD(m,c,s,r) * atmfsd(m,c,s,r)}}}
   3864               + sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VMSB(c,s,r) * ams(c,s,r)}}
   3865           !< Changes in terms of trade >!
   3866           + sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VFOB(c,r,s) * pfob(c,r,s)}}
   3867               + sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r) * pds(m,r)}
   3868               + NETINV(r) * pinv(r)
   3869               - sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VFOB(c,s,r) * pfob(c,s,r)}}
   3870               - sum{m,MARG, VTMD(m,r) * pt(m)}
   3871               - SAVE(r) * psave(r)]
   3872           !< Changes in population >!
   3873           + 0.01 * INCOMEEV(r) * pop(r);
   3874    
   3875   Variable (linear,change)
   3876       WEV_ALT # expression for WEV computed in alternative way #;
   3877   Equation E_WEV_ALT
   3878   # Equivalent Variation for the world #
   3879       WEV_ALT = sum{r,REG, EV_ALT(r)};
   3880    
   3881   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   3882       CNTdpar(r) # contribution to EV of change in distribution parameters #;
   3883   Equation E_CNTdpar
   3884   # contribution to EV of change in distribution parameters #
   3885   (all,r,REG)
   3886       CNTdpar(r)
   3887           = -0.01 * UTILELASEV(r) * INCOMEEV(r)
   3888           * [DPARPRIV(r) * loge(UTILPRIVEV(r) / UTILPRIV(r)) * dppriv(r)
   3889               + DPARGOV(r) * loge(UTILGOVEV(r) / UTILGOV(r)) * dpgov(r)
   3890               + DPARSAVE(r) * loge(UTILSAVEEV(r) / UTILSAVE(r)) * dpsave(r)];
   3891    
   3892   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   3893       CNTpop(r) # contribution to EV in region r of change in population #;
   3894   Equation E_CNTpop
   3895   # contribution to EV in region r of change in population #
   3896   (all,r,REG)
   3897       CNTpop(r) = 0.01 * INCOMEEV(r) * pop(r);
   3898    
   3899   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   3900       CNTqor(r) # contribution to EV in region r of output changes #;
   3901   Equation E_CNTqor
   3902   # contribution to EV in region r of output changes #
   3903   (all,r,REG)
   3904       CNTqor(r) = 0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)
   3905                 * sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS, PTAX(c,a,r) * [qca(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}};
   3906    
   3907   Variable (linear,change) (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3908       CNTqo(a,r)
   3909       # contribution to EV of changes in industry output of act. a in region r #;
   3910   Equation E_CNTqo
   3911   # contribution to EV of changes in industry output of act. a in region r #
   3912   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3913       CNTqo(a,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3914                    * sum{c,COMM, PTAX(c,a,r) * [qca(c,a,r) - pop(r)]};
   3915    
   3916   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3917       CNTqca(c,a,r)
   3918       # contribution to EV of changes in output c of act. a in region r #;
   3919   Equation E_CNTqca
   3920   # contribution to EV of changes in industry output of act. a in region r #
   3921   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3922       CNTqca(c,a,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3923                       * PTAX(c,a,r) * [qca(c,a,r) - pop(r)];
   3924    
   3925   Variable (linear,change) (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   3926       CNTqe(e,r)
   3927       # contribution to EV of changes in supply of ENDW e in reg. r #;
   3928   Equation E_CNTqe
   3929   # contribution to EV of changes in supply of ENDW e in reg. r #
   3930   (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   3931       CNTqe(e,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3932                  * sum{a,ACTS, [EVFB(e,a,r) - EVOS(e,a,r)]
   3933                                 * [qes(e,a,r) - pop(r)]};
   3934    
   3935   Variable (linear,change) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3936       CNTqea(e,a,r)
   3937       # contribution to EV of changes in supply of ENDW e to act. a in reg. r #;
   3938   Equation E_CNTqea
   3939   # contribution to EV of changes in supply of ENDW e in reg. r #
   3940   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3941       CNTqea(e,a,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3942                     * [EVFB(e,a,r) - EVOS(e,a,r)] * [qes(e,a,r) - pop(r)];
   3943    
   3944   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   3945       CNTqfer(r)
   3946       # contribution to EV of changes in use of all ENDW in r #;
   3947   Equation E_CNTqfer
   3948   # contribution to EV of changes in use of all ENDW in r #
   3949   (all,r,REG)
   3950       CNTqfer(r)
   3951           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3952           * sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, ETAX(e,a,r) *  [qfe(e,a,r) - pop(r)]}};
   3953    
   3954   Variable (linear,change) (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   3955       CNTqfeer(e,r)
   3956       # contribution to EV of changes in use of ENDW e in all firms in r #;
   3957   Equation E_CNTqfeer
   3958   # contribution to EV of changes in use of ENDW e in all firms in r #
   3959   (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   3960       CNTqfeer(e,r)
   3961           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3962           * sum{a,ACTS, ETAX(e,a,r) *  [qfe(e,a,r) - pop(r)]};
   3963    
   3964   Variable (linear,change) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3965       CNTqfe(e,a,r)
   3966       # contribution to EV of changes in use of ENDW e in a in r #;
   3967   Equation E_CNTqfe
   3968   # contribution to EV of changes in use of ENDW e in a in r #
   3969   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3970       CNTqfe(e,a,r)
   3971           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * ETAX(e,a,r) * [qfe(e,a,r) - pop(r)];
   3972    
   3973   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   3974       CNTqfr(r,d)
   3975       # cont. to EV of changes in use of dom. and imp. intermediates in r #;
   3976   Equation E_CNTqfr
   3977   # cont. to EV of changes in use of dom. and imp. intermediates in r #
   3978   (all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   3979       CNTqfr(r,d)
   3980           = IF[d="domestic", [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3981               * sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS, DFTAX(c,a,r) *  [qfd(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}}]
   3982           + IF[d="imported", [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   3983               * sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS, MFTAX(c,a,r) *  [qfm(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}}];
   3984    
   3985   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3986       CNTqfm(c,a,r)
   3987       # cont. to EV of changes in use of imported intermediates by a in r #;
   3988   Equation E_CNTqfm
   3989   # cont. to EV of changes in use of imported intermediates in r #
   3990   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3991       CNTqfm(c,a,r)
   3992           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * MFTAX(c,a,r) * [qfm(c,a,r) - pop(r)];
   3993    
   3994   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   3995       CNTqfd(c,a,r)
   3996       # cont. to EV of changes in use of domestic intermediates by a in r #;
   3997   Equation E_CNTqfd
   3998   # cont. to EV of changes in use of domestic intermediates by a in r #
   3999   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4000       CNTqfd(c,a,r)
   4001           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * DFTAX(c,a,r) * [qfd(c,a,r) - pop(r)];
   4002    
   4003   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4004       CNTqpm(c,r)
   4005       # contribution to EV of changes in consumption of imported good c in r #;
   4006   Equation E_CNTqpm
   4007   # contribution to EV of changes in consumption of imported good c in r #
   4008   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4009       CNTqpm(c,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * MPTAX(c,r) * [qpm(c,r) - pop(r)];
   4010    
   4011   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4012       CNTqpd(c,r)
   4013       # contribution to EV of changes in consumption of domestic good c in r #;
   4014   Equation E_CNTqpd
   4015   # contribution to EV of changes in consumption of domestic good c in r #
   4016   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4017       CNTqpd(c,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * DPTAX(c,r) * [qpd(c,r) - pop(r)];
   4018    
   4019   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4020       CNTqpr(r,d)
   4021       # cont. to EV of changes in consumption of dom. and imp. goods in r #;
   4022   Equation E_CNTqpr
   4023   # cont. to EV of changes in consumption of dom. and imp. goods in r #
   4024   (all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4025       CNTqpr(r,d)
   4026           = IF[d="domestic", [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4027                              * sum{c,COMM, DPTAX(c,r) *  [qpd(c,r) - pop(r)]}]
   4028           + IF[d="imported", [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4029                              * sum{c,COMM, MPTAX(c,r) * [qpm(c,r) - pop(r)]}];
   4030    
   4031   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4032       CNTqia(r,d)
   4033       # contribution to EV of changes in dom. and imp. investment goods in r #;
   4034   Equation E_CNTqia
   4035   # contribution to EV of changes in dom. and imp. investment goods in r #
   4036   (all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4037       CNTqia(r,d)
   4038           = IF[d="domestic", sum{c,COMM,
   4039                   DITAX(c,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qid(c,r) - pop(r)]}]
   4040           + IF[d="imported", sum{c,COMM,
   4041                   MITAX(c,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qim(c,r) - pop(r)]}];
   4042    
   4043   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4044       CNTqim(c,r)
   4045       # contribution to EV of changes in imported investment good c in r #;
   4046   Equation E_CNTqim
   4047   # contribution to EV of changes in imported investment good c in r #
   4048   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4049       CNTqim(c,r) = MITAX(c,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qim(c,r) - pop(r)];
   4050    
   4051   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4052       CNTqid(c,r)
   4053       # contribution. to EV of changes in domestic investment good c in r #;
   4054   Equation E_CNTqid
   4055   # contribution. to EV of changes in domestic investment good c in r #
   4056   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4057       CNTqid(c,r) = DITAX(c,r) * [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [qid(c,r) - pop(r)];
   4058    
   4059   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4060       CNTqgr(r,d)
   4061       # cont. to EV of changes in gov't consumption of dom. and imp goods in r #;
   4062   Equation E_CNTqgr
   4063   # cont. to EV of changes in gov't consumption of dom. and imp goods in r #
   4064   (all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4065       CNTqgr(r,d)
   4066           = IF[d="domestic", [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4067                               * sum{c,COMM, DGTAX(c,r) * [qgd(c,r) - pop(r)]}]
   4068           + IF[d="imported", [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4069                               * sum{c,COMM, MGTAX(c,r) * [qgm(c,r) - pop(r)]}];
   4070    
   4071   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4072       CNTqgm(c,r)
   4073       # contribution to EV of changes in gov't consumption of import c in r #;
   4074   Equation E_CNTqgm
   4075   # contribution to EV of changes in gov't consumption of import c in r #
   4076   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4077       CNTqgm(c,r) =  [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * MGTAX(c,r) * [qgm(c,r) - pop(r)];
   4078    
   4079   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4080       CNTqgd(c,r)
   4081       # contribution to EV of changes in gov't consumption of domestic c in r #;
   4082   Equation E_CNTqgd
   4083   # contribution to EV of changes in gov't consumption of domestic c in r #
   4084   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4085       CNTqgd(c,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * DGTAX(c,r) * [qgd(c,r) - pop(r)];
   4086    
   4087   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4088       CNTqxsr(r)
   4089       # cont. to EV of changes in exports of all goods from SRCE r to all DEST #;
   4090   Equation E_CNTqxsr
   4091   # cont. to EV of changes in exports of all goods from SRCE r to all DEST #
   4092   (all,r,REG)
   4093       CNTqxsr(r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4094                  * sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, XTAXD(c,r,s) * [qxs(c,r,s) - pop(r)]}};
   4095    
   4096   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4097       CNTqxs(c,s,d)
   4098       # contribution to EV of changes in exports of c from SRCE s to DEST d #;
   4099   Equation E_CNTqxs
   4100   # contribution to EV of changes in exports of c from SRCE s to DEST d #
   4101   (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4102       CNTqxs(c,s,d) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(s)]
   4103                      * XTAXD(c,s,d) *  [qxs(c,s,d) - pop(s)];
   4104    
   4105   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4106       CNTqmsr(r)
   4107       # cont. to EV of changes in imports of all goods from all SRCE to DEST r #;
   4108   Equation E_CNTqmsr
   4109   # cont. to EV of changes in imports of all goods from all SRCE to DEST d #
   4110   (all,d,REG)
   4111       CNTqmsr(d) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(d)]
   4112                  * sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, MTAX(c,s,d) *  [qxs(c,s,d) - pop(d)]}};
   4113    
   4114   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4115       CNTqms(c,s,d)
   4116       # contribution to EV of changes in imports of c from SRCE s to DEST d #;
   4117   Equation E_CNTqms
   4118   # contribution to EV of changes in imports of c from SRCE s to DEST d #
   4119   (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4120       CNTqms(c,s,d) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(d)]
   4121                     * MTAX(c,s,d) * [qxs(c,s,d) - pop(d)];
   4122    
   4123   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)(all,t,CTAX)
   4124       CNTalleffr(r,t) # total contribution to regional EV of allocative effects #;
   4125   Equation E_CNTalleffr
   4126   # total contribution to regional EV of allocative effects #
   4127   (all,r,REG)(all,t,CTAX)
   4128       CNTalleffr(r,t)
   4129           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4130           * [ IF[t="prodtax",   sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   4131                                    PTAX(c,a,r) * [qca(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}}]
   4132             + IF[t="inctax",    sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS,
   4133                                    INCTAX(e,a,r) * [qes(e,a,r) - pop(r)]}}]
   4134             + IF[t="pfacttax",  sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS,
   4135                                    ETAX(e,a,r) * [qfe(e,a,r) - pop(r)]}}]
   4136             + IF[t="inputtax",  sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   4137                                   MFTAX(c,a,r) * [qfm(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}}
   4138                                 + sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   4139                                   DFTAX(c,a,r) * [qfd(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}}]
   4140             + IF[t="contax",    sum{c,COMM, MPTAX(c,r) * [qpm(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   4141                                 + sum{c,COMM, DPTAX(c,r) * [qpd(c,r) - pop(r)]}]
   4142             + IF[t="govtax",    sum{c,COMM, MGTAX(c,r) * [qgm(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   4143                                 + sum{c,COMM, DGTAX(c,r) * [qgd(c,r) - pop(r)]}]
   4144             + IF[t="invtax",    sum{c,COMM, MITAX(c,r) * [qim(c,r) - pop(r)]}
   4145                                 + sum{c,COMM, DITAX(c,r) * [qid(c,r) - pop(r)]}]
   4146             + IF[t="xtax",      sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG,
   4147                                     XTAXD(c,r,s) * [qxs(c,r,s) - pop(r)]}}]
   4148             + IF[t="mtax",      sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG,
   4149                                     MTAX(c,s,r) * [qxs(c,s,r) - pop(r)]}}]];
   4150    
   4151   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4152       CNTalleffcr(c,r)
   4153       # total contribution to regional EV of allocative effects #;
   4154   Equation E_CNTalleffcr
   4155   # total contribution to regional EV of allocative effects #
   4156   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4157       CNTalleffcr(c,r)
   4158           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]*
   4159           [ sum{a,ACTS, MFTAX(c,a,r) * [qfm(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}
   4160           + sum{a,ACTS, DFTAX(c,a,r) * [qfd(c,a,r) - pop(r)]}
   4161           + MPTAX(c,r) * [qpm(c,r) - pop(r)]
   4162           + DPTAX(c,r) * [qpd(c,r) - pop(r)]
   4163           + MGTAX(c,r) * [qgm(c,r) - pop(r)]
   4164           + DGTAX(c,r) * [qgd(c,r) - pop(r)]
   4165           + MITAX(c,r) * [qim(c,r) - pop(r)]
   4166           + DITAX(c,r) * [qid(c,r) - pop(r)]
   4167           + sum{s,REG, XTAXD(c,r,s) * [qxs(c,r,s) - pop(r)]}
   4168           + sum{s,REG, MTAX(c,s,r) * [qxs(c,s,r) - pop(r)]} ] ;
   4169    
   4170   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4171       CNTtotr(r)
   4172       # contribution to regional EV of changes in its terms of trade #;
   4173   Equation E_CNTtotr
   4174   # contribution to regional EV of changes in its terms of trade #
   4175   (all,r,REG)
   4176       CNTtotr(r)
   4177           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4178           * [sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VFOB(c,r,s) * [pfob(c,r,s) - pxwwld]}}
   4179               + sum{m,MARG, VST(m,r) * [pds(m,r) - pxwwld]}
   4180               - sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG, VFOB(c,s,r) * [pfob(c,s,r) - pxwwld]}}
   4181               - sum{m,MARG, VTMD(m,r) * [pt(m) - pxwwld]}];
   4182    
   4183   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4184       CNTpinv(r) # contribution to regional EV of changes in investment price #;
   4185   Equation E_CNTpinv
   4186   # contribution to regional EV of changes in investment price index #
   4187   (all,r,REG)
   4188       CNTpinv(r)
   4189           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4190           * [NETINV(r) * [pinv(r) - pxwwld] - SAVE(r) * [psave(r) - pxwwld]];
   4191    
   4192   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4193       CNTendwr(r) # contribution to regional EV of changes in all ENDW #;
   4194   Equation E_CNTendwr
   4195   # contribution to regional EV of changes in all ENDW #
   4196   (all,r,REG)
   4197       CNTendwr(r)
   4198           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4199           * [sum{e,ENDW, sum{a,ACTS, EVOS(e,a,r) * [qes(e,a,r) - pop(r)]}}
   4200               - VDEP(r) * [kb(r) - pop(r)]];
   4201    
   4202   Variable (linear,change) (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   4203       CNTendw(e,r) # contribution to regional EV of changes in ENDW e in r #;
   4204   Equation E_CNTendw
   4205   # contribution to regional EV of changes in ENDW e in r #
   4206   (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   4207       CNTendw(e,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] *
   4208                      sum{a,ACTS, [EVOS(e,a,r) * [qes(e,a,r) - pop(r)]]};
   4209    
   4210   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)(all,t,TECHTYPE)
   4211       CNTtechr(t,r) # contribution to regional EV of all technical change #;
   4212   Equation E_CNTtechr
   4213   # contribution to regional EV of all technical change #
   4214   (all,t,TECHTYPE)(all,r,REG)
   4215       CNTtechr(t,r)
   4216           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4217           * [ IF[t="output",  sum{a,ACTS, VOS(a,r) * ao(a,r)}]
   4218             + IF[t="ininput", sum{a,ACTS, sum{c,COMM,
   4219                                   [VMFP(c,a,r) + VDFP(c,a,r)] * afa(c,a,r)}}
   4220                               + sum{c,COMM, sum{a,ACTS,
   4221                                    VFP(c,a,r) * aint(a,r)}}]
   4222             + IF[t="primfac", sum{a,ACTS,
   4223                               sum{e,ENDW, VFP(e,a,r) * afe(e,a,r)}}]
   4224             + IF[t="v_added", sum{a,ACTS, VVA(a,r) * ava(a,r)}]
   4225             + IF[t="transp",  sum{m,MARG, sum{c,COMM, sum{s,REG,
   4226                               VTMFSD(m,c,s,r) * atmfsd(m,c,s,r)}}}]
   4227             + IF[t="import",  sum{c,COMM,
   4228                               sum{s,REG, VMSB(c,s,r) * ams(c,s,r)}}]];
   4229    
   4230   Variable (linear,change) (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4231       CNTtech_ao(a,r)
   4232       # cont. to regional EV of output augmenting tech change in a #;
   4233   Equation E_CNTtech_ao
   4234   # cont. to regional EV of output augmenting tech change in a #
   4235   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4236       CNTtech_ao(a,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VOS(a,r) * ao(a,r);
   4237    
   4238   Variable (linear,change) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4239       CNTtech_afe(e,a,r)
   4240       # cont. to EV of primary factor e augmenting tech change in a #;
   4241   Equation E_CNTtech_afe
   4242   # cont. to EV of primary factor e augmenting tech change in a #
   4243   (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4244       CNTtech_afe(e,a,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VFP(e,a,r) * afe(e,a,r);
   4245    
   4246   Variable (linear,change) (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4247       CNTtech_ava(a,r)
   4248       # cont. to EV of value added augmenting tech change in act. a #;
   4249   Equation E_CNTtech_ava
   4250   # cont. to EV of value added augmenting tech change in act. a #
   4251   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4252       CNTtech_ava(a,r) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VVA(a,r) * ava(a,r);
   4253    
   4254   Variable (linear,change) (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4255       CNTtech_aint(a,r)
   4256       # cont. to EV of composite c input augmenting tech change in act. a #;
   4257   Equation E_CNTtech_aint
   4258   # cont. to EV of composite c input augmenting tech change in act. a #
   4259   (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4260       CNTtech_aint(a,r)
   4261           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)]
   4262           * sum{c,COMM, [VMFP(c,a,r) + VDFP(c,a,r)] * aint(a,r)};
   4263    
   4264   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4265       CNTtech_af(c,a,r)
   4266       # cont. to EV of composite c input augmenting tech change in act. a #;
   4267   Equation E_CNTtech_af
   4268   # cont. to EV of composite c input augmenting tech change in act. a #
   4269   (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4270       CNTtech_af(c,a,r)
   4271           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * [VMFP(c,a,r) + VDFP(c,a,r)] * afa(c,a,r);
   4272    
   4273   Variable (linear,change)(all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4274       CNTtech_atmfsd(m,c,r,s)
   4275       # cont. to EV of tech change in transportation efficiency #;
   4276   Equation E_CNTtech_atmfsd
   4277   # cont. to EV of tech change in transportation efficiency #
   4278   (all,m,MARG)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4279       CNTtech_atmfsd(m,c,r,s)
   4280           = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(s)] * VTMFSD(m,c,r,s) * atmfsd(m,c,r,s);
   4281    
   4282   Variable (linear,change) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4283       CNTtech_ams(c,r,s)
   4284       # cont. to EV of bilateral import augmenting tech change for COMM c #;
   4285   Equation E_CNTtech_ams
   4286   # cont. to EV of bilateral import augmenting tech change for COMM c #
   4287   (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4288       CNTtech_ams(c,r,s) = [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VMSB(c,r,s) * ams(c,r,s);
   4289    
   4290   Variable (linear,change) (all,r,REG)
   4291       CNTkb(r)
   4292       # cont. to EV of changes to beg. period capital stock and depreciation #;
   4293   Equation E_CNTkb
   4294   # cont. to EV of changes to beg. period capital stock and depreciation #
   4295   (all,r,REG)
   4296       CNTkb(r) = - [0.01 * EVSCALFACT(r)] * VDEP(r) * [kb(r) - pop(r)];
   4297    
   4298   !<
   4299       ===========================
   4300       END OF GTAP model equations
   4301       ===========================
   4302   >!
   4303    
   4304   !<
   4305       ================================================
   4306       Welfare summary and post-simulation calculations
   4307       ================================================
   4308   >!
   4309    
   4310   !<
   4311       --------------------------
   4312       C. Welfare summary modules
   4313       --------------------------
   4314       C-A:  EV decomposition: Summary
   4315       C-A1: Allocative efficiency effect: Commodity summary
   4316       C-A2: Allocative efficiency effect: Tax type summary
   4317       C-AX: Decomposition of allocative effect, by tax type and commodity
   4318       C-B1: Endowment effect: Gross of depreciation
   4319       C-B2: Endowment effect: Depreciation
   4320       C-C1: Technical change effect
   4321       C-D1: Population effect
   4322       C-E1: Terms of trade (ToT) effect
   4323       C-F1: I-S Effect: Explanatory factors
   4324   >!
   4325    
   4326   !<
   4327       Preliminaries: Assign initial values
   4328       ------------------------------------
   4329   >!
   4330    
   4331   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0;
   4332   Zerodivide (zero_by_zero) default 0;
   4333    
   4334   Coefficient (parameter) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4335       BEVFP(e,a,r) # producer expenditure on c by act. a #;
   4336   Formula (initial) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4337       BEVFP(e,a,r) = EVFP(e,a,r);
   4338    
   4339   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4340       BVMFP(c,a,r) # purchases of imported c r for use in a in region r #;
   4341   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4342       BVMFP(c,a,r) = VMFP(c,a,r);
   4343    
   4344   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4345       BVDFP(c,a,r) # purchases of domestic c r for use in a in region r #;
   4346   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4347       BVDFP(c,a,r) = VDFP(c,a,r);
   4348    
   4349   Coefficient (parameter) (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4350       BVOS(a,r) # value of commodity c output in region r #;
   4351   Formula (initial)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4352       BVOS(a,r)
   4353           = sum{e,ENDW, BEVFP(e,a,r)}
   4354           + sum{c,COMM, BVMFP(c,a,r) + BVDFP(c,a,r)};
   4355    
   4356   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4357       BVXSB(c,r,s)
   4358       # exports of c from r to s at basic prices (tradeables only) #;
   4359   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4360       BVXSB(c,r,s) = VXSB(c,r,s);
   4361    
   4362   Coefficient (parameter)(all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4363       BVDPB(c,r) # private household expenditure on domestic c in r #;
   4364   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4365       BVDPB(c,r) = VDPB(c,r);
   4366    
   4367   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4368       BVDGB(c,r) # government household expenditure on domestic c in r #;
   4369   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4370       BVDGB(c,r) = VDGB(c,r);
   4371    
   4372   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4373       BVDFB(c,a,r) # purchases of domestic c for use in a in region r #;
   4374   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4375       BVDFB(c,a,r) = VDFB(c,a,r) ;
   4376    
   4377   Coefficient (parameter) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4378       BEVFB(e,a,r) # producer expenditure on c by a in r at basic prices #;
   4379   Formula (initial)  (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4380       BEVFB(e,a,r) = EVFB(e,a,r);
   4381    
   4382   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4383       BVDB(c,r) # domestic sales of c in r at basic prices (tradeables only) #;
   4384   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4385       BVDB(c,r) =  VDB(c,r);
   4386    
   4387   Coefficient (parameter) (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   4388       BVST(m,r)
   4389       # exports of m from r for int'l transp. at basic prices (tradeables only) #;
   4390   Formula (initial) (all,m,MARG)(all,r,REG)
   4391       BVST(m,r) =  VST(m,r);
   4392    
   4393   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4394       BVCB(c,r) # value of commodity c output in region r at basic prices #;
   4395   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4396       BVCB(c,r) = VCB(c,r);
   4397   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4398       BVCB(c,r) = BVDB(c,r) + sum{s,REG, BVXSB(c,r,s)}
   4399                 + IF[c in MARG, BVST(c,r)];
   4400    
   4401   Coefficient (parameter) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4402       BVEB(e,a,r) # value of endowment e in region r at basic prices #;
   4403   Formula (initial) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4404       BVEB(e,a,r) = EVFB(e,a,r);
   4405    
   4406   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4407       BMAKEB(c,a,r) # value of total output of firm a at initial basic prices #;
   4408   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4409       BMAKEB(c,a,r) = MAKEB(c,a,r);
   4410    
   4411   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4412       BOUTAX(c,a,r) # power of activity output tax, base #;
   4413   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4414       BOUTAX(c,a,r) = [MAKEB(c,a,r) - MAKES(c,a,r)] / MAKES(c,a,r) * 100;
   4415    
   4416   Coefficient (parameter) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4417       BEVOS(e,a,r) # initial endowment supply #;
   4418   Formula (initial) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4419       BEVOS(e,a,r) = EVOS(e,a,r);
   4420    
   4421   Coefficient (parameter)(all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4422       BINCTAX(e,a,r) # initial income tax #;
   4423   Formula (initial) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4424       BINCTAX(e,a,r) = [[BVEB(e,a,r) - BEVOS(e,a,r)] / BEVOS(e,a,r)] * 100;
   4425    
   4426   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4427       BVMFB(c,a,r) # purchases of imports c for use in act. a in region r #;
   4428   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4429       BVMFB(c,a,r) = VMFB(c,a,r);
   4430    
   4431   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4432       BVMPB(c,r) # private household expenditure on c in r #;
   4433   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4434       BVMPB(c,r) = VMPB(c,r);
   4435    
   4436   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4437       BVMPP(c,r) # private household expenditure on imported c #;
   4438   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4439       BVMPP(c,r) = VMPP(c,r);
   4440    
   4441   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4442       BVDPP(c,r) # private household expenditure on domestic c in r #;
   4443   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4444       BVDPP(c,r) = VDPP(c,r);
   4445    
   4446   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4447       BVMGB(c,r) # gov't household expenditure on c in r #;
   4448   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4449       BVMGB(c,r) = VMGB(c,r);
   4450    
   4451   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4452       BVMGP(c,r) # government household expenditure on imported c #;
   4453   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4454       BVMGP(c,r) = VMGP(c,r);
   4455    
   4456   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4457       BVDGP(c,r) # government household expenditure on domestic c in r #;
   4458   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4459       BVDGP(c,r) = VDGP(c,r);
   4460    
   4461   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4462       BVMIB(c,r) # investment expenditure on c in r #;
   4463   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4464       BVMIB(c,r) = VMIB(c,r);
   4465    
   4466   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4467       BVMIP(c,r) # investment expenditure on imported c #;
   4468   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4469       BVMIP(c,r) = VMIP(c,r);
   4470    
   4471   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4472       BVDIP(c,r) # investment expenditure on domestic c in r #;
   4473   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4474       BVDIP(c,r) = VDIP(c,r);
   4475    
   4476   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4477       BVDIB(c,r) # investment expenditure on domestic c in r #;
   4478   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   4479       BVDIB(c,r) = VDIB(c,r);
   4480    
   4481   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4482       BVMSB(c,s,d) # imports of c from r to s at domestic basic prices #;
   4483   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4484       BVMSB(c,s,d) = VMSB(c,s,d);
   4485    
   4486   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4487       BVCIF(c,s,d) # imports of c from r to s valued cif (tradeables only) #;
   4488   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4489       BVCIF(c,s,d) = VCIF(c,s,d);
   4490    
   4491   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4492       BMTAX(c,s,d) # power of import tax, base #;
   4493   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4494       BMTAX(c,s,d) = [BVMSB(c,s,d) - BVCIF(c,s,d)] / BVCIF(c,s,d) * 100;
   4495    
   4496   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4497       BVFOB(c,s,d) # exports of c from r to s valued fob (tradeables only) #;
   4498   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4499       BVFOB(c,s,d) = VFOB(c,s,d);
   4500    
   4501   Coefficient (parameter) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4502       BXTAX(c,s,d) # power of exports tax, base #;
   4503   Formula (initial) (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4504       BXTAX(c,s,d) = [BVFOB(c,s,d) - BVXSB(c,s,d)] / BVXSB(c,s,d) * 100;
   4505    
   4506   Coefficient (parameter) (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4507       BETAX(e,a,r) # power of exports tax, base #;
   4508   Formula (initial)(all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4509       BETAX(e,a,r) = [BEVFP(e,a,r) - BEVFB(e,a,r)] / BEVFB(e,a,r) * 100;
   4510    
   4511   Coefficient (parameter) (all,r,REG)
   4512       BSAVE(r) # expenditure on NET saving in region r at producer prices #;
   4513   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   4514       BSAVE(r) = SAVE(r);
   4515    
   4516   Coefficient (parameter) (all,r,REG)
   4517       ISBAL(r) # I-S balance, NETINV(r) - SAVE(r) #;
   4518   Formula (initial) (all,r,REG)
   4519       ISBAL(r) = NETINV(r) - BSAVE(r);
   4520   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) off;
   4521    
   4522   !<
   4523       Begin post-sim calculations
   4524       ...........................
   4525   >!
   4526    
   4527   postsim (begin);
   4528   Zerodivide (nonzero_by_zero) default 0.5;
   4529    
   4530   File (new) WELVIEW # output file containing welfare decomposition summary #;
   4531    
   4532   !<
   4533       SET definitions for Welfare summary file. Supplementary sets for "toggles"
   4534       in VIEWHAR.
   4535   >!
   4536   Set
   4537       UNITA # dummy (unit) set for activities # (a);
   4538   Set
   4539       UNITC # dummy (unit) set for commodities # (c);
   4540   Set
   4541       UACT = UNITA x ACTS;
   4542   Set
   4543       UCOM = UNITC x COMM;
   4544   Set
   4545       ALLOCEFF = ENDW + UACT + UCOM;
   4546   Set
   4547       ENDWACTS = ENDW + ACTS;
   4548   Set
   4549       TAXSUM(pfacttax,prodtax,comtax);
   4550   Set
   4551       TYPE(xtax,mtax);
   4552   Subset
   4553       TYPE is subset of CTAX;
   4554   Set
   4555       PRICES(pworld,pexport,pimport);
   4556   Set
   4557       ACTIVITY(firm, private, investment, govt);
   4558   Set
   4559       COL(welcnt, dvol, taxrateb, taxrateu);
   4560   Set
   4561       DIREC(import,export);
   4562   Set
   4563       FORM(percent,value);
   4564   Set
   4565       COLM(ISbal,p_cgds,p_save);
   4566    
   4567   !<
   4568       C-A: EV decomposition summary
   4569       -----------------------------
   4570   >!
   4571    
   4572   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,c,COLUMN)
   4573       WELFARE(r,c) # aggregate report of welfare change #;
   4574   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4575       WELFARE(r,"alloc_A1")= sum{t, CTAX, CNTalleffr(r,t)};
   4576   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4577       WELFARE(r,"ENDWB1") = CNTendwr(r);
   4578   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4579       WELFARE(r,"tech_C1") = sum{t,TECHTYPE, CNTtechr(t,r)};
   4580   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4581       WELFARE(r,"pop_D1")  = CNTpop(r);
   4582   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4583       WELFARE(r,"tot_E1")  = CNTtotr(r);
   4584   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4585       WELFARE(r,"IS_F1")   = CNTpinv(r);
   4586   Formula (all,r,REG)
   4587       WELFARE(r,"PREF_G1") = CNTdpar(r);
   4588    
   4589   Write
   4590       WELFARE to file WELVIEW header "A"
   4591       longname "EV Decomposition: Summary";
   4592    
   4593   !<
   4594       C-A1: Allocative efficiency effect: Activity, comodity and endowment Summary
   4595       ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   4596   >!
   4597    
   4598   Mapping UCOM2COMM from UCOM to COMM;
   4599   Formula (all,c,UCOM)
   4600       UCOM2COMM(c) = $POS(c);
   4601   Mapping UACT2ACTS from UACT to ACTS;
   4602   Formula (all,a,UACT)
   4603       UACT2ACTS(a) = $POS(a);
   4604   Coefficient (all,a,ALLOCEFF)(all,r,REG)
   4605       CNTalleff(a,r) # allocative efficiency #;
   4606   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,e,ENDW)
   4607       CNTalleff(e,r) = CNTqfeer(e,r) + CNTqe(e,r);
   4608   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,c,UCOM)
   4609       CNTalleff(c,r) = CNTalleffcr(UCOM2COMM(c),r);
   4610   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,a,UACT)
   4611       CNTalleff(a,r) = sum{c,COMM, CNTqca(c,UACT2ACTS(a),r)};
   4612    
   4613   Write
   4614       CNTalleff to file WELVIEW header "A1"
   4615       longname "Allocative Efficiency Effect: Summary";
   4616    
   4617   !<
   4618       C-A2: Allocative efficiency effect: Tax type summary
   4619       ----------------------------------------------------
   4620   >!
   4621   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,t,CTAX)
   4622       CNTalleffkr(r,t) # allocative efficiency effect #;
   4623   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,t,CTAX)
   4624       CNTalleffkr(r,t) = CNTalleffr(r,t);
   4625   Write
   4626       CNTalleffkr to file WELVIEW header "A2"
   4627       longname "Allocative Efficiency Effect: Tax Type Summary";
   4628    
   4629   !<
   4630       C-AX: Decomposition of allocative effect: Tax type
   4631       --------------------------------------------------
   4632    
   4633       C-A21:  Output tax effect
   4634       C-A22:  Domestic tax effect
   4635       C-A23:  Trade tax effect
   4636       C-A24:  Endowment tax effect
   4637       C-A25:  Factor income tax effect
   4638   >!
   4639    
   4640   !<
   4641       C-A21:  Output tax effect
   4642       .........................
   4643   >!
   4644    
   4645   Coefficient (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4646       OTAX(a,r) # output tax effect #;
   4647   Formula (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4648       OTAX(a,r) = CNTqo(a,r);
   4649    
   4650   Write
   4651       OTAX to file WELVIEW header "A21"
   4652       longname "Output Tax Effect";
   4653    
   4654   !<
   4655       C-A211: Output tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4656       ..............................................
   4657   >!
   4658    
   4659   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4660       UOUTAX(c,a,r) # power of activity output tax, updated #;
   4661   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4662       UOUTAX(c,a,r) = [MAKEB(c,a,r) - MAKES(c,a,r)] / MAKES(c,a,r) * 100;
   4663    
   4664   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4665       OUTPUT(c,a,r,co) # output tax, explanatory factors #;
   4666   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4667       OUTPUT(c,a,r,co)
   4668           = IF[co="welcnt", CNTqca(c,a,r)]
   4669           + IF[co="dvol",   BMAKEB(c,a,r) * qo(a,r) / 100]
   4670           + IF[co="taxrateb", BOUTAX(c,a,r)]
   4671           + IF[co="taxrateu", UOUTAX(c,a,r)];
   4672   Write
   4673       OUTPUT to file WELVIEW header "A211"
   4674       longname "Output Tax Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   4675    
   4676   !<
   4677       C-A22:  Domestic tax effect
   4678       ---------------------------
   4679    
   4680       C-A22:  Domestic tax effect: Summary
   4681       C-A221: Intermed. input tax effect
   4682       C-A222: Investment interm. input tax effect
   4683       C-A22F: Intermed. input tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4684       C-A22P: Private cons. tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4685       C-A22G: Government cons. tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4686       C-A22I: Investment demand Tax Effect: Explanatory factors
   4687   >!
   4688    
   4689   !<
   4690       C-A22: Domestic tax effect: Summary
   4691       ...................................
   4692   >!
   4693    
   4694   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,ac,ACTIVITY)(all,r,REG)(all,t,DIR)
   4695       ATAX(c,ac,r,t) # tax effect: summary #;
   4696   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,ac,ACTIVITY)(all,r,REG)
   4697       ATAX(c,ac,r,"domestic")
   4698           = IF[ac="firm",       sum{a,ACTS, CNTqfd(c,a,r)}]
   4699           + IF[ac="private",    CNTqpd(c,r)]
   4700           + IF[ac="govt",       CNTqgd(c,r)]
   4701           + IF[ac="investment", CNTqid(c,r)];
   4702   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,ac,ACTIVITY)(all,r,REG)
   4703       ATAX(c,ac,r,"imported")
   4704           = IF[ac="firm",       sum{a,ACTS, CNTqfm(c,a,r)}]
   4705           + IF[ac="private",    CNTqpm(c,r)]
   4706           + IF[ac="govt",       CNTqgm(c,r)]
   4707           + IF[ac="investment", CNTqim(c,r)];
   4708    
   4709   Write
   4710       ATAX to file WELVIEW header "A22"
   4711       longname "Domestic Tax Effect: Summary";
   4712    
   4713   !<
   4714       C-A221: Intermediate input tax effect
   4715       .....................................
   4716   >!
   4717    
   4718   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4719       STAX(c,a,r,d) # intermediate input tax effect #;
   4720   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4721       STAX(c,a,r,d)
   4722           = IF[d="domestic", CNTqfd(c,a,r)]
   4723           + IF[d="imported", CNTqfm(c,a,r)];
   4724    
   4725   Write
   4726       STAX to file WELVIEW header "A221"
   4727       longname "Intermed. Input Tax Effect";
   4728    
   4729   !<
   4730       C-A222: Investment intermediate input tax effect
   4731       ................................................
   4732   >!
   4733    
   4734   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4735       ITAX(c,r,d) # investment intermediate input tax effect #;
   4736   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4737       ITAX(c,r,d)
   4738           = IF[d="domestic", CNTqid(c,r)]
   4739           + IF[d="imported", CNTqim(c,r)];
   4740    
   4741   Write
   4742       ITAX to file WELVIEW header "A222"
   4743       longname "Investment Intermed. Input Tax Effect";
   4744    
   4745   !<
   4746       C-A22F: Intermediate input tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4747       ..........................................................
   4748   >!
   4749    
   4750   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)(all,co,COL)
   4751       FIRM(c,a,r,d,co) # explanatory factors: firm interm. input tax effect #;
   4752   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4753       FIRM(c,a,r,"domestic",co)
   4754           = IF[co="dvol",     [BVDFB(c,a,r) * qfd(c,a,r)] / 100]
   4755           + IF[co="taxrateb", 100 * [BVDFP(c,a,r) - BVDFB(c,a,r)] / BVDFB(c,a,r)]
   4756           + IF[co="taxrateu", 100 * [VDFP(c,a,r) - VDFB(c,a,r)] / VDFB(c,a,r)];
   4757   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4758       FIRM(c,a,r,"imported",co)
   4759           = IF[co="dvol",     [BVMFB(c,a,r) * qfm(c,a,r)] / 100]
   4760           + IF[co="taxrateb", 100 * [BVMFP(c,a,r) - BVMFB(c,a,r)] / BVMFB(c,a,r)]
   4761           + IF[co="taxrateu", 100 * [VMFP(c,a,r) - VMFB(c,a,r)] / VMFB(c,a,r)];
   4762   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4763       FIRM(c,a,r,d,"welcnt") = STAX(c,a,r,d);
   4764    
   4765   Write
   4766       FIRM to file WELVIEW header "A22F"
   4767       longname "Intermed. Input Tax Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   4768    
   4769   !<
   4770       C-A22P: Private consumption tax Effect: Explanatory Factors
   4771       ...........................................................
   4772   >!
   4773    
   4774   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)(all,co,COL)
   4775       PRIVATE(c,r,d,co) # explanatory factors: priv hh consumption tax effect #;
   4776   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4777       PRIVATE(c,r,"domestic",co)
   4778           = IF[co="dvol",     [BVDPB(c,r) * qpd(c,r)] / 100]
   4779           + IF[co="taxrateb", 100 * [BVDPP(c,r) - BVDPB(c,r)] / BVDPB(c,r)]
   4780           + IF[co="taxrateu", 100 * [VDPP(c,r) - VDPB(c,r)] / VDPB(c,r)];
   4781   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4782       PRIVATE(c,r,"imported",co)
   4783           = IF[co="dvol",     [BVMPB(c,r) * qpm(c,r)] / 100]
   4784           + IF[co="taxrateb", 100 * [BVMPP(c,r) - BVMPB(c,r)] / BVMPB(c,r)]
   4785           + IF[co="taxrateu", 100 * [VMPP(c,r) - VMPB(c,r)] / VMPB(c,r)];
   4786   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4787       PRIVATE(c,r,d,"welcnt") = ATAX(c,"private",r,d);
   4788    
   4789   Write
   4790       PRIVATE to file WELVIEW header "A22P"
   4791       longname "Private Cons. Tax Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   4792    
   4793   !<
   4794       C-A22G: Government consumption tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4795       ..............................................................
   4796   >!
   4797    
   4798   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)(all,co,COL)
   4799       GOVT(c,r,d,co) # explanatory factors: gov't hh consumption tax effect #;
   4800   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4801       GOVT(c,r,"domestic",co)
   4802           = IF[co="dvol",     [BVDGB(c,r) * qgd(c,r)] / 100]
   4803           + IF[co="taxrateb", 100 * [BVDGP(c,r) - BVDGB(c,r)] / BVDGB(c,r)]
   4804           + IF[co="taxrateu", 100 * [VDGP(c,r) - VDGB(c,r)] / VDGB(c,r)];
   4805   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4806       GOVT(c,r,"imported",co)
   4807           = IF[co="dvol",     [BVMGB(c,r) * qgm(c,r)] / 100]
   4808           + IF[co="taxrateb", 100 * [BVMGP(c,r) - BVMGB(c,r)] / BVMGB(c,r)]
   4809           + IF[co="taxrateu", 100 * [VMGP(c,r) - VMGB(c,r)] / VMGB(c,r)];
   4810   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4811       GOVT(c,r,d,"welcnt") = ATAX(c,"govt",r,d);
   4812    
   4813   Write
   4814       GOVT to file WELVIEW header "A22G"
   4815       longname "Government Cons. Tax Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   4816    
   4817   !<
   4818       C-A22I: Investment tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4819       ..................................................
   4820   >!
   4821    
   4822   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)(all,co,COL)
   4823       INVESTMENT(c,r,d,co) # explanatory factors: investment tax effect #;
   4824   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4825       INVESTMENT(c,r,"domestic",co)
   4826           = IF[co="dvol",     [BVDIB(c,r) * qid(c,r)] / 100]
   4827           + IF[co="taxrateb", 100 * [BVDIP(c,r) - BVDIB(c,r)] / BVDIB(c,r)]
   4828           + IF[co="taxrateu", 100 * [VDIP(c,r) - VDIB(c,r)] / VDIB(c,r)];
   4829   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4830       INVESTMENT(c,r,"imported",co)
   4831           = IF[co="dvol",     [BVMIB(c,r) * qim(c,r)] / 100]
   4832           + IF[co="taxrateb", 100 * [BVMIP(c,r) - BVMIB(c,r)] / BVMIB(c,r)]
   4833           + IF[co="taxrateu", 100 * [VMIP(c,r) - VMIB(c,r)] / VMIB(c,r)];
   4834   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,d,DIR)
   4835       INVESTMENT(c,r,d,"welcnt") = ATAX(c,"investment",r,d);
   4836    
   4837   Write
   4838       INVESTMENT to file WELVIEW header "A22I"
   4839       longname "Investment Tax Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   4840    
   4841   !<
   4842       C-A23: Trade tax effect
   4843       ------------------------
   4844    
   4845       C-A23:  Trade tax effect
   4846       C-A231: Trade tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4847   >!
   4848    
   4849   !<
   4850       C-A23: Trade tax effect
   4851       ........................
   4852   >!
   4853    
   4854   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)(all,k,TYPE)
   4855       TTAX(c,r,s,k) # trade tax effect #;
   4856   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)
   4857       TTAX(c,r,s,"xtax") = CNTqxs(c,r,s);
   4858   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4859       TTAX(c,s,d,"mtax") = CNTqms(c,s,d);
   4860    
   4861   Write
   4862       TTAX to file WELVIEW header "A23"
   4863       longname "Trade Tax Effect";
   4864    
   4865   !<
   4866       C-A231: Trade tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4867       .............................................
   4868   >!
   4869    
   4870   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4871       UMTAX(c,s,d) # power of import tax, updated # ;
   4872   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4873       UMTAX(c,s,d) = [VMSB(c,s,d) - VCIF(c,s,d)] / VCIF(c,s,d) * 100;
   4874    
   4875   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4876       UXTAX(c,s,d) # power of export tax, updated #;
   4877   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   4878       UXTAX(c,s,d) = [VFOB(c,s,d) - VXSB(c,s,d)] / VXSB(c,s,d) * 100;
   4879    
   4880   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)(all,co,COL)(all,d,DIREC)
   4881       TRADE(c,r,s,co,d) # trade tax effect: explanatory factors # ;
   4882   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4883       TRADE(c,r,s,co,"export")
   4884           = IF[co="welcnt",   TTAX(c,r,s,"xtax")]
   4885           + IF[co="dvol",     BVXSB(c,r,s) * qxs(c,r,s) / 100]
   4886           + IF[co="taxrateb", BXTAX(c,r,s)]
   4887           + IF[co="taxrateu", UXTAX(c,r,s)];
   4888   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,s,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4889       TRADE(c,r,s,co,"import")
   4890           = IF[co="welcnt",   TTAX(c,r,s,"mtax")]
   4891           + IF[co="dvol",     BVXSB(c,r,s) * qxs(c,r,s) / 100]
   4892           + IF[co="taxrateb", BMTAX(c,r,s)]
   4893           + IF[co="taxrateu", UMTAX(c,r,s)];
   4894    
   4895   Write
   4896       TRADE to file WELVIEW header "A231"
   4897       longname "Trade Tax Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   4898    
   4899   !<
   4900       C-A24: Endowment tax effect
   4901       ---------------------------
   4902    
   4903       C-A24:  Endowment tax effect
   4904       C-A241: Endowment tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4905   >!
   4906    
   4907   !<
   4908       C-A24:   Endowment tax effect
   4909       .............................
   4910   >!
   4911    
   4912   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   4913       FACTAX(e,r) # Endowment tax effect #;
   4914   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   4915       FACTAX(e,r) = sum{a,ACTS, CNTqfe(e,a,r)};
   4916   Write
   4917       FACTAX to file WELVIEW header "A24"
   4918       longname "Endowment Tax Effect";
   4919    
   4920   !<
   4921       C-A241: Endowment tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4922       .................................................
   4923   >!
   4924   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4925       UETAX(e,a,r) # power of factor tax, updated #;
   4926   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4927       UETAX(e,a,r) = [EVFP(e,a,r) - EVFB(e,a,r)] / EVFB(e,a,r) * 100;
   4928    
   4929   ! Note: PFACTOR in "classic" welfare decomp was changed to FACTORTAX because
   4930           the variable pfactor(r) has already been defined !
   4931   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4932       FACTORTAX(e,a,r,co) # Endowment tax effect #;
   4933   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4934       FACTORTAX(e,a,r,co)
   4935           = IF[co="welcnt",   CNTqfe(e,a,r)]
   4936           + IF[co="dvol",     BEVFB(e,a,r) * qfe(e,a,r) / 100]
   4937           + IF[co="taxrateb", BETAX(e,a,r)]
   4938           + IF[co="taxrateu", UETAX(e,a,r)];
   4939    
   4940   Write FACTORTAX to file WELVIEW header "A241"
   4941         longname "Endowment Tax Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   4942    
   4943   !<
   4944       C-A25: Income tax effect
   4945       ------------------------
   4946    
   4947       C-A25:  Income tax effect
   4948       C-A251: Income tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4949   >!
   4950    
   4951   !<
   4952       C-A25: Income tax effect
   4953       ........................
   4954   >!
   4955    
   4956   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   4957       YTAX(e,r) # factor income tax effect #;
   4958   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,r,REG)
   4959       YTAX(e,r) = sum{a,ACTS, CNTqea(e,a,r)};
   4960   Write
   4961       YTAX to file WELVIEW header "A25"
   4962       longname "Income Tax Effect";
   4963    
   4964   !<
   4965       C-A251: Income tax effect: Explanatory factors
   4966       ..............................................
   4967   >!
   4968   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4969       UINCTAX(e,a,r) # power of income tax, updated #;
   4970   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   4971       UINCTAX(e,a,r) = [[EVFB(e,a,r) - EVOS(e,a,r)] / EVOS(e,a,r)] * 100;
   4972   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4973       INCOMETAX(e,a,r,co) # income tax effect: Explanatory Factors #;
   4974   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)(all,co,COL)
   4975       INCOMETAX(e,a,r,co)
   4976           = IF[co="welcnt",   CNTqea(e,a,r)]
   4977           + IF[co="dvol",     BVEB(e,a,r) * qes(e,a,r) / 100]
   4978           + IF[co="taxrateb", BINCTAX(e,a,r)]
   4979           + IF[co="taxrateu", UINCTAX(e,a,r)];
   4980   Write
   4981       INCOMETAX to file WELVIEW header "A251"
   4982       longname "Income Tax Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   4983    
   4984   !<
   4985       C-B1: Endowment effect: Gross of depreciation
   4986       ---------------------------------------------
   4987   >!
   4988    
   4989   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,e,ENDW)
   4990       CNTendowment(r,e) # contribution to welfare by ENDW e in region r #;
   4991   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,e,ENDW)
   4992       CNTendowment(r,e) = CNTendw(e,r);
   4993   Write
   4994       CNTendowment to file WELVIEW header "B1"
   4995       longname "Endowment Effect, Gross of Depreciation";
   4996    
   4997   !<
   4998       C-B2: Endowment effect: depreciation
   4999       ------------------------------------
   5000   >!
   5001    
   5002   Write
   5003       CNTkb to file WELVIEW header "B2"
   5004       longname "Endowment Effect: Depreciation";
   5005    
   5006   !<
   5007       C-C1: Technical change effect
   5008       -----------------------------
   5009    
   5010       C-C1:  Technical change effect: Summary
   5011       C-C1X: Technical change effect: Further decomposition
   5012   >!
   5013    
   5014   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,t,TECHTYPE)
   5015       CNTtech(r,t) # contribution to welfare change by tech #;
   5016   Formula (all,r,REG)(all,t,TECHTYPE)
   5017       CNTtech(r,t) = CNTtechr(t,r);
   5018    
   5019   Write
   5020       CNTtech to file WELVIEW header "C1"
   5021       longname "Technical Change Effect: Summary";
   5022    
   5023   Write
   5024       CNTtech_ao to file WELVIEW header "C11"
   5025       longname "(ao) Output Augm. Tech. Change Effect";
   5026   Write
   5027       CNTtech_afe to file WELVIEW header "C12"
   5028       longname "(afe) Primary Factor Augm. Tech. Change Effect";
   5029   Write
   5030       CNTtech_ava to file WELVIEW header "C13"
   5031       longname "(ava) Value Added Augm. Tech. Change Effect";
   5032   Write
   5033       CNTtech_aint to file WELVIEW header "C14"
   5034       longname "(aint) Composite Intermed. Input Augm. Tech. Change Effect";
   5035   Write
   5036        CNTtech_af to file WELVIEW header "C15"
   5037       longname "(af) Intermed. Input Augm. Tech. Change Effect";
   5038   Write
   5039       CNTtech_atmfsd to file WELVIEW header "C16"
   5040       longname "(atmfsd) Internat. Margin Augm. Tech. Change Effect";
   5041   Write
   5042       CNTtech_ams to file WELVIEW header "C17"
   5043       longname "(ams) Bilateral Import Augm. Tech. Change Effect";
   5044    
   5045   !<
   5046       C-D1: Population effect
   5047       -----------------------
   5048    
   5049       No decomposition required here.
   5050   >!
   5051    
   5052   !<
   5053       C-E1: Terms of Trade (ToT) effect
   5054       ---------------------------------
   5055   >!
   5056    
   5057   ! Note: TOT(c,r,t,s) in Welfare Decomp was renamed to WTOT(c,r,t,s) because a
   5058           prior tot(r) variable has been declared in the model!
   5059   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)(all,t,PRICES)(all,s,FORM)
   5060       WTOT(c,r,t,s)
   5061       # terms trade effects decomposed by effects of different prices #;
   5062   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5063       WTOT(c,r,"pworld","percent") = c1_cr(c,r);
   5064   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5065       WTOT(c,r,"pexport","percent") = c2_cr(c,r);
   5066   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5067       WTOT(c,r,"pimport","percent") = -c3_cr(c,r);
   5068   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5069       WTOT(c,r,"pworld","value")
   5070           = CNTtotr(r) * c1_cr(c,r)
   5071           / sum{k,COMM, sum{t,PRICES, WTOT(k,r,t,"percent")}};
   5072   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5073       WTOT(c,r,"pexport","value")
   5074           = CNTtotr(r) * c2_cr(c,r)
   5075           / sum{t,PRICES, sum{k,COMM, WTOT(k,r,t,"percent")}};
   5076   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5077       WTOT(c,r,"pimport","value")
   5078           = -c3_cr(c,r) * CNTtotr(r)
   5079           / sum{t,PRICES, sum{k,COMM, WTOT(k,r,t,"percent")}};
   5080    
   5081   Write
   5082       WTOT to file WELVIEW header "E1"
   5083       longname "Terms of Trade Effect";
   5084    
   5085   !<
   5086       C-F1: I-S Effect: Explanatory factors
   5087       -------------------------------------
   5088   >!
   5089    
   5090   Coefficient (all,r,REG)(all,c,COLM)
   5091       CGDSCOMP(r,c) # components of cgds effect #;
   5092   Formula (all,r,REG)
   5093       CGDSCOMP(r,"ISbal") = ISBAL(r);
   5094   Formula (all,r,REG)
   5095       CGDSCOMP(r,"p_cgds") = pinv(r);
   5096   Formula (all,r,REG)
   5097       CGDSCOMP(r,"p_save") = psave(r);
   5098   Write
   5099       CGDSCOMP to file WELVIEW header "F1"
   5100       longname "I-S Effect: Explanatory Factors";
   5101    
   5102   !<
   5103       -----------------------------
   5104       END OF Welfare summary module
   5105       -----------------------------
   5106   >!
   5107    
   5108   !<
   5109       -------------------------------------------------
   5110       D. GTAPVol (post-simulation) summary calculations
   5111       -------------------------------------------------
   5112   >!
   5113    
   5114   !<
   5115       Compute the relevant volume changes
   5116       -----------------------------------
   5117   >!
   5118    
   5119   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   5120       DQXS(c,s,d)
   5121       # ch. in vol. of exports of c from region s to d at initial basic prices #;
   5122   Formula  (all,c,COMM)(all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   5123       DQXS(c,s,d) = [qxs(c,s,d) / 100] * BVXSB(c,s,d);
   5124    
   5125   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5126       DQDS(c,r)
   5127       # ch. in vol. of domestic sales of com. c in r at initial basic prices #;
   5128   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5129       DQDS(c,r) = [qds(c,r) / 100] * BVDB(c,r) ;
   5130    
   5131   Coefficient (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   5132       DQFE(e,a,r)
   5133       # ch. in vol. of endowment e by activity a in r at initial basic prices #;
   5134   Formula (all,e,ENDW)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   5135       DQFE(e,a,r) = [qfe(e,a,r) / 100] * BEVFB(e,a,r) ;
   5136    
   5137   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   5138       DQFM(c,a,r)
   5139       # ch. in vol. of imp. intermed. c by act. a in r at initial basic prices #;
   5140   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   5141       DQFM(c,a,r) = [qfm(c,a,r) / 100] * BVMFB(c,a,r) ;
   5142    
   5143   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   5144       DQFD(c,a,r)
   5145       # ch. in vol. of dom. intermed. c by act. a in r at initial basic prices #;
   5146   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   5147            DQFD(c,a,r) = [qfd(c,a,r) / 100] * BVDFB(c,a,r) ;
   5148    
   5149   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5150       DQPM(c,r)
   5151       # ch. in vol. of priv. hhld cons. for imp. c in r at initial basic prices #;
   5152   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5153       DQPM(c,r) = [qpm(c,r) / 100] * BVMPB(c,r) ;
   5154    
   5155   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5156       DQPD(c,r)
   5157       # ch. in vol. of priv. hhld cons. for dom. c in r at initial basic prices #;
   5158   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5159       DQPD(c,r) = [qpd(c,r) / 100] * BVDPB(c,r) ;
   5160    
   5161   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5162       DQGM(c,r)
   5163       # ch. in vol. of government cons. for imp. c in r at initial basic prices #;
   5164   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5165       DQGM(c,r) = [qgm(c,r) / 100] * BVMGB(c,r) ;
   5166    
   5167   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5168       DQGD(c,r)
   5169       # ch. in vol. of government cons. for dom. c in r at initial basic prices #;
   5170   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5171       DQGD(c,r) = [qgd(c,r) / 100] * BVDGB(c,r) ;
   5172    
   5173   Coefficient (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   5174       DQO(a,r)
   5175       # ch. in vol. of output by activity a in r at initial basic prices #;
   5176   Formula (all,a,ACTS)(all,r,REG)
   5177       DQO(a,r) = [qo(a,r) / 100] * BVOS(a,r) ;
   5178    
   5179   Coefficient (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5180       DQC(c,r)
   5181       # ch. in vol. of supply of com. c in r at initial basic prices #;
   5182   Formula (all,c,COMM)(all,r,REG)
   5183       DQC(c,r) = [qc(c,r) / 100] * BVCB(c,r) ;
   5184    
   5185   Coefficient (all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   5186       DTOT(s,d)
   5187       # ch. in vol. of total exports from region s to d at initial basic prices #;
   5188   Formula (all,s,REG)(all,d,REG)
   5189       DTOT(s,d) = sum{c,COMM, DQXS(c,s,d)};
   5190    
   5191   Zerodivide off;
   5192    
   5193   FILE
   5194    (New) GTAPVOL # HAR file of volume changes # ;
   5195   !< Write the output of this module to ViewHAR for easy viewing and summation >!
   5196    
   5197   Write
   5198       DQXS to file GTAPVOL header "DQXS";
   5199       DQDS to file GTAPVOL header "DQDS";
   5200       DQFE to file GTAPVOL header "DQFE";
   5201       DQFM to file GTAPVOL header "DQFM";
   5202       DQFD to file GTAPVOL header "DQFD";
   5203       DQPM to file GTAPVOL header "DQPM";
   5204       DQPD to file GTAPVOL header "DQPD";
   5205       DTOT to file GTAPVOL header "DTOT";
   5206       DQO  to file GTAPVOL header "DQO ";
   5207       DQC  to file GTAPVOL header "DQC ";
   5208       DQGD to file GTAPVOL header "DQGD";
   5209       DQGM to file GTAPVOL header "DQGM";
